  (215, 23, 212, 9, 'I don’t care if you think it’s too long, listen to the whole thing', '2025-06-26T00:20:36Z', -1),
  (216, 23, 213, 6, NULL, '2025-06-25T18:01:44Z', -1),
  (217, 23, 214, 1, 'Timeless story, timeless music. Zimmer is a GOAT.', '2025-06-25T20:01:49Z', 6),
  (218, 23, 32, 11, NULL, '2025-06-25T17:04:15Z', 4),
  (219, 23, 215, 8, NULL, '2025-06-25T21:04:40Z', 2),
  (220, 23, 216, 4, 'I do it for my daddy and I do it for Dale', '2025-06-26T00:15:14Z', 4),
  (221, 23, 217, 2, 'To the Operator, a psalm of Jim', '2025-06-25T19:10:06Z', 0),
  (222, 23, 218, 10, 'Long live the Queen', '2025-06-26T01:15:59Z', 2),
  (223, 23, 219, 3, 'Any Sufjan hate will be met with swift and exacting retribution.', '2025-06-25T17:14:35Z', 4),
  (224, 24, 220, 1, '😌', '2025-06-29T01:40:46Z', 6),
  (225, 24, 221, 5, 'Sammy, I thought you might appreciate knowing that this is the only round so far where I had to create an actual playlist to weigh my options. A whole discernment experience...and Caamp, in the end, prevailed', '2025-06-29T23:46:11Z', 3),
  (226, 24, 222, 6, 'Did he know there was a full version? We will find out. ', '2025-06-29T23:55:02Z', -1),
  (227, 24, 223, 4, 'Sunday Morning 102.3 baby ', '2025-06-30T00:03:03Z', 6),
  (228, 24, 224, 9, NULL, '2025-06-29T02:07:57Z', 1),
  (229, 24, 225, 11, NULL, '2025-06-29T22:31:39Z', 2),
  (230, 24, 226, 10, NULL, '2025-06-30T01:12:54Z', 0),
  (231, 24, 227, 2, NULL, '2025-06-29T23:59:27Z', 4),
  (232, 24, 228, 3, 'I’m hoping this constitutes a somewhat rare intersection on Sammy’s and my musical Venn diagram', '2025-06-29T13:14:52Z', 2),
  (233, 24, 229, 8, NULL, '2025-06-29T02:27:13Z', -3),
  (234, 25, 230, 2, 'Adam Schlesinger is the Andy Warhol of pop music. He is a master at crafting songs that manage to be ironic and earnest at the same time, simple and straightforward yet beautiful in their straightforwardness. It’s no wonder that when Tom Hanks wanted to make a movie about the very concept of the one hit wonder, he got Adam Schlesinger to write the fictional “one hit” in question. (That Thing You Do!, for those keeping score at home.) Stacy’s Mom is unassailable for its lyrical creativity and pop ingenuity, but look even a little bit below the surface and you’ll find a career filled with clever, insightful, delightfully sugary pop goodness. Trust me, this Fountain is deep. ', '2025-07-03T12:15:34Z', 2),
  (235, 25, 231, 11, NULL, '2025-07-03T06:40:15Z', 2),
  (236, 25, 232, 1, 'Unknown bop from some undeniable one hit wonders.', '2025-07-03T03:55:30Z', 6),
  (237, 25, 233, 8, 'Outer space horizons, symphony of synth, West German Woman cries into the long dark night.', '2025-07-03T00:47:21Z', 1),
  (238, 25, 234, 3, NULL, '2025-07-02T14:02:27Z', 4),
  (239, 25, 235, 9, NULL, '2025-07-03T01:03:24Z', 4),
  (240, 25, 236, 6, NULL, '2025-07-02T13:37:10Z', -2),
  (241, 25, 237, 4, 'Carly Rae should be our pop music muse, a role cruelly denied her. ', '2025-07-02T14:34:16Z', -2),
  (242, 25, 238, 5, NULL, '2025-07-03T03:26:10Z', 1),
  (243, 26, 239, 10, 'One of the best live performances', '2025-07-06T23:46:47Z', 0),
  (244, 26, 240, 8, 'I’m not crying there’s something my eye', '2025-07-06T18:36:16Z', 4),
  (245, 26, 241, 4, 'My runner up for Superior Cover. ', '2025-07-07T14:06:38Z', 1),
  (246, 26, 242, 1, NULL, '2025-07-07T02:16:35Z', 3),
  (247, 26, 243, 3, 'I’m prepared to be buried in downvotes, but this is one of the most formative recordings of my musical journey. This very performance opened my eyes to the value of screaming, as it’s used very intentionally to convey the emotion of the song. Haunting performance by one of the all time greats. ', '2025-07-06T14:53:08Z', -1),
  (248, 26, 244, 5, 'An important moment in musical history.', '2025-07-07T01:00:48Z', 0),
  (249, 26, 245, 11, NULL, '2025-07-06T14:24:16Z', 5),
  (250, 26, 246, 2, 'This may be the Avett Brothers best song and there is literally only the live version ', '2025-07-06T14:37:55Z', 2),
  (251, 26, 247, 6, NULL, '2025-07-07T11:42:55Z', 4),
  (252, 26, 248, 9, 'absolute KINGS', '2025-07-07T02:40:16Z', 2),
  (253, 27, 249, 6, NULL, '2025-07-18T14:05:49Z', 6),
  (254, 27, 250, 13, 'There''s a certain vulnerability whenever a man sings in falsetto.  Couple that with the thematic content of this song and you have a heart-wrenching performance from an otherwise upbeat and cynical ska band.', '2025-07-18T00:49:24Z', -5),
  (255, 27, 251, 10, 'God Bless Tiny Tim', '2025-07-21T15:22:56Z', 5),
  (256, 27, 252, 5, NULL, '2025-07-20T16:03:00Z', 6),
  (257, 27, 253, 4, 'Not only is this not a woman, the artist is also not black…..and most offensively….is British ', '2025-07-18T14:59:29Z', 7),
  (258, 27, 254, 3, 'I always pictured the vocalizations at the beginning coming from a gorgeous Indian woman. Alas', '2025-07-18T16:23:13Z', 2),
  (259, 27, 255, 12, NULL, '2025-07-20T11:57:00Z', 3),
  (260, 27, 256, 2, NULL, '2025-07-21T16:06:26Z', 4),
  (261, 27, 257, 11, NULL, '2025-07-20T18:47:41Z', 2),
  (262, 27, 258, 1, NULL, '2025-07-21T16:32:53Z', 2),
  (263, 27, 259, 9, NULL, '2025-07-21T14:58:09Z', 1),
  (264, 27, 260, 14, NULL, '2025-07-20T17:25:25Z', 3),
  (265, 28, 261, 9, 'I know it’s a common song, but I figured I’d risk it cause she deserves it', '2025-07-23T17:50:58Z', 3),
  (266, 28, 262, 11, NULL, '2025-07-24T18:20:07Z', 1),
  (267, 28, 263, 13, 'I was introduced to this band by one of Eddie''s former roommates.', '2025-07-24T22:18:34Z', 2),
  (268, 28, 264, 4, 'Trying to pull a Sammy on you all here. I remember hearing this song when I was about four years old and absolutely loving it. Then for the next 12 years I could distinctly remember the best and the 1-2-3 counting but assumed the song was lost forever. Then one random day, I heard about half a second of the counting part as my mom was flipping through the radio and freaked out and made her flip back through until we found it. And since then it’s been an all-time favorite. One thing I think this reveals is that time and place play a huge role in the music I like, which makes it hard to guess. ', '2025-07-24T12:56:52Z', 1),
  (269, 28, 265, 6, NULL, '2025-07-23T17:05:22Z', 12),
  (270, 28, 266, 3, NULL, '2025-07-23T22:13:00Z', 2),
  (271, 28, 267, 2, NULL, '2025-07-23T17:45:38Z', 4),
  (272, 28, 268, 12, NULL, '2025-07-25T12:47:22Z', 3),
  (273, 28, 269, 5, 'Bob Dylan sound meets 2010s alt-indie', '2025-07-24T14:58:45Z', 0),
  (274, 28, 270, 1, NULL, '2025-07-23T17:32:08Z', 4),
  (275, 28, 271, 10, NULL, '2025-07-23T17:29:04Z', -1),
  (276, 28, 272, 14, 'Vibes with the softcore Catholic social justice themes Eddie personifies—a timeless Holes classic deserves a refresh on Eddie’s mixtape', '2025-07-25T12:36:17Z', 5),
  (277, 29, 273, 12, 'I love Flannery, but I''m having the darndest time finding something that''s accidentally her. So here''s some rural memento mori.', '2025-07-28T21:33:17Z', 3),
  (278, 29, 274, 5, NULL, '2025-07-27T17:26:59Z', 5),
  (279, 29, 275, 11, NULL, '2025-07-27T22:28:08Z', 1),
  (280, 29, 276, 9, NULL, '2025-07-27T23:37:42Z', 7),
  (281, 29, 277, 1, NULL, '2025-07-27T18:00:46Z', 5),
  (282, 29, 278, 14, 'Yes, I do believe she wears aviators and drives a very old car down the road when she’s listens to this one ', '2025-07-29T02:51:10Z', 2),
  (283, 29, 279, 2, NULL, '2025-07-27T17:29:02Z', 5),
  (284, 29, 280, 13, NULL, '2025-07-27T18:20:01Z', -2),
  (285, 29, 281, 4, 'There is a phrase in this song that I think perfectly summarizes every Flannery O’Connor story. ', '2025-07-28T15:29:43Z', 5),
  (286, 29, 282, 3, NULL, '2025-07-28T16:43:33Z', 4),
  (287, 29, 283, 10, NULL, '2025-07-28T21:48:47Z', 2),
  (288, 29, 284, 6, NULL, '2025-07-27T18:05:53Z', -4),
  (289, 30, 285, 6, NULL, '2025-07-31T12:39:58Z', 3),
  (290, 30, 286, 10, 'On repeat.', '2025-08-01T05:52:24Z', -2),
  (291, 30, 287, 2, NULL, '2025-07-31T03:30:25Z', 4),
  (292, 30, 288, 3, 'A maximally peaceful song to bring a little calm to the frenzy. Devin wrote this specifically to listen to amid the hustle and bustle of airports.', '2025-07-31T13:58:13Z', -2),
  (293, 30, 289, 13, NULL, '2025-08-01T21:40:42Z', 4),
  (294, 30, 290, 14, NULL, '2025-08-02T10:41:22Z', 4),
  (295, 30, 291, 12, 'I don''t know who I am, I don''t know why I''m here. All I know is I must pack.', '2025-08-01T22:32:37Z', 4),
  (296, 30, 292, 11, NULL, '2025-08-01T23:49:15Z', 8),
  (297, 30, 293, 1, 'Tested and approved by experts', '2025-07-31T03:29:12Z', 3),
  (298, 30, 294, 5, 'I moved to this song in 2023', '2025-07-31T06:16:31Z', 0),
  (299, 30, 295, 9, 'My sister gets the credit for this one (her fav Clara) (this is Clara typing it)', '2025-08-01T15:42:24Z', 7),
  (300, 31, 296, 5, 'I’m not sure this song is Juddcore sound, but it is Juddcore vibes at large', '2025-08-06T06:35:11Z', -1);
