  (844, 148, 10, 1, NULL, '2025-05-29T16:57:11Z'),
  (845, 151, 10, -1, NULL, '2025-05-29T16:57:11Z'),
  (846, 154, 5, 0, 'tbh, the Helder Camara quote "when I feed the poor, they call me a saint, but when I ask why the poor are hungry, they call me a communist" lives rent free in my brain and that''s why I submitted this song', '2025-06-10T03:22:12Z'),
  (847, 155, 5, -1, 'I''m v sad to downvote such a bop & want to be convinced more that this is "communist anthem"! Though I''m open to being corrected, first listen reads to me like an exploration of the suffering/real life challenges experienced by many and how love might serve as a response/motivator through those things', '2025-06-10T03:22:12Z'),
  (848, 156, 5, 0, 'Yep, that hit', '2025-06-10T03:22:12Z'),
  (849, 158, 5, 1, 'Okay wow this went way harder than I anticipated', '2025-06-10T03:22:12Z'),
  (850, 160, 5, 1, NULL, '2025-06-10T03:22:12Z'),
  (851, 162, 5, 1, NULL, '2025-06-10T03:22:12Z'),
  (852, 153, 8, 0, 'Nice but a third of the song was unnecessary intro. Endearing to some, but it annoyed me.', '2025-06-10T04:02:38Z'),
  (853, 154, 8, 0, 'I couldn''t tell if this was a man or a woman I was really sure that it was a man but then I googled it', '2025-06-10T04:02:38Z'),
  (854, 155, 8, 1, 'What an amazing pick for this category; it would have slipped my mind. Captures both a negative and positive aspect. Gotta love it and reward it.', '2025-06-10T04:02:38Z'),
  (855, 156, 8, 0, '"A bit much" - Larry David', '2025-06-10T04:02:38Z'),
  (856, 157, 8, 1, 'I didn''t begin the song thinking I''d love it, but it captured me by the end. The anger and frustration is palpable. Seething resentment for the play-acting rich college student--very well done.', '2025-06-10T04:02:38Z'),
  (857, 158, 8, 0, 'Imagining an army of Transformers Miatas and other cars marching in place and singing this song before a high maestro Joseph, high collared dracula cape around neck and hands busily turning knobs and dials on his synthesizer, conducting the mechanical orchestra.', '2025-06-10T04:02:38Z'),
  (858, 159, 8, 0, 'My father would have me go against the wall for not voting for this, but I just ran out of votes! I absolutely love the interpretation of the category; reflects deep reading.', '2025-06-10T04:02:38Z'),
  (859, 161, 8, -1, 'Bella ciao is the best of the communist folk songs and remains a hot button thing in Italy today, but it is, as I said, a communist folk song. I was look for something more incidental and not directly communist here.', '2025-06-10T04:02:38Z'),
  (860, 162, 8, 0, 'Better picks for this category on American Idiot that the titular song.', '2025-06-10T04:02:38Z'),
  (861, 163, 8, 1, 'Harry McClintock is one of the great masters; if you like American folk, you better be thanking him, as he is at the head of that tradition in its modern form. This song perfectly captures the theme, portraying the fantastic, anarchic dreamland of the American hobo, whose modern successors are the schizophrenic drifters at OLR who will get into heaven long before any of us. You get my last upvote. ', '2025-06-10T04:02:38Z'),
  (862, 153, 6, 1, NULL, '2025-06-10T12:59:44Z'),
  (863, 154, 6, 1, NULL, '2025-06-10T12:59:44Z'),
  (864, 155, 6, -1, NULL, '2025-06-10T12:59:44Z'),
  (865, 156, 6, 1, NULL, '2025-06-10T12:59:44Z'),
  (866, 154, 4, 0, 'This was great, I’ve never heard it! Beat slightly by others. ', '2025-06-10T15:20:09Z'),
  (867, 155, 4, -1, 'I’m gonna make a bold (educated) guess here. This is a Joseph submission, chosen because he resents the category and wanted to subvert it with something not radical in the way Sammy intended it.
And therefore, -1', '2025-06-10T15:20:09Z'),
  (868, 156, 4, 0, 'As a RATM purist, I actually think there are like 5 other songs from them that would fit the category better. However, it’s a banger ', '2025-06-10T15:20:09Z'),
  (869, 157, 4, 1, 'I want to give this +2 because it’s such an incredible, near perfect song. However, it doesn’t jive as well with Sammy’s description. +1', '2025-06-10T15:20:09Z'),
