  (953, 169, 4, 0, 'I love this interpretation, which is very much legit. However, this is a bit too melancholic for me. Another choice from the “fallujah-core” corpus would have done better imo ', '2025-06-13T18:36:18Z'),
  (954, 170, 4, 1, 'The year: 2003. Your cousin is returning from his second deployment to Afghanistan and your aunt is holding a barbecue to welcome him home. His 18 year old girlfriend Kathy is pregnant but neither of them knows it yet. As you put down your carton of Bug Juice™(the fluorescent blue one), you see your aunt’s third husband, Daryl, smoking a cigarette as he places a few more dogs on the grill, silhouetted by a gentle sunset. All is right in the world. ', '2025-06-13T18:36:18Z'),
  (955, 171, 4, 0, 'This is a summer chilling song, but not one that screams grilling to me ', '2025-06-13T18:36:18Z'),
  (956, 172, 4, 0, 'Yes but not a standout imo ', '2025-06-13T18:36:18Z'),
  (957, 173, 4, 1, 'I love to hate this song, in the same way I hate to love it. It’s perfect, sadly. ', '2025-06-13T18:36:18Z'),
  (958, 174, 4, 0, 'Again, so good. But too melancholic. I think there’s a subtle distinction between “sunset grilling over an empty yard” and “summer grilling for friends” and I interpreted the latter as the way to go for this category. ', '2025-06-13T18:36:18Z'),
