  (1649, 271, 13, 0, 'Sounds almost enough like fleetwood mac to get a vote.', '2025-07-26T13:31:14Z'),
  (1650, 272, 13, 0, 'This is not even the most Eddie-coded Bradio song: https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=RCzBN-kUPHo

However, it does have funky + city pop vibes, which is on point.', '2025-07-26T13:31:14Z'),
  (1651, 273, 13, 0, 'While the Bob Dylan influence is there, it''s a little TOO there.  And anyone who is trying to be someone else too hard is definitely not Bob Dylan-esque.', '2025-07-26T13:31:14Z'),
  (1652, 274, 13, 1, NULL, '2025-07-26T13:31:14Z'),
  (1653, 276, 13, 1, 'This is the most unexpected upvote for me.  Could definitely see Eddie listening to this one while driving to his parents'' lake house on a Saturday morning.', '2025-07-26T13:31:14Z'),
  (1654, 265, 5, 0, 'The whole time, I just wanted to tell Eva, "slay girl!" Love the song.', '2025-07-26T18:06:56Z'),
  (1655, 269, 5, 2, 'This song is perfect and I loved every minute of it. TGoPR is one of my newfound Music League faves!! Thanks, Alex (I''m like 98% sure?), for this.', '2025-07-26T18:06:56Z'),
  (1656, 270, 5, 1, 'This one surprised me... but I LOVED it. A vibe.', '2025-07-26T18:06:56Z'),
  (1657, 274, 5, 1, 'Such a bop.', '2025-07-26T18:06:56Z'),
  (1658, 275, 5, -1, 'I don''t know why this didn''t strike me as very Eddie (maybe I''m totally off the mark) but I LOVE the Band Camino. & this is one of my fave of their new songs! But... was really considering an Eddie aesthetic when voting, hence the downvote in the end :(', '2025-07-26T18:06:56Z'),
