  (1670, 269, 11, 1, 'Eddie loves a song that tells a story, and a story about the civil war? It’s almost too on the nose', '2025-07-27T04:28:10Z'),
  (1671, 270, 11, 1, 'Sad indie boy is an important facet of Eddie’s taste', '2025-07-27T04:28:10Z'),
  (1672, 271, 11, 0, 'hi Judd :)

Would’ve voted for this if I had more. Female fronted indie rock is squarely Eddie core
', '2025-07-27T04:28:10Z'),
  (1673, 273, 11, 0, 'I thought about voting for this one, and if I had more votes I probably would have, but it’s almost too Bob Dylan in a way that doesn’t feel sufficiently original (but I recognize that this comment will look really dumb if this was Eddie’s submission and/or he votes for it)', '2025-07-27T04:28:10Z'),
  (1674, 274, 11, 1, 'Maybe this is me falling prey to the Eddie caricature but this song is on point lyrically as well as musically imo. Building a 21st century city', '2025-07-27T04:28:10Z'),
  (1675, 275, 11, -1, 'Those who know me know how much I love this band, but I’m not sure I see Eddie vibing with this song in particular. I’d be happy to be proven wrong tho', '2025-07-27T04:28:10Z'),
  (1676, 276, 11, 1, 'I’m sure Eddie knows of shaggy but I could see him not knowing this song (I hadn’t heard it until now) and I feel like he could really rock with it', '2025-07-27T04:28:10Z'),
  (1677, 266, 2, 0, 'I quite enjoyed this', '2025-07-27T12:20:35Z'),
  (1678, 267, 2, 0, 'I’m not positive where this fits in the Eddie musical constellation but this was extremely fun', '2025-07-27T12:20:35Z'),
  (1679, 268, 2, 0, 'All respect to Gloria Estefan', '2025-07-27T12:20:35Z'),
  (1680, 269, 2, 2, 'I think this song is phenomenal, and I feel like Eddie would like it too. It’s grandiose in a way that I think Eddie will like', '2025-07-27T12:20:35Z'),
  (1681, 270, 2, 1, 'I’m not 100% positive that this hits the Eddie mark, but it is a great song, and for being just out-there enough I feel like I can justify an upvote ', '2025-07-27T12:20:35Z'),
  (1682, 272, 2, 0, 'This was good, but I think it is too modern and not citypop enough for a properly Eddiecore Japanese submission. ', '2025-07-27T12:20:35Z'),
  (1683, 273, 2, 0, 'I like this song but didn’t upvote just because it is almost too Bob Dylan-y', '2025-07-27T12:20:35Z'),
  (1684, 275, 2, -1, 'Great song but I’m not convinced it is sufficiently Eddiecore', '2025-07-27T12:20:35Z'),
  (1685, 276, 2, 1, 'I’m going out on a limb and saying that Eddie will enjoy this, I think it’s a hilarious out there choice to submit a Shaggy song for this round but I feel like I want to reward that kind of outside of the box thinking. ', '2025-07-27T12:20:35Z'),
  (1686, 265, 12, 1, NULL, '2025-07-27T15:47:39Z'),
  (1687, 269, 12, 2, NULL, '2025-07-27T15:47:39Z'),
  (1688, 271, 12, 1, NULL, '2025-07-27T15:47:39Z'),
  (1689, 276, 12, -1, 'I''m gambling on this one, but I trust my instincts.', '2025-07-27T15:47:39Z'),
  (1690, 265, 4, 0, 'You’re totally right that it was worth it to post this version even though this song is well known. I really enjoyed this, the vocal effect she brings to it makes it unique, even though it would be easy for it to just be another one of many versions. Despite what many think, I’m not actually a big singer-songwriter and folk fan in general. It’s only very specific types and artists, and this fit in the niche.', '2025-07-27T17:26:28Z'),
  (1691, 266, 4, 0, 'You are right to identify that I love the occasional alt girl indie pop. And I enjoy this song a good deal, even though it drifts a bit into sad girl territory. It won’t make it to the podium, but I enjoyed it a lot more on the second listen-through.', '2025-07-27T17:26:28Z'),
  (1692, 267, 4, 0, 'This is a straight banger, and really one of only two truly upbeat song of the bunch. Which is interesting because I would say I listen to upbeat music vastly more than I listen to anything else. This has Brad’s fingerprints all over it, although from the comment I think it’s probably Joseph. This is my choice for runner-up. I think I only went with the others over this because they were a bit more unique and out of the box.', '2025-07-27T17:26:28Z'),
  (1693, 269, 4, 1, 'This is a bold pick, since this type of history folk is often hit or miss in quality. But this one was a direct hit. Well done, knowing that I wouldn’t be able to resist a well crafted historical narrative and especially one about reigning in the treacherous confederacy. I’m also a sucker for regional Americana, and I love the exploration of having a deep Maine pride. One of my favorite themes is the mythologizing of the American experience, which is in so many ways, unique in the history of the world. We often think of ourselves as post-history, but we are simply the creators of the myths now. You could imagine someone 500 years from now hearing this with the same sense of wonder in the soldiers and Lincoln that we experience read about King Arthur and the Knights of the round table. This one got me a little emotional, well done. 
🥇', '2025-07-27T17:26:28Z'),
  (1694, 270, 4, 0, 'I enjoyed this song a lot, and the writing is really beautiful. But even though it picks up a bit, I found it still a bit more melancholy in a way that will keep it off the podium. ', '2025-07-27T17:26:28Z'),
  (1695, 271, 4, 1, 'This is one that I did not enjoy as much on the first listen, but came back to with much more love the second time around. Reminds me a lot of the cranberries. I really like the overall sound of this, there’s an earnestness to it that makes it sound very 90s in an achingly beautiful way. Seems like a Judd pull to me. Why people need to get it together and start making music like this again. 
🥉', '2025-07-27T17:26:28Z'),
  (1696, 272, 4, 0, 'The heart is in the right place for this one, and it’s a great song, but a bit more modern K-pop sounding, which is not my style with Japanese/korean music. This sounds beautiful though, the production is stellar. ', '2025-07-27T17:26:28Z'),
  (1697, 273, 4, -1, 'I really love the narrative of this one, it states something beautiful about male melancholy. 
Another one where you followed the thread dutifully and properly, but I am a weirdo and have no coherent sense whatsoever to my music taste. So I have to deeply apologize, because I think this was a pick made with love (and I receive it happily), but 2010s folk just doesn’t do it for me. And that’s not to say it’s not a good song, I enjoyed it, but if I had to rank (and I do)…..it must happen ', '2025-07-27T17:26:28Z'),
  (1698, 274, 4, 1, 'We love a content choice. Very bold and brave to choose a song that has to stand primarily on the merit of its theme. I was against this song for the first 30 seconds until they really get into it. And then I realized very clearly that this was a choice made with great love. I can only be who I am, and this sees me very clearly. I think often of how many hopes I still have for my life, and how many of them have not come to pass yet. And it makes me wonder what I’ve been doing all this time. But knowing the effort I’ve put in to cultivating community in the exact way this describes, knowing that it has made the lives of those I care about better, I know I’m doing all right. Thank you, my friends. 
The only reason this gets number two is because I think musically the other struck me more. But this one holds deeper personal meaning.
🥈', '2025-07-27T17:26:28Z'),
  (1699, 275, 4, 1, 'I really, really love this song, it reminds me of the one other band Camino song that I know. Which is a good thing, because I also love that one. It’s been topical recently to ask the question whether or not men truly urine, and the song should put that to rest.
4️⃣', '2025-07-27T17:26:28Z'),
  (1700, 276, 4, 0, 'Incredibly fun choice. I didn’t know Shaggy had it in him to be so philosophical. The curse of these rounds is that you get so many good songs, but you can only choose so many to be at the top. This is a great pick, but won’t make it to the top', '2025-07-27T17:26:28Z');
INSERT INTO votes (id, submission_id, voter_id, points, comment, created_at) VALUES
  (1701, 278, 13, 1, 'This song is weird and grotesque enough to be a FO''C story.  Though it''s hard to see where grace pops in.', '2025-07-29T13:58:48Z'),
  (1702, 280, 13, 1, 'The vision of the lone rider at the end of this story really gives it the mystical sheen it needs to be FO''C-esque', '2025-07-29T13:58:48Z'),
  (1703, 277, 13, 1, 'A phenomenal song. A bluegrass singer who has been performing for probably 50 years at this point.  A serenade to death would definitely take place in a FO''C story', '2025-07-29T13:58:48Z'),
  (1704, 281, 13, 0, 'A tale of romance and revenge, but not truly Flannery-esque, I''m sorry.', '2025-07-29T13:58:48Z'),
  (1705, 283, 13, 0, 'This song had potential, but it seemed like Jesus and the Virgin Mary were just things to be ignored.  I don''t think God is ever one to be ignored (without consequence) in an FO''C story.', '2025-07-29T13:58:48Z'),
  (1706, 284, 13, 0, 'The Whiskey washing over Tim can definitely be seen as a symbol of baptism, which takes place in the midst of the fury and warring of man.

"The uncontrollable mystery on the bestial floor" (Yeats)', '2025-07-29T13:58:48Z'),
  (1707, 286, 13, 1, NULL, '2025-07-29T13:58:48Z'),
  (1708, 287, 13, 0, 'I can''t pick this one simply because it''s a song of despair and cynicism.  Despite the darkness and ugliness of Flannery''s stories, there''s always a glimmer of light.  Bruce Springsteen seems to imply that people are delusional and that''s why they have a reason to believe.', '2025-07-29T13:58:48Z'),
  (1709, 288, 13, -1, 'I''m sorry, but this doesn''t really belong on this list.', '2025-07-29T13:58:48Z'),
  (1710, 278, 6, 1, NULL, '2025-07-29T14:32:45Z'),
  (1711, 281, 6, 1, NULL, '2025-07-29T14:32:45Z'),
  (1712, 282, 6, -1, NULL, '2025-07-29T14:32:45Z'),
  (1713, 283, 6, 1, NULL, '2025-07-29T14:32:45Z'),
  (1714, 284, 6, 1, NULL, '2025-07-29T14:32:45Z'),
  (1715, 277, 4, 0, 'Southern traditional does not a Flannery story make. I think this is a trap many fell into. My voting this round is 100% about themes - it''s easier (imo) to find a vibe fit (Southern Gothic) or a cool narrative than it is to tap into the flow of a theme that runs deep within the song that matches a theme embedded in the O''Connor mythos. I''ll be calling them out where I see them, and I don''t see one here. ', '2025-07-29T14:41:27Z'),
  (1716, 278, 4, 0, 'Hmmmmm everyone makes fun of Eddie for sending song recommendations after the rounds, but then they use them in future rounds 🤔🤔🤔

This pick is like Joe Torma at South Bend Idol. You hear it and you think this is “southern”! This is “gothic” and “grotesque”! But like Joe it’s all flair, coasting on adulation. Like Joe, we are in need of a Colleen to brutally shut down this nonsense before everyone gets carried away by surface level comparisons. This is not like a Flannery O’Connor story. It’s just southern and vaguely violent. There’s no themes here that fit, and to me, that’s much more important than the idea of grotesque story set in southern environs.', '2025-07-29T14:41:27Z'),
  (1717, 279, 4, 1, 'This was a great pick, and I think its strongest connection is the theme of being endlessly pursued by God. Dorothy Day opens her autobiography with the line from Dostoevsky “All my life I have been haunted by God.” This feeling of grasping futilely and for God but not wanting to go all the way is a theme I think you see in "Parker''s Back" and other O''Connor stories. Also, I only knew Julien Baker as "the small one from boygenius" so glad to know she can write a solo banger. ', '2025-07-29T14:41:27Z'),
  (1718, 280, 4, 0, 'Actually a great pick because it fits the overall theme in many Flannery stories of singular moments impacting people in huge ways. But there were a few others songs that I think slightly edged this one out for me. Runner up. ', '2025-07-29T14:41:27Z'),
  (1719, 281, 4, 0, 'Don''t see the fit here. If it had more religious imagery I could see it fitting, but it''s just a good narrative. Absent other elements it doesn''t connect imo. ', '2025-07-29T14:41:27Z'),
  (1720, 282, 4, 0, 'I really like this pick, the idea of being at a crossroads but unsure what to do is a good theme. But I think it needs to develop beyond that, and the song just doesn''t go any further. Totally fine, but that keeps it off the podium for me. ', '2025-07-29T14:41:27Z'),
  (1721, 283, 4, 1, 'Of all the songs, I think this one "gets" the feeling of a Flannery story best. The saccharine, commercialized, ever-present but unimposing sense of Christianity is captured perfectly by the "Plastic Jesus" image.  Reminds me very deeply of "Wise Blood". Seems like a Judd pick. Despite my insistence upon theme, I think this one wins a vote for setting up the start of a Flannery story perfectly. The character is poised for some sort of shock, followed up by the kitschy plastic Jesus staring dead eyed into her soul at the end. ', '2025-07-29T14:41:27Z'),
  (1722, 284, 4, -1, 'This is a straight banger but don''t see the fit at all. Not through vibe, narrative, or themes. ', '2025-07-29T14:41:27Z'),
  (1723, 285, 4, 0, 'In every Flannery O''Connor story, a character thinks they know what they want and who they are. Then through some inbreaking of grace, typically through the least likely avenue, they invariably get what they need. But never in the way they want to receive it. 
If I was to summarize every Flannery O''Connor story in one sentence, it would be "You can''t always get what you want, but if you try, sometimes you just might find, you get what you need."', '2025-07-29T14:41:27Z'),
  (1724, 286, 4, 1, 'I think it''s easier to find a vibe fit or a weird story, but it''s a lot harder and more meaningful to find a real deep fit with a theme in O''Connor stories. This one nails it with the visionary imagery all leading up the line "He will take you. If you run, he will chase you." ', '2025-07-29T14:41:27Z'),
  (1725, 287, 4, 1, 'This song combines the best of all worlds - Southern vibe fit, theme (although weaker than the others), and narrative. I am actually kind of mad, because I was trying to find a Springsteen song to use, but the vast majority of them are about a different kind of Americana and just miss the boat for O''Connor connection. The opening scene with the dead dog in the ditch could 100% be out of one of her stories. Belief in the face of the mundane and the tragic is a theme she explores too. I think theme fit is a bit weaker than others, otherwise this would be a +2. Incredible pull. ', '2025-07-29T14:41:27Z'),
  (1726, 288, 4, 0, 'I actually love this pick, especially because of the line "Your love is like a shadow on me all of the time." That''s classic Flannery. However, in my review, I think the Julien Baker song does this theme a little bit better. Runner up. ', '2025-07-29T14:41:27Z'),
  (1727, 277, 3, 1, 'Total classic and feels like a very Flannery vibe', '2025-07-29T14:49:17Z'),
  (1728, 278, 3, -1, 'This has the accidents of a Flannery story but feels lacking in substance. No emotional pull. The mystery in this song feels cheap, and thus it receives my downvote ', '2025-07-29T14:49:17Z'),
  (1729, 279, 3, 0, 'This just feels so musically lacking to me that I can’t give it a vote. The phrasing is really awkward and comes off as ‘music as lyric delivery mechanism.’ There are some intriguing lyrics here however, so I can see the angle', '2025-07-29T14:49:17Z'),
  (1730, 280, 3, 2, 'I love this pick not just because Sting wrote this song. Although the original is much more interesting, the Americana flavor brings out the O’Connorness of the song more for sure. What I love most about this song is that there seems to be forgiveness or even friendship implied between the lone rider and the boy who killed him at the end. That’s what makes this more than a standard murder ballad, and I wonder if it’s playing to a broader trope - something similar happens in Dune, where there’s this mysterious kinship between Paul and Jamis, the Fremen who Paul kills in ritual combat. Jamis appears to him in moments of crisis and supplies guidance. Anyways, great song', '2025-07-29T14:49:17Z'),
  (1731, 281, 3, 1, 'Yeah, this is it. Heartbreaking and beautiful. The last verse where they find her a century later is so spooky and really sells it for this round. ', '2025-07-29T14:49:17Z'),
  (1732, 282, 3, 0, 'Eh. Just not enough substance here when there are so many great picks.', '2025-07-29T14:49:17Z'),
  (1733, 283, 3, 0, 'Kind of cute I guess', '2025-07-29T14:49:17Z'),
  (1734, 284, 3, 0, 'No', '2025-07-29T14:49:17Z'),
  (1735, 285, 3, 0, 'I just can’t stand the Stones ', '2025-07-29T14:49:17Z'),
  (1736, 287, 3, 0, 'Decent enough lyrics at times but I just don’t like Springsteen. The vibe I get from him is a non musician who somehow ended up having a music career', '2025-07-29T14:49:17Z'),
  (1737, 288, 3, 0, 'Interesting read but not quite enough. Truly a great song though, pretty much prog pop', '2025-07-29T14:49:17Z'),
  (1738, 279, 5, 0, 'I love Julien Baker and unsurprisingly I loved this. Especially lyrically moving to pray with/about. I do indeed think that Julien and Flannery would be friends. Unfortunately other things in the end won out.', '2025-07-29T14:54:08Z'),
  (1739, 281, 5, 2, 'The sound & that plot twist at the end hit the nail on the head!! Yes yes yes!!', '2025-07-29T14:54:08Z'),
  (1740, 283, 5, 1, 'Okay this is fun!!! A bop & I totally agree — Flannery coded!', '2025-07-29T14:54:08Z'),
  (1741, 284, 5, 0, 'This surprised me. At first, I dead set against it— “no way” does Flannery give me Irish vibes. In the end, maybe I came around!!', '2025-07-29T14:54:08Z'),
  (1742, 285, 5, 0, 'Totally agree. I like this song, a classic, but I struggled a bit to connect it to Flannery in the end.', '2025-07-29T14:54:08Z'),
  (1743, 286, 5, 1, 'I loved this Sufjan moment I got to have on the South Shore line into Chicago. His sound is perfectly on brand Flannery, so too the religious & lyrical turns. Thank you for this.', '2025-07-29T14:54:08Z'),
  (1744, 287, 5, 0, 'I like this. I don’t know why this song feels like 5 years long to me… but a good pick. Especially the opening lines resonated.', '2025-07-29T14:54:08Z'),
  (1745, 288, 5, -1, 'I listened to this one like 3 times 1) because it’s a bop and 2) because I’m not sure if it strikes me as “accidentally Flannery.” In the end, I feel conflicted and have to think more about it. I love this song and its poetic description for love, but my read of Flannery’s take on love is more a project of expanding the categories of love, vs. a clinging/grasping one; for example, Revelation comes to mind: Flannery demands that Mrs. Turpin (and by extension all of us) see beyond her biases/stereotypes to love Mary Grace instead of writing her off as “white trash.” Flannery is so good at making me feel like I have to do the heart work to be more Christian than I say I am, in a sacrificial and ever growing way. So idk…in the end, I’m rambling and confused…how I often feel at the end of a Flannery work. Hahahah. ', '2025-07-29T14:54:08Z'),
  (1746, 279, 9, 0, 'I''m not sure if this captures O''Connor completely, but I think it''s close!', '2025-07-29T17:04:53Z'),
  (1747, 277, 9, 0, 'The fact that it''s a cappella adds an extra grittiness that is cool', '2025-07-29T17:04:53Z'),
  (1748, 278, 9, 1, NULL, '2025-07-29T17:04:53Z'),
  (1749, 281, 9, 1, NULL, '2025-07-29T17:04:53Z'),
  (1750, 282, 9, 1, NULL, '2025-07-29T17:04:53Z'),
  (1751, 283, 9, 0, 'I''m not sure that this fits, but it''s super cute!', '2025-07-29T17:04:53Z'),
  (1752, 284, 9, 0, 'Fiona-coded', '2025-07-29T17:04:53Z'),
  (1753, 285, 9, 1, NULL, '2025-07-29T17:04:53Z'),
  (1754, 288, 9, -1, 'Sam, if this is you, I still love you:) but I''m confused', '2025-07-29T17:04:53Z'),
  (1755, 286, 12, -1, NULL, '2025-07-29T18:09:18Z'),
  (1756, 282, 12, 1, NULL, '2025-07-29T18:09:18Z'),
  (1757, 278, 12, 1, NULL, '2025-07-29T18:09:18Z'),
  (1758, 280, 12, 2, NULL, '2025-07-29T18:09:18Z'),
  (1759, 281, 2, 0, 'I think this is a little bit too overt without the deeper religious epiphany ', '2025-07-29T20:00:27Z'),
  (1760, 282, 2, 0, 'I didn’t know John Mayer did this kind of sound tbh', '2025-07-29T20:00:27Z'),
  (1761, 283, 2, 0, 'Aside from getting the southern aesthetic right, the thing that makes this song thematically Flannery-coded to me is the image of the “plastic Jesus,” a kitschy, even ironic religious symbol that grins while the narrator is sinning in the backseat of the car. The image (blatant sin juxtaposed with kitschy religiosity) is ugly, honest, and secretly grace-filled. You don’t expect the real presence of Christ in the kitschy image, and yet He is really there. ', '2025-07-29T20:00:27Z'),
  (1762, 284, 2, -1, 'Accidentally James Joyce', '2025-07-29T20:00:27Z'),
  (1763, 285, 2, 1, 'This is an inspired take. Flannery O’Connor short story titles have a particular ring to them; this song title actually sounds like a Flannery short story title, which I had never noticed before despite hearing this song a million times. Thematically/aesthetically, it’s perfect too. The encounter with “Mr. Jimmy,” sharing a soda at the country drugstore while he simply whispers “Dead” to the narrator, could be a scene straight out of Wise Blood. The deceptive woman covered in blood (but is she really?). It’s murky, it’s violent but subtly so, it implies mystery and grace in weird ways. Never paid close attention to the words before. Great pick. ', '2025-07-29T20:00:27Z'),
  (1764, 286, 2, 1, 'Spooky, murky Christ images will always get my vote in a category like this. ', '2025-07-29T20:00:27Z'),
  (1765, 288, 2, 0, 'I’m not seeing it ', '2025-07-29T20:00:27Z'),
  (1766, 278, 2, 1, 'Of the more overt submissions in this round (straight up Southern violence), I think this one was my favorite. ', '2025-07-29T20:00:27Z'),
  (1767, 279, 2, 1, 'Saline communion in the back of an ambulance as an image for encountering Jesus after a horrific car accident? Bravo. Pure Flannery. ', '2025-07-29T20:00:27Z'),
  (1768, 280, 2, 0, 'This is a good shout but I think there’s almost too much falling action for it to be a Flannery story. The moment of epiphany/grace has to occur alongside the shock, normally we don’t see as much of the developing interior life as this song depicts. ', '2025-07-29T20:00:27Z'),
  (1769, 279, 1, -1, 'I almost skipped this because I hate her voice. Sorry shea (I think? Or Judd?) the words also confused me ', '2025-07-30T03:43:05Z'),
  (1770, 281, 1, 0, 'I should have submitted this last league so I had to now. It just sounds and feels like Flannery to me although the story isn’t perfect.', '2025-07-30T03:43:05Z'),
  (1771, 282, 1, 0, 'Unmemorable', '2025-07-30T03:43:05Z'),
  (1772, 283, 1, 1, 'This was a great pick. Parker’s Back for the lighthearted.', '2025-07-30T03:43:05Z'),
  (1773, 284, 1, 0, 'I love Irish music but it’s not Flannery enough for that reason regardless of lyrics. A ton of Irish songs are Flannery vibes if you overlook the Irishness (but I don’t).', '2025-07-30T03:43:05Z'),
  (1774, 285, 1, 1, 'My dad would sing this to us as kids and it was infuriating but imma do that to my kids too. This was an unexpected but great pick.', '2025-07-30T03:43:05Z'),
  (1775, 286, 1, 0, 'I hate his voice here personally ', '2025-07-30T03:43:05Z'),
  (1776, 287, 1, 1, 'I almost submitted bruce. This is a great pick!', '2025-07-30T03:43:05Z'),
  (1777, 288, 1, 0, 'This song always reminds me of in the movie diary of a wimpy kid when he gets the part of Dorothy in the play and this is his audition. But also the eclipse my freshman year of college. I don’t understand you for picking this. Go read some Flannery.', '2025-07-30T03:43:05Z'),
  (1778, 277, 1, 0, 'This is an example of a bit too on the nose for me. Just barely tho.', '2025-07-30T03:43:05Z'),
  (1779, 278, 1, 0, 'Didn’t like the voice enough but this is lyrically super duper strong ', '2025-07-30T03:43:05Z'),
  (1780, 280, 1, 1, 'This might be the perfect submission.', '2025-07-30T03:43:05Z'),
  (1781, 285, 11, 1, 'Getting what you need (not what you want) is very on point. The rest of the song didn’t quite fit the vibe imo. But it gets a vote from me because the hook is distinctively Flannery in a way that other songs were not', '2025-07-30T05:06:22Z'),
  (1782, 278, 11, 0, 'The South + violence, which is the classic Flannery vibe, and there’s mistaken identity too I guess, but there’s no real revelation that happens here ', '2025-07-30T05:06:22Z'),
  (1783, 280, 11, 1, 'A mistake is made, suffering follows, but the character has hope of forgiveness and prays for mercy as he faces death. Pretty on point
', '2025-07-30T05:06:22Z'),
  (1784, 281, 11, 0, 'Is the idea that Claire was going to sin, but her murder was a weird sort of mercy that kept her from going through with it? Maybe, but that doesn’t feel like that’s the point of the song, it feels more like a straight up southern murder song to me ', '2025-07-30T05:06:22Z'),
  (1785, 282, 11, 0, 'Love John Mayer but there’s not enough lyrically here for me to really judge how well it fits the, for better or worse, quite literary theme', '2025-07-30T05:06:22Z'),
  (1786, 283, 11, 1, 'Clearly the lyrics themselves are meant to be ironic from the perspective of the speaker, but I feel like the plastic Jesus motif is the sort of thing that you’d find in an O’Connor story that could end up later being the catalyst for some kind of spiritual experience. Even if keeping the plastic Jesus up there is more or less a joke, I think that still says something about the speaker’s awareness of their sin, and that conscience, however dulled or ignored it might be, could be where grace enters in. Am I reading into this too much? It’s possible', '2025-07-30T05:06:22Z'),
  (1787, 284, 11, -1, 'It’s a classic but it just doesn’t work for the theme imo. Sure, a dead man comes back to life, but in a gimmicky magical drinking song way', '2025-07-30T05:06:22Z'),
  (1788, 286, 11, 1, 'I feel like a broken record for voting for Sufjan every single time he’s submitted,  but this is a really good read of the theme imo. Little boy sees a fire in the backyard and it turns into this wild spiritual revelation. Is he delusional? Is it really a vision from God? Unclear. But he clearly was deeply impacted by it. That’s a Flannery O’Connor moment for sure', '2025-07-30T05:06:22Z'),
  (1789, 288, 11, 0, 'Did not vote for this song but it is an all time banger and I would be remiss if I did not acknowledge that fact', '2025-07-30T05:06:22Z'),
  (1790, 277, 10, 1, NULL, '2025-07-30T23:47:55Z'),
  (1791, 278, 10, 1, NULL, '2025-07-30T23:47:55Z'),
  (1792, 282, 10, 1, NULL, '2025-07-30T23:47:55Z'),
  (1793, 285, 10, 1, NULL, '2025-07-30T23:47:55Z'),
  (1794, 288, 10, -1, NULL, '2025-07-30T23:47:55Z'),
  (1795, 289, 1, 0, 'This doesn’t quite do it for me.', '2025-08-02T15:53:43Z'),
  (1796, 290, 1, -1, 'No. At least do a remix ', '2025-08-02T15:53:43Z'),
  (1797, 291, 1, 1, 'This and a silent film of Peter Seeley packing while also baking bread and dealing with a few barn animals running around the rectory  ', '2025-08-02T15:53:43Z'),
  (1798, 292, 1, 0, 'With headphones on I could see this helping me continue to hyper focus but I was looking for high energy ', '2025-08-02T15:53:43Z'),
  (1799, 293, 1, 0, 'Cute ', '2025-08-02T15:53:43Z'),
  (1800, 294, 1, 1, 'Yep this is the stuff ', '2025-08-02T15:53:43Z');
INSERT INTO votes (id, submission_id, voter_id, points, comment, created_at) VALUES
  (1801, 295, 1, 0, 'I personally just wouldn’t listen to this while packing but I respect your culture ', '2025-08-02T15:53:43Z'),
  (1802, 296, 1, 1, 'HELL YEAH 🔨🪚🪛🔩👷🏼‍♂️👷🏼‍♀️THATS THE POWER OF THE HOME DEPOT 🗣️🔊‼️💯™️📣🧡', '2025-08-02T15:53:43Z'),
  (1803, 297, 1, 0, 'Keeps the blood pumping but has you dancing through the stress', '2025-08-02T15:53:43Z'),
  (1804, 298, 1, 0, 'I enjoy the driving rhythm of this. More of a driving song to me though.', '2025-08-02T15:53:43Z'),
  (1805, 299, 1, 1, 'Hi Clara ily. Regina has discovered getting help with her submissions and it’s helping her in the polls.', '2025-08-02T15:53:43Z'),
  (1806, 290, 3, -1, 'Ha', '2025-08-02T18:43:34Z'),
  (1807, 289, 3, 0, 'Don’t really see the angle. For me this is going to need to be either frenetic or uber calm and this is neither', '2025-08-02T18:43:34Z'),
  (1808, 291, 3, 1, 'Inspired choice. Actually some pretty cool melodies in this ', '2025-08-02T18:43:34Z'),
  (1809, 293, 3, 0, 'I can never quite jive with Snarky Puppy. It’s all very funky and groovy but the melodies just don’t grab me. This is in theory a good submission, but there is stuff I greatly prefer in this genre (namely Explorer by T-Square)', '2025-08-02T18:43:34Z'),
  (1810, 294, 3, 0, 'Kind of annoying and empty sounding', '2025-08-02T18:43:34Z'),
  (1811, 295, 3, 1, 'Frantic. This is it', '2025-08-02T18:43:34Z'),
  (1812, 296, 3, 0, 'The industrial sounds are kind of a vibe. It’s got a surprising amount of ambience which I like. It’s not the Arctic Monkeys blues rock slop riff it could have been, and I appreciate that', '2025-08-02T18:43:34Z'),
  (1813, 297, 3, 1, 'This fits the vibe. Really fun song', '2025-08-02T18:43:34Z'),
