  (1875, 305, 3, 1, 'This feels thoroughly Juddcore, from the 90s alternative sound to the uncomfortable artist name to the mysterious and intriguing lyrics. The line “feed the tree” goes quite hard', '2025-08-07T17:09:30Z'),
  (1876, 304, 3, 0, 'Beautiful, I really love this. I don’t know if this will make Judd’s podium, but he will certainly enjoy', '2025-08-07T17:09:30Z'),
  (1877, 310, 3, 1, 'This seems alternative enough to pass. Least favorite of my upvotes but gotta reward it ', '2025-08-07T17:09:30Z'),
  (1878, 309, 3, 0, 'What is this guy’s voice?? He should be voicing an oversized lovable Disney side character', '2025-08-07T17:09:30Z'),
  (1879, 308, 3, 0, 'This was lovely, but a little too Midwest emo for Judd', '2025-08-07T17:09:30Z'),
  (1880, 306, 3, 2, 'From the very first chord I knew this was pure Juddcore. Piano rock is a load bearing log in Judd’s musical Hangar. I could easily picture him singing this for karaoke, more so than any other here, so it gets the double upvote.', '2025-08-07T17:09:30Z'),
  (1881, 300, 3, 0, 'This brings me back, Switchfoot was big for me in high school. Not super feeling it for Judd though. The up-and-down piano lick in the chorus is a major ick', '2025-08-07T17:09:30Z'),
  (1882, 301, 3, 0, 'Singing and playing upright bass is so cool. Unfortunately it’s not too memorable and feels a little lowkey for this round', '2025-08-07T17:09:30Z'),
  (1883, 302, 3, 0, 'Judd may well like this, but it’s a little too on the modern Latin pop side of things and not alternative enough', '2025-08-07T17:09:30Z'),
  (1884, 303, 3, -1, 'Even if I thought this would be Judd’s favorite song of all time, I could not in conscience vote because it is ANNOYING', '2025-08-07T17:09:30Z'),
