  (1929, 301, 12, 4, 'I wasn''t expecting to see Esperanza here, I''m going all in.', '2025-08-09T00:39:08Z'),
  (1930, 307, 12, -1, 'Unfortunately someone had to take the hit, and that someone is Radiohead.', '2025-08-09T00:39:08Z'),
  (1931, 300, 4, -1, 'Just don’t like it ', '2025-08-09T01:24:30Z'),
  (1932, 301, 4, 0, 'I think this is faux-Judd. And maybe I’m wrong. But Spanish is not the only key to his heart, and this needs more ', '2025-08-09T01:24:30Z'),
  (1933, 302, 4, 0, 'Adding a Joseph comment: This made no impression on me. ', '2025-08-09T01:24:30Z'),
  (1934, 303, 4, 1, 'I LOVE a Zydeco pick. Judd loves the regionalisms ', '2025-08-09T01:24:30Z'),
  (1935, 304, 4, 1, NULL, '2025-08-09T01:24:30Z'),
  (1936, 306, 4, 0, 'I liked this a good amount (especially the very sneaky Bob Dylan homage). But others stood out more to me. Runner up. ', '2025-08-09T01:24:30Z'),
  (1937, 307, 4, 0, 'Hate Radiohead, simple as. Sorry y’all. I know this is for Judd but I hope he doesn’t like it.', '2025-08-09T01:24:30Z'),
  (1938, 308, 4, 0, 'No from me ', '2025-08-09T01:24:30Z'),
  (1939, 309, 4, 0, 'This was my Alex trade so I will not vote out of principle. ', '2025-08-09T01:24:30Z'),
  (1940, 310, 4, 2, 'This is the only song on this list that I really and truly loved and felt that Judd would really and truly love through and through. Just a perfect 90s banger, everything you could want, yet somehow unknown. ', '2025-08-09T01:24:30Z'),
  (1941, 304, 2, 1, 'This was one of 2 songs on this list (besides my own submission) that I had already heard. And indeed it’s an excellent choice, because I love this song and I absolutely love this album. There are several songs on this album that I like more than this one and it’s beat out by a few other songs on this playlist, and I feel somewhat compelled to rate more highly songs that were altogether new to me. But for getting one of my favorite deep cut albums (seriously, these guys never made another record) this gets a vote. 
4️⃣', '2025-08-09T03:05:45Z'),
  (1942, 307, 2, 0, 'This was a great shout from Joseph, who knows exactly which Radiohead records I have and haven’t heard. It was narrowly beaten by other songs that I liked more through the whole runtime, but I do love Radiohead instrumentation and the breakdown around 3:57 is fantastic. ', '2025-08-09T03:05:45Z'),
  (1943, 308, 2, 0, 'I liked this but again not quite my style. I actually think the degree to which I like indie music is sort of overstated. I like alternative, which is a species of indie I suppose, but the really pared down singer songwriter-y SoundCloud indie sound isn’t quite my cup of tea. This is musically impressive though, just not particularly interesting to me. ', '2025-08-09T03:05:45Z'),
  (1944, 309, 2, 1, 'This was spectacular. I have been thinking for a while that I should probably do a Tom Waits deep dive, and listening to this was the sign I needed. I really appreciate that I had never heard this song before, and indeed I have very little familiarity with Tom Waits, so this was an introduction into a whole new experience for me. It’s exactly the kind of late 20th century experimental rock that I love. It’s bold and the lyrics are phenomenal. Poetic. I loved this and I especially loved that it is not a caricature of the kind of stuff I love. 
🥇', '2025-08-09T03:05:45Z'),
  (1945, 310, 2, 1, 'Now THIS is the kind of indie/alternative that I like. There were two songs on this playlist that I just fell in love with more instantly (or that I had already been in love with for a long time). But this is a fabulous shout. It starts out just a little too low and slow for my taste but the chorus is excellent. Bonus points for international band. Great shout. 
🥉', '2025-08-09T03:05:45Z'),
  (1946, 300, 2, -1, 'I appreciate the goal here. But this just isn’t what I listen to. It’s sort of giving fake indie, like acoustic pop masquerading as an indie song. It’s a little bit too poppy and not in the way that I like. The sound is maybe a bit too simple. ', '2025-08-09T03:05:45Z'),
  (1947, 301, 2, 0, 'I liked this song, but I didn’t love it. All my respect and love for Esperanza Spalding (I see you Regina ❤️) but this song is a little too sparse and pared down for me to LOVE. I love ostentatious instrumentation, a song as low key as this one is working a lot harder to keep my attention. Good submission tho 🇪🇸 ', '2025-08-09T03:05:45Z'),
  (1948, 302, 2, 0, 'This was a valiant submission and of course I love that there were a few Spanish tracks on this playlist. But this just isn’t the kind of Latin indie that I like. This song is good and very fun, but there’s just a little bit too much production and vocal modulation on it for me to love it. It’s a little bit too modern pop for my tastes. Good but not maximally my thing. Extremely awesome lyrics though. ', '2025-08-09T03:05:45Z'),
  (1949, 303, 2, 0, 'A sleeper hit. I’m getting Brad vibes from this? Which if so, well done, from someone who doesn’t really know anything about my music taste. This song gives me a hit of a genre I love and don’t talk about very much: traditional/classic R&B. This gets an honorable mention. 
5️⃣', '2025-08-09T03:05:45Z'),
  (1950, 305, 2, 1, 'A fantastic submission. Made me smile the instant I saw it. This was one of 2 songs I had heard already (besides my own submission) and this is a deeply nostalgic track for me. I almost chose it as my #1 for the round; but I felt compelled to give top spot to a song that was a completely new introduction to me. But seriously phenomenal read. 80s/90s female vocalist alternative rock is my jam always. 
🥈', '2025-08-09T03:05:45Z'),
