  (2167, 333, 3, 1, 'Classic', '2025-09-08T14:56:02Z'),
  (2168, 342, 3, 0, 'Imagine going on a coast to coast roadtrip and this is the only song you can play ', '2025-09-08T14:56:02Z'),
  (2169, 343, 3, 0, 'Unmemorable', '2025-09-08T14:56:02Z'),
  (2170, 344, 3, -1, NULL, '2025-09-08T14:56:02Z'),
  (2171, 333, 11, 1, 'It’s just a perfect song in general. But also perfect for driving with the windows down, reveling in the freedom of the open road, which to me was really the litmus test this round', '2025-09-08T17:53:41Z'),
  (2172, 337, 11, 1, 'Is it really a road trip if you don’t sink into a melancholy reverie at some point?', '2025-09-08T17:53:41Z'),
  (2173, 340, 11, 1, 'Your dad cooked with this one. Perfect vibe for driving through the CA mountains', '2025-09-08T17:53:41Z'),
  (2174, 341, 11, -1, 'I like the song well enough but downvote on grounds of anachronism', '2025-09-08T17:53:41Z'),
  (2175, 342, 11, 1, 'This is of course the canonical road trip song on how I met your mother and that’s all I can really think of when listening to this song in this round. I feel like it could be moderately annoying as a road trip song but if it’s late enough in the day and you’re the perfect amount of cracked/slap happy, it could absolutely hit', '2025-09-08T17:53:41Z'),
  (2176, 340, 4, 0, 'I’ve just never really liked this song. Can’t describe exactly why, since by all accounts it’s very good ', '2025-09-09T02:06:18Z'),
  (2177, 333, 4, 0, 'Yes, of course, but also not the vibe I was imagining. If you downvoted this, know that Joe Torma knows it was you and he felt it personally ', '2025-09-09T02:06:18Z'),
  (2178, 335, 4, 1, 'I have to assume this is Sammy’s return to music league, and he understands what no one else in this group does. And that’s that in 1995 if you were road tripping across America, you were listening to Garth Brooks.', '2025-09-09T02:06:18Z'),
  (2179, 336, 4, 1, '100% yes. This is exactly how this theme sits in my mind. Also, this song is the GOAT for literally having an entire verse that’s just the opening of “Idiot Wind” by Bob Dylan. That makes 2 songs in this playlist that prove the theory that every musician since 1965 is just trying to be Bob Dylan.  ', '2025-09-09T02:06:18Z'),
  (2180, 337, 4, 0, 'This was actually good, which I was sad to learn. Never been a big Radiohead guy, but props to Thom Yorke and whatnot ', '2025-09-09T02:06:18Z'),
  (2181, 339, 4, 1, 'Heck yeah. Absolutely. This to me is such a road trip vibe. Also the 2nd Bob Dylan shoutout, props for that. ', '2025-09-09T02:06:18Z'),
  (2182, 341, 4, -1, 'This song came out in 2013 ', '2025-09-09T02:06:18Z'),
  (2183, 342, 4, 0, 'Sorry Brad, but no', '2025-09-09T02:06:18Z'),
  (2184, 343, 4, 0, 'This is a banger, especially for being barely 2 min long. But not the vibe for me. ', '2025-09-09T02:06:18Z'),
  (2185, 344, 4, 1, 'I was not going to vote for this, but it just hits right especially when you think about driving through the western desert at night ', '2025-09-09T02:06:18Z'),
  (2186, 341, 5, -1, 'Hahah, I love everything absolutely about this song, but gotta downvote it for the sake of historical accuracy (released 2013)', '2025-09-09T02:32:05Z'),
  (2187, 344, 5, 1, 'An immaculate vibe. I want to come along for the ride!', '2025-09-09T02:32:05Z'),
  (2188, 342, 5, 1, NULL, '2025-09-09T02:32:05Z'),
  (2189, 333, 5, 1, NULL, '2025-09-09T02:32:05Z'),
