  (2225, 351, 1, 1, NULL, '2025-09-13T15:22:13Z'),
  (2226, 352, 1, 1, 'This one wasn’t the vibe I wanted but is the best outlaw song which is not the exact same thing as a villain. But it was great I enjoyed it and the fact that I didn’t have to go back and read the lyrics to check if it fit.', '2025-09-13T15:22:13Z'),
  (2227, 354, 1, 0, 'No', '2025-09-13T15:22:13Z'),
  (2228, 355, 1, 0, 'Honorable mention ', '2025-09-13T15:22:13Z'),
  (2229, 345, 4, 0, 'I just really don’t like this song, and it also strikes me as too cringe for the villain category', '2025-09-13T20:46:56Z'),
  (2230, 346, 4, 0, 'I’ve always been ambivalent on this song, but paying closer attention to it made me really dislike it. The lyric “looking at you leaving out the window that’s why they call it window pain” is maybe the worst lyric I have ever heard', '2025-09-13T20:46:56Z'),
  (2231, 347, 4, 0, 'This one is very on brand for the category, but at the same time, I can’t imagine Taylor Swift singing this without forcing it. Just can’t take you seriously when you put this out after 10+ years of girl pop.', '2025-09-13T20:46:56Z'),
  (2232, 348, 4, 2, 'This is the only one of the villain era 💅 style submissions I actually liked. Especially since this is so early in her career, it doesn’t come off as forced also love the idea of the guy thinking he’s the villain, but he’s not. It gets a second up vote because I think it was most on theme', '2025-09-13T20:46:56Z'),
  (2233, 349, 4, 1, 'A Prog rock song about a vaudeville style occultist magician. Easy upvote.', '2025-09-13T20:46:56Z'),
  (2234, 351, 4, 0, 'To me, this is too mopey to be villain era. I know she’s talking about being evil, but there’s too much simping. ', '2025-09-13T20:46:56Z'),
  (2235, 352, 4, 1, 'I enjoyed this a good deal, but I didn’t see it as a great fit for the category. However, I disliked most of the songs, so it comes out with an upvote.', '2025-09-13T20:46:56Z'),
  (2236, 353, 4, 0, 'This is the most Gen X slop song I have ever heard.', '2025-09-13T20:46:56Z'),
  (2237, 354, 4, -1, '￼ there are parts of this song that are so awkward and listless I was genuinely in awe', '2025-09-13T20:46:56Z'),
  (2238, 355, 4, 0, 'I want to make sure I am fair. I trashed a few of the girl villain era songs because I said they were cringe and insincere. This is the male version of that. Never liked this song.', '2025-09-13T20:46:56Z'),
  (2239, 356, 4, 0, 'I don’t actually think this is a good pull for the category, but it’s a great song', '2025-09-13T20:46:56Z'),
  (2240, 345, 11, -1, 'Fall out boy is one of the bands I love most in the world and it causes me actual pain to downvote but this just does not feel villainous to me', '2025-09-14T06:11:05Z'),
  (2241, 346, 11, 0, 'Another song that I really love but that doesn’t feel like it fits the theme. I feel like villainy isn’t the right way to describe the (admittedly dark and fraught) kind of relationship that’s depicted here ', '2025-09-14T06:11:05Z'),
  (2242, 347, 11, 1, 'I feel like I can’t not vote for this one. Girly villain era fr', '2025-09-14T06:11:05Z'),
  (2243, 348, 11, 0, 'Maybe this is a me problem but I’ve simply never liked this song, even thought I think some of her music is really cool. It’s pretty on theme but I simply am not moved to vote', '2025-09-14T06:11:05Z'),
  (2244, 354, 11, 1, 'I can’t say this is my favorite musically but I think it suits the theme well ', '2025-09-14T06:11:05Z'),
  (2245, 355, 11, 1, 'He’ll make a rich woman beg and make a good woman steal. Maybe not intended by the person who submitted, but when I heard that line I realized this song does in its own way speak to (my particular read of) the theme.', '2025-09-14T06:11:05Z'),
  (2246, 356, 11, 1, 'This is surely Sammy. And yet I’m voting for it anyway—why, you ask? Because it’s sassy, and in that sense, it captures the spirit of the 💅', '2025-09-14T06:11:05Z'),
