  (2722, 415, 5, 1, NULL, '2025-10-26T02:59:22Z'),
  (2723, 407, 2, 2, 'A psalm of 2pac', '2025-10-26T03:58:38Z'),
  (2724, 408, 2, 0, 'Big Thief knows how to write a downer ', '2025-10-26T03:58:38Z'),
  (2725, 409, 2, 1, 'Excellent', '2025-10-26T03:58:38Z'),
  (2726, 410, 2, 1, NULL, '2025-10-26T03:58:38Z'),
  (2727, 411, 2, -1, NULL, '2025-10-26T03:58:38Z'),
  (2728, 429, 3, 1, 'This is a little too chill for a kickoff, but the iconic intro helps a lot. I love this song so much though', '2025-10-28T15:49:11Z'),
  (2729, 428, 3, 0, 'Close. Not quite a kickoff', '2025-10-28T15:49:11Z'),
  (2730, 427, 3, 1, 'This is a good song and good fit. I never noticed how bizarre the singing in this is but it is unhinged ', '2025-10-28T15:49:11Z'),
  (2731, 426, 3, -1, 'Kind of sounds like Peter Gabriel which I like, but not a good fit for this at all', '2025-10-28T15:49:11Z'),
  (2732, 425, 3, 1, 'Yes, this works', '2025-10-28T15:49:11Z'),
  (2733, 421, 3, 0, 'This is a great song. More of a second hour of road trip song though ', '2025-10-28T15:49:11Z'),
  (2734, 420, 3, 0, 'Absolutely a 10/10 road trip song, but only once things have simmered down nicely, preferably during sunset or after nightfall. This is for the part of the roadtrip where half the passengers in the back are sleeping and a quiet conversation is taking place between the driver and copilot', '2025-10-28T15:49:11Z'),
  (2735, 416, 3, 0, 'The production on this album is absolutely immaculate. It’s kind of a wonder to listen to just for that, but unfortunately it’s lipstick on a very dull and uninteresting pig. These riffs would have been cliche in 1970, much less 2002, and the vocals, while impressive, are hook free ', '2025-10-28T15:49:11Z'),
  (2736, 419, 3, 0, 'Just not feeling it', '2025-10-28T15:49:11Z'),
  (2737, 418, 3, 0, 'This is good for the last third of a road trip as the light starts to go golden, this is in no way hype enough for a kickoff', '2025-10-28T15:49:11Z'),
  (2738, 417, 3, 1, 'Hi Judd', '2025-10-28T15:49:11Z'),
  (2739, 420, 12, 1, NULL, '2025-10-28T16:34:49Z'),
  (2740, 419, 12, -1, 'May just be me, but this feels more like an intracity drive track than a proper road trip song.', '2025-10-28T16:34:49Z'),
  (2741, 424, 12, 2, NULL, '2025-10-28T16:34:49Z'),
  (2742, 425, 12, 1, NULL, '2025-10-28T16:34:49Z'),
  (2743, 417, 4, 0, 'This is a really great song! But.....hear me out.....I really don''t feel like this is a round for unheard of songs. To me a road trip kickoff involved other people, and to get them hyped, you need a song with shared memory. This is my own criteria, but it''s how I imagine the category. ', '2025-10-28T21:02:15Z'),
  (2744, 418, 4, 1, 'I was right away biased against this, because to me, road trip kickoff needs to be energetic. But I will say that as I listened, I could very easily picture a solo road trip, one meant to clear the mind and reflect, starting off with something like this. It expanded the category for me, and for that it gets a vote. ', '2025-10-28T21:02:15Z'),
  (2745, 419, 4, 0, 'This was my runner up for a 5th vote, if we had one. This is such a banger, and really gets the hype. I awarded my 4th vote to Peaceful Easy Feeling, however, since it really made me imagine a different view of the category that I could still relate to. ', '2025-10-28T21:02:15Z'),
  (2746, 416, 4, 0, 'This is a really great song. I always forget that Audioslave is just Rage Against the Machine with Chris Cornell instead of Zac de la Rocha on vocals. I should like them more than I do, and this song was great. But it didn''t stand out to me for the category, especially against some of the others. ', '2025-10-28T21:02:15Z'),
  (2747, 420, 4, 0, 'Absolute banger, but not one I would use for kickoff. This is a cruising into the sunset song. ', '2025-10-28T21:02:15Z'),
  (2748, 421, 4, 0, 'You could say it''s hypocritical of me to ignore this one and upvote the other Eagles song, but this one does not invoke for me the same "Let''s start on a new journey" feeling that  Peaceful Easy Feeling does.', '2025-10-28T21:02:15Z'),
  (2749, 422, 4, 1, 'My friend Nick had a music blog back in the day when people had music blogs, and he had an article that actually inspired this category. He said the best road trip kickoff song when you''re 16-22 is "The Great Escape" by Boys Like Girls (my runner up for my submission) - "for when you''re young and still feel the shiny promise of life". And that "Thunder Road" is the perfect kickoff song for "when you''re past college and the gleam and glamour is starting to wear thin and you''re wondering what life might hold." I agree with him still, and therefore this gets my vote. Impeccable choice. ', '2025-10-28T21:02:15Z'),
  (2750, 423, 4, 0, 'I love this song, and it''s a cruising song for sure, but would not be my kickoff song. ', '2025-10-28T21:02:15Z'),
  (2751, 424, 4, 1, 'It''s so cliche, but then as soon as the beat hits you know exactly why it''s achieved that status. It''s infectious, you can''t argue with it. It does exactly what it tries to do, which is be perfect for starting out on the road. ', '2025-10-28T21:02:15Z'),
  (2752, 425, 4, 1, '100% - perfect choice. Hype, destination, energy, raucousness. You can imagine a car of the bros belting it out as you start. ', '2025-10-28T21:02:15Z'),
  (2753, 426, 4, -1, 'This is similar to Peaceful Easy Feeling in terms of the type of road trip vibe it creates, but sadly I am just not a big fan of Yusuf Islam, the artist formerly known as Cat Stevens. Probably the hardest downvote to assign so far, so don''t feel too bad! ', '2025-10-28T21:02:15Z'),
  (2754, 427, 4, 0, 'The whole world opens up with its immense potential as you listen to this song. The build up is perfect for drawing you in to the road trip mood.', '2025-10-28T21:02:15Z'),
  (2755, 428, 4, 0, 'Another absolute road trip banger (Alex) but not one I would use for kickoff. ', '2025-10-28T21:02:15Z'),
  (2756, 429, 4, 0, 'I do not see this as a road trip kickoff song. This is a late night, 2 hours into the road trip after dark has set in, type of song. Better than I remember it being tho. ', '2025-10-28T21:02:15Z'),
  (2757, 420, 1, 0, 'This is a little bit more middle of the road trip for me, but this is a classic for me and an ex of mine (in a fond way)', '2025-10-28T21:32:02Z'),
  (2758, 417, 1, -1, NULL, '2025-10-28T21:32:02Z'),
  (2759, 418, 1, 0, 'So good but I voted for only one eagle song and thought the other was better ', '2025-10-28T21:32:02Z'),
  (2760, 419, 1, 0, 'This was the easiest choice I’ve ever made for a submission. I just remembered this one time that I started a road trip this and it slapped. So I can be at peace that I was true to myself even if I get hate (if you’re hating it youre hating on the real me)', '2025-10-28T21:32:02Z'),
  (2761, 421, 1, 1, 'I think this wins as far as which eagles submission is best', '2025-10-28T21:32:02Z'),
  (2762, 422, 1, 0, 'I wanted to vote for Bruce but not enough votes ', '2025-10-28T21:32:02Z'),
  (2763, 424, 1, 1, 'OK, probably the definitive answer', '2025-10-28T21:32:02Z'),
  (2764, 426, 1, 0, 'I think the key part of this prompt is that it’s the very first song kicking off the roadtrip but many of these are great for middle of the trip vibes ', '2025-10-28T21:32:02Z'),
  (2765, 427, 1, 0, 'Damn i do NOT have enough votes ', '2025-10-28T21:32:02Z'),
  (2766, 428, 1, 1, 'Wait I’m crying we have a video of me dancing to this as a baby I love this song ', '2025-10-28T21:32:02Z'),
  (2767, 429, 1, 1, 'Yep. 

it’s basic in some ways but surely the people will exalt it and I won’t be mad ', '2025-10-28T21:32:02Z'),
  (2768, 416, 9, 1, NULL, '2025-10-28T22:26:54Z'),
  (2769, 425, 9, 0, 'This was #5 for me!', '2025-10-28T22:26:54Z'),
  (2770, 422, 9, 1, NULL, '2025-10-28T22:26:54Z'),
  (2771, 419, 9, -1, 'Not my vibe for the start of a road trip', '2025-10-28T22:26:54Z'),
  (2772, 429, 9, 1, NULL, '2025-10-28T22:26:54Z'),
  (2773, 427, 9, 1, NULL, '2025-10-28T22:26:54Z'),
  (2774, 418, 6, -1, NULL, '2025-10-28T22:53:29Z'),
  (2775, 416, 6, 1, NULL, '2025-10-28T22:53:29Z'),
  (2776, 419, 6, 3, NULL, '2025-10-28T22:53:29Z'),
  (2777, 420, 13, 0, 'This is 100% Eddie, only because I know of the personal connection you have to this song.

This song has a sort of nostalgic feeling to it, as if it''s more about the place that''s being left than the place you''re going.  Doesn''t quite have the pep or the build needed for a good kickoff song.', '2025-10-28T23:13:54Z'),
  (2778, 416, 13, 0, 'This had me tapping my foot.  But I''m not sure this is a road trip starter, a little too heavy.  But definitely a fun listen.', '2025-10-28T23:13:54Z'),
  (2779, 417, 13, 1, 'High energy.  I can imagine accelerating on the highway during the bridge on this one.', '2025-10-28T23:13:54Z'),
  (2780, 419, 13, -1, 'Can''t upvote this one, because the original version is called "let''s get retarded" (the rest of the lyrics remain unchanged) and has nothing to do with actually starting things off.', '2025-10-28T23:13:54Z'),
  (2781, 421, 13, 0, 'Halfway through a road trip? Absolutely.
Starting off a roadtrip? Not quite energetic enough.', '2025-10-28T23:13:54Z'),
  (2782, 422, 13, 0, 'The way this song builds just seems to lend itself really well to getting onto the highway and "rolling down the windows and letting back your hair"', '2025-10-28T23:13:54Z'),
  (2783, 424, 13, 0, '
Also, Cars is not a top 10 pixar movie', '2025-10-28T23:13:54Z'),
  (2784, 425, 13, 1, 'Where''s my car.  Need to jump in it and start driving after hearing this song.', '2025-10-28T23:13:54Z'),
  (2785, 426, 13, 0, 'I kept waiting for this song to build to something that it never built to.', '2025-10-28T23:13:54Z'),
  (2786, 427, 13, 1, '3 seconds in I knew.  Yes.', '2025-10-28T23:13:54Z'),
  (2787, 428, 13, 1, 'Love me some doobie brothers.  This is just a great song.', '2025-10-28T23:13:54Z'),
  (2788, 416, 8, 0, 'Truly terrible, nigh unlistenable. Should’ve known such a big group would traffic in poopoo', '2025-10-29T02:31:17Z'),
  (2789, 417, 8, 0, 'Nearly as bad as the first, slightly more tolerable.', '2025-10-29T02:31:17Z'),
  (2790, 418, 8, 0, 'Great song, but there’s a better Eagles pick here.', '2025-10-29T02:31:17Z'),
  (2791, 419, 8, 0, 'Millennial round from last league called, they want their submission back.', '2025-10-29T02:31:17Z'),
  (2792, 420, 8, 0, 'A superb song, one of the best country music songs ever written. The violin breaks my heart every time I listen to it. George is a singer whose voice stayed so consistent yet also changed in beautiful ways as he changed, and I hope that everyone here, young or old, longtime fans or newcomers, encounters the true joy that is George Strait. Too slow for theme, didn''t vote.', '2025-10-29T02:31:17Z'),
  (2793, 421, 8, 1, 'This was the Eagles'' song to pick. Right tempo', '2025-10-29T02:31:17Z'),
  (2794, 422, 8, 0, 'Hi Fiona! This doesn''t work!', '2025-10-29T02:31:17Z'),
  (2795, 424, 8, 1, 'One of the two songs on my shortlist, would be hypocritical not to vote for it. ', '2025-10-29T02:31:17Z'),
  (2796, 425, 8, 0, 'I owe Audioslave and the 88 an apology.', '2025-10-29T02:31:17Z'),
  (2797, 426, 8, 1, 'Hi Richard! Or Judd? Maybe Shea if the Communists in Theology have gotten to her just yet.

This is Augustine: the Song, and if you can''t see that, you''re a moral pervert. Cat Stevens was usually on during Roberts family car trips.', '2025-10-29T02:31:17Z'),
  (2798, 427, 8, 1, 'Ice Age!!! This was the second one on mu shortlist. Such an iconic intro, and the gobbledygook refrain with the whistling is peak 90s slop.', '2025-10-29T02:31:17Z'),
  (2799, 428, 8, 0, 'Pains me not to vote for this masterpiece but I''m out of votes. Hard 5th for sure.', '2025-10-29T02:31:17Z'),
  (2800, 429, 8, -1, 'Every damn U2 song is the same, and even so, you go with this instead of the obvious pick, "Still Haven''t Found What I''m Looking For." Mistake! Colin would never have done this!', '2025-10-29T02:31:17Z');
INSERT INTO votes (id, submission_id, voter_id, points, comment, created_at) VALUES
  (2801, 417, 15, -1, 'Eh. ', '2025-10-30T21:39:00Z'),
  (2802, 429, 15, 1, 'Very good getting you hyped but not going full bore just yet. ', '2025-10-30T21:39:00Z'),
  (2803, 428, 15, 1, NULL, '2025-10-30T21:39:00Z'),
  (2804, 425, 15, 0, 'This would be a great for the "it''s 3am and my adrenal glands can no longer process caffeine" part of the road trip ', '2025-10-30T21:39:00Z'),
  (2805, 424, 15, 2, 'This song makes me wish I had wheels. Not in the "own a car sense", but actual wheels as bodily appendages. ', '2025-10-30T21:39:00Z'),
  (2806, 423, 15, 0, 'I''d say this is great for the second day of the road trip, but not as a starter. ', '2025-10-30T21:39:00Z'),
  (2807, 421, 15, 0, 'Good for sixth hour of driving, right before lunch. ', '2025-10-30T21:39:00Z'),
  (2808, 420, 15, 0, 'Good for third or fourth hour of driving.', '2025-10-30T21:39:00Z'),
  (2809, 419, 15, 0, 'I wish to get ignant and hectic after listening to this song. Do I want to drive though? Not sure . ', '2025-10-30T21:39:00Z'),
  (2810, 416, 15, 0, 'Good for night driving.', '2025-10-30T21:39:00Z'),
  (2811, 418, 15, 0, 'Good middle of the road trip song', '2025-10-30T21:39:00Z'),
  (2812, 416, 16, -1, NULL, '2025-10-30T23:30:04Z'),
  (2813, 422, 16, 1, NULL, '2025-10-30T23:30:04Z'),
  (2814, 424, 16, 1, NULL, '2025-10-30T23:30:04Z'),
  (2815, 425, 16, 1, NULL, '2025-10-30T23:30:04Z'),
  (2816, 427, 16, 1, NULL, '2025-10-30T23:30:04Z'),
  (2817, 424, 11, 1, 'I didn’t submit this one bc I thought it would be too obvious/stereotypical and wouldn’t land. But the second it hit on the playlist I realized I was wrong. It’s just a perfect song.', '2025-10-31T19:41:06Z'),
  (2818, 420, 11, 1, NULL, '2025-10-31T19:41:06Z'),
  (2819, 416, 11, 1, 'Good vibes ', '2025-10-31T19:41:06Z'),
  (2820, 418, 11, -1, 'Love the song but of the two eagles songs it’s the one that feels less apt for this round', '2025-10-31T19:41:06Z'),
  (2821, 429, 11, 0, 'I genuinely think this song sounds like what the beginning of a beautiful driving adventure feels like', '2025-10-31T19:41:06Z'),
  (2822, 426, 11, 0, 'Lyrically on theme but didn’t hit music/vibe wise for me', '2025-10-31T19:41:06Z'),
  (2823, 425, 11, 1, 'Got me pumped in exactly the way I want to be pumped for a road trip', '2025-10-31T19:41:06Z'),
  (2824, 418, 5, 1, NULL, '2025-10-31T23:45:15Z'),
  (2825, 424, 5, 1, NULL, '2025-10-31T23:45:15Z'),
  (2826, 426, 5, 1, NULL, '2025-10-31T23:45:15Z'),
  (2827, 428, 5, 1, NULL, '2025-10-31T23:45:15Z'),
  (2828, 416, 5, -1, NULL, '2025-10-31T23:45:15Z'),
  (2829, 426, 10, 1, NULL, '2025-11-01T00:05:45Z'),
  (2830, 424, 10, -1, NULL, '2025-11-01T00:05:45Z'),
  (2831, 419, 10, 1, NULL, '2025-11-01T00:05:45Z'),
  (2832, 417, 10, 1, NULL, '2025-11-01T00:05:45Z'),
  (2833, 428, 10, 1, NULL, '2025-11-01T00:05:45Z'),
  (2834, 422, 2, 0, 'As with other submissions (perhaps even my own, upon hearing the whole playlist): roadtrip, absolutely. Kickoff? I’m not convinced ', '2025-11-01T04:46:18Z'),
  (2835, 419, 2, -1, 'This would be a Corey-esque vote dump from me if the category were kicking off a homeroom party on the last day of sixth grade ', '2025-11-01T04:46:18Z'),
  (2836, 418, 2, 0, 'This is just too low key to be a trip opener. Also being The Eagles is an automatic -10 starting point that has to be overcome somehow (see elsewhere)', '2025-11-01T04:46:18Z'),
  (2837, 417, 2, 0, 'This has the energy of an Eddie submission. I’m not sure if I’m feeling it as a road trip kickoff but golly this is a bange', '2025-11-01T04:46:18Z'),
  (2838, 416, 2, 1, 'This is what blares from the open windows of the Redle family van on their weekly Sunday trip to Giant Eagle', '2025-11-01T04:46:18Z'),
  (2839, 429, 2, 0, 'Great song. Kind of an emo start to a road trip tho', '2025-11-01T04:46:18Z'),
  (2840, 427, 2, 1, 'hot take perhaps but the better of the two submissions from the soundtrack of an early 2000’s digitally animated movie', '2025-11-01T04:46:18Z'),
  (2841, 423, 2, 1, 'Yup. Definitive for a reason. No remarks. 10/10', '2025-11-01T04:46:18Z'),
  (2842, 421, 2, 1, 'See above. As the poet said, “I’ve had a long night and I hate the f-kin Eagles, man”—but with that said, something about this song and only this song really gets me. Platonic form of road trip song almost ', '2025-11-01T04:46:18Z'),
  (2843, 430, 1, -1, 'I….i wasn’t expecting this, a wild kickoff. Corey seems to like songs like this, but I’m not sure about the actual content and meaning of the lyrics.
But he likes a fast and clever/humorous song 

I’m under the impression however that he doesn’t like profanity 
Im downvoting because this offended my ears the most (sorta hate her voice but I tolerate ironic)', '2025-11-03T04:43:56Z'),
  (2844, 441, 1, 0, 'Should have saved for the sax round! ', '2025-11-03T04:43:56Z'),
  (2845, 439, 1, 0, 'Something that’s been in my rotation for several years and you might like my friend 🫱🏻‍🫲🏾', '2025-11-03T04:43:56Z'),
  (2846, 436, 1, 1, '🤘🏼💃🏻', '2025-11-03T04:43:56Z'),
  (2847, 435, 1, 2, '😌😌👦🏽🐍🐅🌳🪷🇮🇳🦜

👹💪🏽
🐑🐑 👦🏽🫱🏼🪨
😵
👦🏽🙌🏽🎖️', '2025-11-03T04:43:56Z'),
  (2848, 431, 1, 1, 'I enjoyed this ', '2025-11-03T04:43:56Z'),
  (2849, 437, 12, 0, 'Honestly, never been much of a Deltron guy. Too urban for my tastes, though I can respect the lyricality. Very Adult Swim.', '2025-11-03T05:38:05Z'),
  (2850, 438, 12, -1, 'Ok Go knows cuss words? I do feel targeted in an amusingly accurate way though.', '2025-11-03T05:38:05Z'),
  (2851, 439, 12, 0, 'The music is there, but the lyrics don''t quite mesh with me. I can''t quite explain it.', '2025-11-03T05:38:05Z'),
  (2852, 440, 12, 0, 'Locked in within 25 seconds. My neon is in overdrive. Incredible synths, very Daft Punk. This would fit in the Wraith soundtrack, with Charlie Sheen.', '2025-11-03T05:38:05Z'),
  (2853, 441, 12, 0, 'A potent rendition of a very nostalgic song. Nevermind, forget what I said, this saxophone is amazing. It has baritone? I feel seen. That genre shift is bonkers in Yonkers.', '2025-11-03T05:38:05Z'),
  (2854, 442, 12, 1, 'DON''T STOP TALKING TO ME I HAVEN''T BEEN LISTENING', '2025-11-03T05:38:05Z'),
  (2855, 431, 12, 0, 'Catchy, but like the above, it has very stiff competition, and I have only so many thumbs.', '2025-11-03T05:38:05Z'),
  (2856, 443, 12, 0, 'Feels like something I''d run into in one of my international compilation albums. Intriguing, but it doesn''t quite grab me.', '2025-11-03T05:38:05Z'),
  (2857, 430, 12, 0, 'I want to like this more, it has that grungy sound I love, but it faces stiff competition. Also Alanis dropping f bombs feels a little juvenile. I''ve never listened to her, but she always struck me as more respectable than that. She''s an alt-rock musician? I hadn''t the slightest idea.', '2025-11-03T05:38:05Z'),
  (2858, 432, 12, 0, 'Exceptional, appeals to my Brazilian side.', '2025-11-03T05:38:05Z'),
  (2859, 433, 12, 1, 'I need more thumbs, it''s unfair that I have to choose between this many strong contenders.', '2025-11-03T05:38:05Z'),
  (2860, 434, 12, 1, 'Oh BABY. I would shred around Tokyo Tower to this. That outro has more sex appeal than Aphrodite.', '2025-11-03T05:38:05Z'),
  (2861, 435, 12, 1, 'You wouldn''t know it, but I''ve been influenced by Gospel adjacent acapellas since highschool. Bravo for an unknowingly deep cut.', '2025-11-03T05:38:05Z'),
  (2862, 431, 3, 0, 'No', '2025-11-03T15:36:47Z'),
  (2863, 443, 3, -1, 'Sorry, this ain’t it', '2025-11-03T15:36:47Z'),
  (2864, 442, 3, 0, 'Very exciting seeing post hardcore in ML. This is really cool but I don’t think this is as on the money for Corey as others here. What an insane voice though', '2025-11-03T15:36:47Z'),
  (2865, 441, 3, 0, 'I’m torn on this. This feels almost a little obvious in a lazy way - just “video games plus jazz”. If you wanted to go the video games route, there are far more Corey-coded ways to go. Good idea, B- execution. Still, this song is a total banger', '2025-11-03T15:36:47Z'),
  (2866, 440, 3, 1, 'Ah, here we go. Musically and thematically perfect. Wouldn’t be surprised if the man himself submitted this', '2025-11-03T15:36:47Z'),
  (2867, 439, 3, 0, 'I don’t think Camino is quite Coreycore I’m afraid. I don’t think he would hate it still ', '2025-11-03T15:36:47Z'),
  (2868, 437, 3, 1, 'This is it!! An anarchist plot to overthrow one world government by crashing the world’s computer systems is as Coreycore as it gets. The super 90s beat and jungle-like atmosphere are perfect. The humorous undertones are spot on. I could easily picture Corey doing this (censored) for karaoke ', '2025-11-03T15:36:47Z'),
  (2869, 436, 3, 1, 'A techno love song full of computer metaphors seems spot on', '2025-11-03T15:36:47Z'),
  (2870, 435, 3, 0, 'I’m shocked and flabbergasted. I was going to comment “Jacob Collier at home” and then checked the year. I don’t understand how this was even possible in 1988. No pitch correction?? That was utterly unreal. Unfortunately, this doesn’t strike me as especially Corey, although he would certainly appreciate it.', '2025-11-03T15:36:47Z'),
  (2871, 433, 3, 1, 'I think this is just a little better than the other jazz-funk-pop song here, and Japanese is just a lot more Corey coded than Portuguese or whatever that other one was', '2025-11-03T15:36:47Z'),
  (2872, 432, 3, 0, 'Of the two submissions in this style, this is slightly worse', '2025-11-03T15:36:47Z'),
  (2873, 430, 3, 0, 'I think this is close, especially the very 90s verse. Some options here just nail the category more. The amount of poisonous vitriol this lady can distill into her voice is astonishing, have to say', '2025-11-03T15:36:47Z'),
  (2874, 432, 6, -1, NULL, '2025-11-03T18:45:57Z'),
  (2875, 438, 6, 3, 'Corey Nuke for Corey', '2025-11-03T18:45:57Z'),
  (2876, 437, 6, 1, NULL, '2025-11-03T18:45:57Z'),
  (2877, 431, 4, 0, 'This is a great song, I’ve only heard one other Saint Motel song and I liked that one too. I think this is a song Corey would like, but I just don’t think it stands out among the others.', '2025-11-03T19:58:13Z'),
  (2878, 432, 4, 0, 'Recognizing the spiritual connection between Japanese jazz fusion and Brazilian jazz funk notes that this submitter knows what they’re talking about. Sadly, I only have four votes to give. A common theme for this round.', '2025-11-03T19:58:13Z'),
  (2879, 433, 4, 0, 'Naturally, this whole round was chock full of good jazz fusion and/or city pop style songs. I think others beat this one.', '2025-11-03T19:58:13Z'),
  (2880, 434, 4, 1, 'I have a feeling this is Joseph, and while I don’t like the leading comment, all I had in mind while I was listening to this was Joseph’s idea of Tokyo Night Driving as a theme. This is my favorite of the jazzy submissions and knowing some of the stuff Corey has shared with me, I think it will be his as well.', '2025-11-03T19:58:13Z'),
  (2881, 435, 4, 1, 'I know that stylistically is not the same, but I was thinking during this about Corey’s love for the song Mack the Knife. Not only is this stylistically complex and beautiful, it also has the X factor of a little weirdness.', '2025-11-03T19:58:13Z'),
  (2882, 436, 4, 0, 'I really think Corey would like this a lot, but I’m on the eight or so songs where I feel similarly, this one just doesn’t rise high enough to get a vote', '2025-11-03T19:58:13Z'),
  (2883, 437, 4, 0, 'I''ve had this in mind for a Corey round for weeks. Early 2000s concept rap album about a dystopian society in the year 3030. Corey could actually be Del the Funky Homosapien (or Deltron 3030). ', '2025-11-03T19:58:13Z'),
  (2884, 438, 4, 0, 'I actually do think Corey is going to love this lol. Hearing OK Go say swear words is jarring, I always think of them as like a middle school band.', '2025-11-03T19:58:13Z'),
  (2885, 439, 4, 0, 'Great song, make it three by the band Camino that I like, Claire. But again, doesn’t rise to the top.', '2025-11-03T19:58:13Z'),
  (2886, 440, 4, 1, 'I am obsessed with this song. The sound, the vibe, and the specific cheesy, 90s anime dialogue style is so perfectly at tuned. I can imagine this as a scene in one of the old anime movies. I have watched with Corey. ', '2025-11-03T19:58:13Z'),
  (2887, 442, 4, 0, 'I have a feeling this might actually be Corey’s submission. From his extensive Hangar Dialogues™ with Joseph (available as a three CD set wherever fine media is sold) I know he likes this kind of thing. This is one where personal preference leads me to place this just outside the winner’s circle.', '2025-11-03T19:58:13Z'),
  (2888, 441, 4, 1, 'Not only knowing this exists, but then finding it on Spotify, elevates this to near perfection. ', '2025-11-03T19:58:13Z'),
  (2889, 443, 4, 0, 'This has Judd written all over it. Great song, but middle of the pack for me, and therefore, I assume it is also the middle of the pack for Corey. ', '2025-11-03T19:58:13Z'),
  (2890, 430, 4, -1, 'I want to downvote this, but have a sneaking suspicion it is actually Corey. It''s just so out of left field for what we know of his music taste. ', '2025-11-03T19:58:13Z'),
  (2891, 433, 8, 1, NULL, '2025-11-03T23:29:19Z'),
  (2892, 439, 8, -1, NULL, '2025-11-03T23:29:19Z'),
  (2893, 432, 8, 1, NULL, '2025-11-03T23:29:19Z'),
  (2894, 438, 8, 2, NULL, '2025-11-03T23:29:19Z'),
  (2895, 438, 13, 1, 'Would Corey tolerate the vulgarity?  Probably.  And I think he would probably sympathize with this song on a deep level.', '2025-11-04T00:48:29Z'),
  (2896, 430, 13, 0, 'I''m sorry, just didn''t like this one.  Although the chorus is definitely an earworm.  Would Corey Like it? Maybe.', '2025-11-04T00:48:29Z'),
  (2897, 432, 13, 1, 'Funky Fresh.  I can see a 1990s Corey strolling around town in some medium sized brazilian city with a Sony Walkman listening to this', '2025-11-04T00:48:29Z'),
  (2898, 434, 13, 0, 'Definitely sounds like the background track of a furistic metroidvania style game.  and I''m guessing this is Joseph''s submission.', '2025-11-04T00:48:29Z'),
  (2899, 435, 13, 1, 'Whoa.  This one blew me away with the dense harmonies, and the jazzy a capella break a minute into the song.  Loved it.  This also could have fit in the next category.  I think Corey would dig it.', '2025-11-04T00:48:29Z'),
  (2900, 436, 13, 0, 'I can imagine Corey as a DJ, and him blasting this song at a club.  But do I imagine him loving this song while he does it?  I don''t think so.  It just didn''t stand out to me.', '2025-11-04T00:48:29Z');
INSERT INTO votes (id, submission_id, voter_id, points, comment, created_at) VALUES
  (2901, 437, 13, 0, 'Eh.', '2025-11-04T00:48:29Z'),
  (2902, 439, 13, 0, 'I dug this one, but nothing about it stuck out to me as particularly Corey flavored.', '2025-11-04T00:48:29Z'),
  (2903, 441, 13, 0, 'I don''t know if I can vote for this one.  But I definitely want to hear Corey''s sultry voice talking about something over these smooth bars.', '2025-11-04T00:48:29Z'),
  (2904, 442, 13, -1, 'A whiny outlier on this list.  Would Corey like it? Maybe, but I don''t think so.', '2025-11-04T00:48:29Z'),
  (2905, 443, 13, 1, 'This is awesome.  And I think Corey would love it. Well chosen.', '2025-11-04T00:48:29Z'),
  (2906, 430, 15, 0, 'Eh.  ', '2025-11-04T04:32:48Z'),
  (2907, 438, 15, 0, 'I feel like this is a Brad song. Probably weirdly cathartic or something. ', '2025-11-04T04:32:48Z'),
  (2908, 440, 15, 1, 'I think this is Corey or Judd''s submission. Probably Corey''s.', '2025-11-04T04:32:48Z'),
  (2909, 442, 15, 0, 'Joe? Is this you?', '2025-11-04T04:32:48Z'),
  (2910, 441, 15, 1, 'He literally listens to this stuff all the time, it just has funny names like "Samurai Chicken Genshen" or "Honkey Tonk Sushimi Crusaders"', '2025-11-04T04:32:48Z'),
  (2911, 431, 15, 0, 'Corey would like this, but I gave only so many votes to give.', '2025-11-04T04:32:48Z'),
  (2912, 432, 15, 2, 'This song single handedly justifies the existence of the Portuguese language. Also, totally something Corey would love. ', '2025-11-04T04:32:48Z'),
  (2913, 433, 15, 0, 'If I had another vote I''d give it to this.', '2025-11-04T04:32:48Z'),
  (2914, 434, 15, 0, 'If I had another vote I''d give it to this.', '2025-11-04T04:32:48Z'),
  (2915, 437, 15, -1, 'Pain.', '2025-11-04T04:32:48Z'),
  (2916, 440, 16, 0, 'This is like Sonic the Hedgehog meets GTA.', '2025-11-06T00:18:14Z'),
  (2917, 435, 16, 0, 'This makes my blood boil with hatred for you pirouetting theatre nerds. ', '2025-11-06T00:18:14Z'),
  (2918, 433, 16, 0, 'This isn’t English either!', '2025-11-06T00:18:14Z'),
  (2919, 432, 16, 1, 'This isn’t English, but it seems pretty Corey.', '2025-11-06T00:18:14Z'),
  (2920, 430, 16, 1, 'Is it wishful thinking that Corey is the kind of man who would love Alanis Morissette but somehow has never heard of her? Yes. ', '2025-11-06T00:18:14Z'),
  (2921, 442, 16, -1, 'I don’t know what this is, but probably no one would love it. ', '2025-11-06T00:18:14Z'),
  (2922, 441, 16, 2, 'If there is a lobby between purgatory and heaven, this is the best approximation of the music there. And if there is a man who may be tempted to forego the beatific vision for a Nintendo themed auricular delight, well I hope that man is Corey. ', '2025-11-06T00:18:14Z'),
  (2923, 438, 10, -1, NULL, '2025-11-06T04:04:09Z'),
  (2924, 434, 10, 1, NULL, '2025-11-06T04:04:09Z'),
  (2925, 433, 10, 1, NULL, '2025-11-06T04:04:09Z'),
  (2926, 443, 10, 1, NULL, '2025-11-06T04:04:09Z'),
  (2927, 440, 10, 1, NULL, '2025-11-06T04:04:09Z'),
  (2928, 430, 11, 0, 'Generational banger, and a song that would be my go to karaoke track were I not wary of offending render ears. But I have absolutely no idea how Corey would feel about it', '2025-11-06T07:00:00Z'),
  (2929, 443, 11, 1, NULL, '2025-11-06T07:00:00Z'),
  (2930, 438, 11, 0, 'I have no idea whether Corey would like this song, but it definitely was stuck in my head for an entire freshman science class this week', '2025-11-06T07:00:00Z'),
  (2931, 439, 11, 0, 'I obviously love this song but I have zero intuition as to whether or not Corey would', '2025-11-06T07:00:00Z'),
  (2932, 434, 11, 1, 'I see the vision', '2025-11-06T07:00:00Z'),
  (2933, 433, 11, 1, 'Hell yeah', '2025-11-06T07:00:00Z'),
  (2934, 432, 11, 1, 'This merits an upvote purely on the merits of these lyrics:
“É hora de salvar a pélvis
Soltá-la, libertá-la
Agitá-la como o elvis
Grande guerreiro e mártir
Da nação do rock''n''roll”', '2025-11-06T07:00:00Z'),
  (2935, 431, 11, -1, 'Meh ¯\_(ツ)_/¯ ', '2025-11-06T07:00:00Z'),
  (2936, 435, 2, 0, 'gosh this is amazing. I am feeling the upvote scarcity ', '2025-11-06T13:45:40Z'),
  (2937, 431, 2, 0, 'I really like the one other Saint Motel song I’ve heard but this one is a little underwhelming and I don’t think I really see this as a Coreycore submission. ', '2025-11-06T13:45:40Z'),
  (2938, 430, 2, 0, 'an Alanis Morisette submission is an enlightened choice. I’m only not upvoting because lyrically I’m not sure if it’s exactly Corey’s thing, and I wouldn’t be surprised if he’s heard it already. Also it’s a stacked round and votes are in short supply', '2025-11-06T13:45:40Z'),
  (2939, 443, 2, 1, 'last but not least, wow. I thought I was being clever by submitting Brazilian funk and someone had to one up me with Senegalese folk fusion. Obscure international fusion rock is an essential pillar of the Coreybait genre ', '2025-11-06T13:45:40Z'),
  (2940, 442, 2, 0, 'we were missing a true blue emo track. Thank you for delivering ', '2025-11-06T13:45:40Z'),
  (2941, 441, 2, 0, 'Listening to this whole track made me appreciate anew how excellent the Mii Channel theme is from a video game music engineering perspective  ', '2025-11-06T13:45:40Z'),
  (2942, 440, 2, 1, 'I have a sneaking feeling this is the man himself. I would be pretty surprised if Corey has never heard this song before. But it is an utterly perfect choice (and if it isn’t Corey, then hats off to the submitter). Lyrically, thematically, sonically, pure unadulterated Coreybait. Should be a front runner. Also a banger. I need to listen to this whole album', '2025-11-06T13:45:40Z'),
  (2943, 439, 2, 0, 'yawn. Maybe Corey would like this but I say, next ', '2025-11-06T13:45:40Z'),
  (2944, 438, 2, -1, 'user was banished to the focaccia mines for this post ', '2025-11-06T13:45:40Z'),
  (2945, 437, 2, 1, 'This is a grand slam of a pick. Every part of it is perfect. The hook is funky, the lyrics are spectacular, this captures both the Corey ethos and a fairly niche part of the Coreycore genre. A+. ', '2025-11-06T13:45:40Z'),
  (2946, 436, 2, 0, 'This is the part of the playlist I hit snooze on, which admittedly is a good sign in terms of how much Corey (and Joseph) would love it. ', '2025-11-06T13:45:40Z'),
  (2947, 434, 2, 0, 'this sounds awesome and is full metal Corey. This makes the leaderboard if I had one more upvote ', '2025-11-06T13:45:40Z'),
  (2948, 433, 2, 1, 'JPop felt too easy but this is something special. Excellent pick. I am confident that Corey would love this song, and that is after all the name of the round. Also this lead vocalist sounds almost exactly like the lead singer of Frederic ', '2025-11-06T13:45:40Z'),
  (2949, 432, 9, 1, NULL, '2025-11-06T16:27:40Z'),
  (2950, 430, 9, -1, NULL, '2025-11-06T16:27:40Z'),
  (2951, 441, 9, 0, 'I’d like to think Corey vibes with this… ', '2025-11-06T16:27:40Z'),
  (2952, 437, 9, 1, 'Great read of Corey’s anarchist side', '2025-11-06T16:27:40Z'),
  (2953, 434, 9, 1, NULL, '2025-11-06T16:27:40Z'),
  (2954, 433, 9, 1, NULL, '2025-11-06T16:27:40Z'),
  (2955, 433, 5, 1, NULL, '2025-11-06T19:52:22Z'),
  (2956, 431, 5, 0, 'I tried to find my musical overlap with Corey... in the end, I''m not convinced I got it right! I do like this song though lol', '2025-11-06T19:52:22Z'),
