  (2965, 455, 6, 1, NULL, '2025-11-09T23:13:11Z'),
  (2966, 456, 6, -1, 'Feels more like a dream than a story. Love the song, for some reason just didn’t fit for me.', '2025-11-09T23:13:11Z'),
  (2967, 446, 6, 1, NULL, '2025-11-09T23:13:11Z'),
  (2968, 449, 6, 1, 'The blues brother version is better', '2025-11-09T23:13:11Z'),
  (2969, 447, 15, 0, 'Every time I hear this song , I think of an actual raccoon with a cowboy hat. It is only by the most strenuous mental effort that I dispel this image. ', '2025-11-10T04:30:20Z'),
  (2970, 456, 15, 0, 'Fun song, but everytime I listen to Rush I go into "Rush mode" in which I ignore the lyrics, forget which Rush song I''m listening to (they are all variations on a theme) and just vibe out. So I had no idea what the song was about until I looked up the lyrics. ', '2025-11-10T04:30:20Z'),
  (2971, 457, 15, 1, 'I hadn''t heard this before. I like it. ', '2025-11-10T04:30:20Z'),
  (2972, 448, 15, 0, 'I loved this song the first time I heard it, but after 70 times, I realized I didn''t love it so much. ', '2025-11-10T04:30:20Z'),
  (2973, 449, 15, 0, 'Classic song, but not a particularly narrative song. ', '2025-11-10T04:30:20Z'),
  (2974, 450, 15, 0, 'I hate it. I love it. I mostly hate it. Yet I am in awe or p', '2025-11-10T04:30:20Z'),
  (2975, 451, 15, 1, 'I was actually touched by the story .', '2025-11-10T04:30:20Z'),
  (2976, 452, 15, 2, 'This is heads and shoulders above everything else on this play list. ', '2025-11-10T04:30:20Z'),
  (2977, 455, 15, 0, 'I like this. Nuanced. ', '2025-11-10T04:30:20Z'),
  (2978, 444, 15, 0, 'The way he says "turkey" is the height of the song. Almost got a vote for that alone.', '2025-11-10T04:30:20Z'),
  (2979, 445, 15, -1, 'Ghastly little story. Music is alright.  I was expecting something more tropical. Down vote for not living up to such an enticing title and for obnoxious ending. ', '2025-11-10T04:30:20Z'),
  (2980, 453, 4, 1, 'The story song with no real point is one of the best country traditions to still live on in some ways. ', '2025-11-10T14:02:33Z'),
  (2981, 444, 4, 0, 'Women, amirite???', '2025-11-10T14:02:33Z'),
  (2982, 445, 4, 0, 'This was fun, and it made me realize "Biggest Ball of Twin in Minnesota" by Weird Al is a style parody of this song. But didn''t stand out above others. ', '2025-11-10T14:02:33Z'),
  (2983, 446, 4, 1, 'This was my favorite by a large margin. Well done. I had considered 2 other Stan Rogers songs for my own submission, but this one beats them both. ', '2025-11-10T14:02:33Z'),
  (2984, 447, 4, 0, 'It''s always important to remember that all the 60s British invasion bands just wanted to be American country and blues artists. Love this song. ', '2025-11-10T14:02:33Z'),
  (2985, 448, 4, 0, 'It''s the GOAT, but a bit of a tired submission for this group, who have heard us talk about it ad nauseam.', '2025-11-10T14:02:33Z'),
  (2986, 449, 4, 0, 'Should have submitted the Blues Brothers version', '2025-11-10T14:02:33Z'),
  (2987, 450, 4, 0, 'One of the songs I''m most glad to have heard live', '2025-11-10T14:02:33Z'),
  (2988, 451, 4, 0, 'It''s the GOAT - only doesn''t get a vote because I want to prioritize songs that we don''t all know. ', '2025-11-10T14:02:33Z'),
  (2989, 452, 4, 1, 'TUESDAY. 50 years on Tuesday. Hence the party/memorial. Getting a vote in spite of the fact we all know it. It''s just the best. ', '2025-11-10T14:02:33Z'),
  (2990, 454, 4, 0, 'This was so good, classic Americana mythos. 5th place for me, just misses a vote. ', '2025-11-10T14:02:33Z'),
  (2991, 455, 4, 0, 'Love this song idea and it''s good but didn''t stand above others. We don''t make up characters with full names for songs anymore, and that''s a shame.  ', '2025-11-10T14:02:33Z'),
  (2992, 456, 4, 1, 'I feel bad upvoting this because I didn''t upvote others that I know, and I have even submitted this for an earlier league lol. But it''s SO GOOD. ', '2025-11-10T14:02:33Z'),
  (2993, 457, 4, -1, 'I LOVE JIM CROCE and I like this song! But all these songs are great, and so I am choosing to downvote the one that stood out to me least, which was this one. ', '2025-11-10T14:02:33Z'),
  (2994, 444, 1, -1, 'Arguably not a song for 75%. Either way it sucks. You had your pick of all songs that tell a story and this is what you picked. Be better.', '2025-11-11T05:05:54Z'),
  (2995, 445, 1, 2, 'Lowkey Flannery O’Connor vibes. But then again maybe that’s too generous. Reads like a children’s book that would be read at a public school. ', '2025-11-11T05:05:54Z'),
  (2996, 446, 1, 1, 'Eh it’s ok ', '2025-11-11T05:05:54Z'),
  (2997, 447, 1, 0, 'Some of these are just not really enough to be a story like it’s a fragment of one. Reminds me of reading my middle school students writing assignments and also my 1st graders for that matter.', '2025-11-11T05:05:54Z'),
  (2998, 448, 1, 0, 'Pleasant sounding so I want to vote for it but it doesn’t really give story to me ', '2025-11-11T05:05:54Z'),
  (2999, 449, 1, 0, 'He says he’s going to tell a story and then he kinda doesn’t ', '2025-11-11T05:05:54Z'),
  (3000, 450, 1, 0, 'I think the key for me was songs that had melodic lyrics that told a story and this has a lot of talking', '2025-11-11T05:05:54Z');
INSERT INTO votes (id, submission_id, voter_id, points, comment, created_at) VALUES
  (3001, 451, 1, 0, 'I like this song a lot and im not sure what all to vote for but this song is similar to Livin on a Prayer in that it’s not really a story to me it’s just like oh a couple of people have it hard and we wanna get outta here together and we are in love etc', '2025-11-11T05:05:54Z'),
  (3002, 452, 1, 1, 'This gets a vote (and doubtless many more) and I know this is the perfect category for it but I wanted some more creativity. But I think most of these are weak submissions so I’ll give a vote for it actually being a story and for the meme lol', '2025-11-11T05:05:54Z'),
  (3003, 453, 1, 0, 'In all humility this is one of the only ones actually telling a story start to finish and you don’t even need to read the words to follow it.', '2025-11-11T05:05:54Z'),
  (3004, 454, 1, 0, 'Sorry this just isn’t a song it’s a guy talking ', '2025-11-11T05:05:54Z'),
  (3005, 455, 1, 0, 'Want to vote for this for S&G and also “Cory” in the league of Corey but it’s not really a narrative which is what I’m looking for ', '2025-11-11T05:05:54Z'),
  (3006, 456, 1, 0, 'My criteria are “could this be made into an illustrated book and read aloud?” And “does this tell a story with a beginning middle and end” (as well as is this actually being sung) and this doesn’t meet all of these ', '2025-11-11T05:05:54Z'),
  (3007, 457, 1, 0, 'Points for actual singing and brevity but it’s still not really giving story ', '2025-11-11T05:05:54Z'),
  (3008, 455, 3, 1, 'This is absolutely great. A rebuke to class resentment: the people who you think have it better than you are often miserable. It’s a great observation of human nature that the narrator still wants to be Richard Cory at the end of this. Also decently musically compelling. ', '2025-11-11T14:34:25Z'),
  (3009, 444, 3, 1, 'Incredible boomer “I hate my wife” energy. This is a clever and compelling song and as an enjoyer of country with talking in it I appreciated this ', '2025-11-11T14:34:25Z'),
  (3010, 445, 3, 0, 'This is not a very compelling or interesting story at the end of the day, basically nothing happens ', '2025-11-11T14:34:25Z'),
  (3011, 446, 3, 1, 'Hauntingly beautiful and leaves me with many questions. It’s a simple and brief story and but well told with just the right admixture of detail and vagueness', '2025-11-11T14:34:25Z'),
  (3012, 447, 3, 0, 'I would think there would be far more compelling Beatles options than this. This is not all that memorable (the white album is also just kind of weird and not always in a great way)', '2025-11-11T14:34:25Z'),
  (3013, 448, 3, 1, 'Amazing Bradcore submission. Hauntingly beautiful, sad, and hopeful', '2025-11-11T14:34:25Z'),
  (3014, 450, 3, -1, 'Brevity is the soul of wit', '2025-11-11T14:34:25Z'),
  (3015, 451, 3, 0, 'I’m very torn on this one. The narrative is very subtle and sad, it doesn’t hit you over the head with “this happened and then this happened” and leaves you to paint a picture of what is going on in these people’s lives. However, despite some strong melodies and sections, the way these solid pieces are put together dumps the momentum over and over again the way we get FOUR bars of that main guitar part between every verse and chorus. There’s also some awkward phrasing at some points and these fumbles hold the song back from receiving a vote. ', '2025-11-11T14:34:25Z'),
  (3016, 452, 3, 0, 'This feels a little too easy. Also, I’d never noticed but there is some really awkward phrasing at numerous points in this song. Sting would have done a much better job. Still, plenty of great iconic lines in this', '2025-11-11T14:34:25Z'),
  (3017, 453, 3, 0, 'Cute', '2025-11-11T14:34:25Z'),
  (3018, 454, 3, 0, 'The plaque just says “he was a really big guy”??? He saved your ungrateful lives! Come on this is stupid', '2025-11-11T14:34:25Z'),
  (3019, 457, 3, 0, 'Didn’t take in a single thing from this', '2025-11-11T14:34:25Z'),
  (3020, 445, 13, 0, 'Surprisingly morbid song of the heroism of a truck driver.  Didn''t much care for it musically but loved the story telling.', '2025-11-12T00:47:00Z'),
  (3021, 446, 13, 0, 'This was another story that was really just told with a musical background.  Great storytelling though.', '2025-11-12T00:47:00Z'),
  (3022, 447, 13, 0, 'Rocky faced with a choice as he confronts Gideon''s Bible.  Will he forgive the man or not?  It seems he does not, to his own demise.  Loved the honky tonk feel of this one.', '2025-11-12T00:47:00Z'),
  (3023, 448, 13, 0, 'Sadly, I think I submitted the second best song about a shipwreck.  What it has going for it is the sweet harmonies and psychological depth.  The other one is a better told story.  

But permit me a story.  This was one of those songs that I listened to for the first time and immediately listened to a second time.  And then a third.  The tears flowed, because it''s a beautiful song of hope.  And I eventually convinced the boys of the hangar to perform this together.  To my knowledge, it'' remains the only joint hangar musical performance (besides karaoke).', '2025-11-12T00:47:00Z'),
  (3024, 449, 13, 1, 'What even is a hoochie coocher? I think that''s a term made up for this song.', '2025-11-12T00:47:00Z'),
  (3025, 444, 13, 0, 'Hilarious title.  But they never should have gotten married.

I guess I was looking for more of a sing-songy song.  This is more talking over a musical background.', '2025-11-12T00:47:00Z'),
  (3026, 450, 13, 1, 'Man I think I could say every word to this song.  I''ve listened to it so many times.  It was the song I analyzed the lyrics for as a project in 7th grade language arts class.  I''m pretty sure my teacher hated me for it.

As far as story telling goes, though, it''s a bit meandering.', '2025-11-12T00:47:00Z'),
  (3027, 452, 13, 1, 'Hard to top this one.  ', '2025-11-12T00:47:00Z'),
  (3028, 453, 13, 0, 'This was fun and musically interesting!', '2025-11-12T00:47:00Z'),
  (3029, 454, 13, -1, 'A cool story of heroism and sacrifice. But not really a song.  ', '2025-11-12T00:47:00Z'),
  (3030, 455, 13, 0, 'Conflicted about this one, because while it technically tells a story, the story is just "rich guy kills himself." At first I thought I might downvote this, but the music saves it.', '2025-11-12T00:47:00Z'),
  (3031, 456, 13, 0, 'I don''t know if there''s a more joseph song than this one.  I just can''t imagine there''s anything that speaks to him than these lines:

Wind in my hair
Shifting and drifting
Mechanical music
Adrenaline surge
Well-weathered leather
Hot metal and oil
The scented country air
Sunlight on chrome
The blur of the landscape
Every nerve aware

But I just don''t really like Rush all that much.  I''m sorry Joseph.', '2025-11-12T00:47:00Z'),
  (3032, 457, 13, 1, 'This might be the best combination of musicality and narrative on the list.', '2025-11-12T00:47:00Z'),
  (3033, 444, 16, 0, 'There really isn’t much of a story here. Just a guy saying he lost a divorce battle a lot. ', '2025-11-12T00:59:46Z'),
  (3034, 445, 16, 0, 'What was this?', '2025-11-12T00:59:46Z'),
  (3035, 448, 16, 1, NULL, '2025-11-12T00:59:46Z'),
  (3036, 450, 16, 0, 'This song is amazing and awful and hilarious and terrible. ', '2025-11-12T00:59:46Z'),
  (3037, 452, 16, 1, 'I feel like a war of attrition against Eddie and now I have to vote for this song. ', '2025-11-12T00:59:46Z'),
  (3038, 453, 16, -1, 'I’m amazed this is the only country song submitted. I feel very blessed by that. ', '2025-11-12T00:59:46Z'),
  (3039, 454, 16, 1, 'Never heard this before, but it was excellent. ', '2025-11-12T00:59:46Z'),
  (3040, 455, 16, 1, 'This is the second song this round about me. ', '2025-11-12T00:59:46Z'),
  (3041, 456, 16, 0, 'It’s painful to not upvote Rush, but this is not much of a story. ', '2025-11-12T00:59:46Z'),
  (3042, 453, 11, 1, 'It’s a little silly but it’s def a story', '2025-11-12T06:57:19Z'),
  (3043, 444, 11, 0, 'I just feel like “she got all the money in the divorce” is hardly a story, even if you’re telling me the details of what she got', '2025-11-12T06:57:19Z'),
  (3044, 445, 11, 1, 'Yep this is for sure a story', '2025-11-12T06:57:19Z'),
  (3045, 446, 11, 1, 'I hadn’t heard this before. Enjoyed it', '2025-11-12T06:57:19Z'),
  (3046, 450, 11, 1, 'Hell yeah. Assuming this is Eddie. I haven’t heard this song in a number of years now and I’d forgotten just how many insane one liners it introduced into the young Murphy kids’ repertoire', '2025-11-12T06:57:19Z'),
  (3047, 452, 11, -1, 'Great song, incredibly significant historical event, it’s just not an original pull, sorry 🔔', '2025-11-12T06:57:19Z'),
  (3048, 456, 11, 0, 'Joseph I’m sorry but driving in a car isn’t a story', '2025-11-12T06:57:19Z'),
  (3049, 444, 5, 1, NULL, '2025-11-12T13:21:27Z'),
  (3050, 447, 5, 1, NULL, '2025-11-12T13:21:27Z'),
  (3051, 448, 5, 1, NULL, '2025-11-12T13:21:27Z'),
  (3052, 451, 5, 1, NULL, '2025-11-12T13:21:27Z'),
  (3053, 452, 5, -1, 'I LOVE this song, but it just felt like an easy choice with the timing of things!', '2025-11-12T13:21:27Z'),
  (3054, 457, 10, 1, NULL, '2025-11-12T14:06:13Z'),
  (3055, 454, 10, 1, NULL, '2025-11-12T14:06:13Z'),
  (3056, 455, 10, 1, NULL, '2025-11-12T14:06:13Z'),
  (3057, 456, 10, 1, NULL, '2025-11-12T14:06:13Z'),
  (3058, 451, 10, -1, NULL, '2025-11-12T14:06:13Z'),
  (3059, 450, 12, -1, NULL, '2025-11-12T14:16:09Z'),
  (3060, 454, 12, 2, 'At the bottom of this league lies a big, big song.', '2025-11-12T14:16:09Z'),
  (3061, 448, 12, 2, 'Always been a big fan of this one, it''s haunting, somber. Appeals to my melancholic side.', '2025-11-12T14:16:09Z'),
  (3062, 445, 2, 0, 'Musically I quite enjoyed this, and the narrative is interesting, and the line in the middle about the protagonist calling upon “the only man who could save him now” is great, as is “God, make this a dream!” All that said, it’s still just too much. There is no cathartic ending to this story, it’s just bleak and sad without a real payoff. It feels like the song can’t quite decide whether it’s supposed to be funny or sad and instead of threading the needle between those two, it doesn’t really fully succeed at either. It starts well and ends up frustrating.', '2025-11-12T16:51:25Z'),
  (3063, 447, 2, 1, 'I adore this song. One of my favorite Beatles tracks. It’s beautiful, funny, clever, poignant, everything a narrative song could be. I think Paul McCartney succeeds at doing the Americana thing here. ', '2025-11-12T16:51:25Z'),
  (3064, 448, 2, 0, 'Songs Mike Whitman Would Love', '2025-11-12T16:51:25Z'),
  (3065, 450, 2, 0, 'I did not care for Weird Al’s “Albuquerque.” Did not care for Albuquerque. It insists upon itself, Lois.', '2025-11-12T16:51:25Z'),
  (3066, 451, 2, 0, 'upon listening again I was struck by how the verses don’t rhyme, they’re just sort of stream of consciousness. Kind of cool', '2025-11-12T16:51:25Z'),
  (3067, 452, 2, 1, 'This seemed almost too easy, and then I listened again and had to give in. Unironically brings me to tears. These men died in the line of duty. I’m sorry for making light of their deaths ', '2025-11-12T16:51:25Z'),
  (3068, 453, 2, 0, 'this is how you write a cathartic ending to a funny song', '2025-11-12T16:51:25Z'),
  (3069, 454, 2, 1, 'When I was a kid, my family used to listen to Old Time Radio, and they would play the original CBS radio commercials from the 1950s. Half of them were commercials for cigarettes, pills, or Pepsi, and the other half were charming public service ads. In the latter category was this series of ads that were literally just retellings of old American tall tales like Paul Bunyan. This song captures that vibe exactly. Wonderful stuff ', '2025-11-12T16:51:25Z'),
  (3070, 456, 2, -1, 'Listened to this playlist with the lights off sitting in bed. This was the one song on the entire list that I finished and said, “I didn’t understand a single word of that story”', '2025-11-12T16:51:25Z'),
  (3071, 457, 2, 1, 'goodness gracious this is beautiful. Jim Croce was a poet', '2025-11-12T16:51:25Z'),
  (3072, 450, 9, 2, NULL, '2025-11-12T18:33:18Z'),
  (3073, 456, 9, 2, NULL, '2025-11-12T18:33:18Z'),
  (3074, 457, 9, -1, NULL, '2025-11-12T18:33:18Z'),
  (3075, 458, 3, 0, 'Lyrical concept is ok, I was hoping this would be some kind of emo song based on the title and was musically dissatisfied. What about this instrumentation and melody communicates angst and yearning? 

Also thought this was “Bellfurries” for a dreadful second', '2025-11-14T16:47:15Z'),
  (3076, 460, 3, 0, 'Tom Staffelbach league. This is a great song. It’s amazing how long they make you wait for the chorus but the payoff is worth it!', '2025-11-14T16:47:15Z'),
  (3077, 462, 3, 0, 'Boring', '2025-11-14T16:47:15Z'),
  (3078, 463, 3, 0, 'Polly is a weird name to fit in this song. There are multiple lines where I really don’t know what they mean. But the vibe is perfect for yearning', '2025-11-14T16:47:15Z'),
  (3079, 464, 3, -1, 'I knew from the first strum I would hate this', '2025-11-14T16:47:15Z'),
  (3080, 465, 3, 0, 'OK this was pretty decent! I don’t know how “yearning” this is as much as “I still like you” though. There are some head scratchers too. Why did you say you didn’t love him? This seems like a self created problem', '2025-11-14T16:47:15Z'),
  (3081, 466, 3, 0, 'Truly awful on every level', '2025-11-14T16:47:15Z'),
  (3082, 467, 3, 0, 'Good submission, I was going to upvote until I heard the Jeff Buckley. This is a great example of how rough-around-the-edges musicianship can contribute to a song. It really sounds like something a few college guys put together in a garage in the best way. The chorus progression is really weird and almost doesn’t work but major points for the creativity. ', '2025-11-14T16:47:15Z'),
  (3083, 468, 3, 2, 'YES!! This is music people! Incredible vocal performance, interesting writing, great musicianship all round. That prechorus guitar part is so perfect. Lyrically on point. I need to listen to Jeff Buckley more. ', '2025-11-14T16:47:15Z'),
  (3084, 469, 3, 2, 'How is this song so great? The pieces are so simple. This song is a transcendent dish at a 5-star restaurant made with vegetables from your dad’s garden. This is truly one for the ages and there is yearning in every note. ', '2025-11-14T16:47:15Z'),
  (3085, 470, 3, 0, 'Much better than the Bob Dylan version', '2025-11-14T16:47:15Z'),
  (3086, 458, 8, 0, 'ML Detective work will reward you with the identity of this poster.', '2025-11-14T23:01:28Z'),
  (3087, 459, 8, 0, 'Eddie hates Eric Clapton, but that''s a moral failing.', '2025-11-14T23:01:28Z'),
  (3088, 460, 8, 1, 'Easy money', '2025-11-14T23:01:28Z'),
  (3089, 461, 8, 1, 'Peter is doing Alex''s BNL bit from the first season of Music League with Stan Rogers, and I am here for it. Fantastic song.', '2025-11-14T23:01:28Z'),
  (3090, 462, 8, 0, 'Should''ve submitted from The Lonely Island', '2025-11-14T23:01:28Z'),
  (3091, 463, 8, 0, 'Very interesting album', '2025-11-14T23:01:28Z'),
  (3092, 464, 8, 0, 'Eddiecore', '2025-11-14T23:01:28Z'),
  (3093, 465, 8, 1, 'Better Eddiecore', '2025-11-14T23:01:28Z'),
  (3094, 466, 8, 0, 'This song is about a rat.', '2025-11-14T23:01:28Z'),
  (3095, 467, 8, 0, 'Hillsdalecore', '2025-11-14T23:01:28Z'),
  (3096, 469, 8, 1, 'Colincore, in fondest memory', '2025-11-14T23:01:28Z'),
  (3097, 470, 8, -1, 'Comedically bad', '2025-11-14T23:01:28Z'),
  (3098, 471, 8, 0, 'First learned about Jewel through the Woodstock 99 documentary. Good sick watch.', '2025-11-14T23:01:28Z'),
  (3099, 459, 15, 0, 'Very sad, knowing the backstory. But it doesn''t make me yearn. ', '2025-11-15T07:19:00Z'),
  (3100, 460, 15, -1, 'Pain, but not from longing.', '2025-11-15T07:19:00Z');
INSERT INTO votes (id, submission_id, voter_id, points, comment, created_at) VALUES
  (3101, 461, 15, 3, 'DEAR OLD STAN! DEAR OLD STAN! DEAR OLD STAN! ', '2025-11-15T07:19:00Z'),
  (3102, 464, 15, 0, 'Fun. Not yearny though. ', '2025-11-15T07:19:00Z'),
  (3103, 466, 15, 0, 'I don''t yearn for this. ', '2025-11-15T07:19:00Z'),
  (3104, 469, 15, 1, 'RIP Collin McCarthy. ', '2025-11-15T07:19:00Z'),
  (3105, 470, 15, 0, 'Ok. ', '2025-11-15T07:19:00Z'),
  (3106, 462, 6, 1, NULL, '2025-11-15T14:49:29Z'),
  (3107, 463, 6, -1, NULL, '2025-11-15T14:49:29Z'),
  (3108, 466, 6, 3, NULL, '2025-11-15T14:49:29Z'),
  (3109, 462, 9, 1, NULL, '2025-11-16T02:46:43Z'),
  (3110, 464, 9, 0, 'middle schoolers are indeed some of the most yearning creatures on the face of this earth. other songs spoke to me more personally, though.', '2025-11-16T02:46:43Z'),
  (3111, 465, 9, 1, 'love the vibe!', '2025-11-16T02:46:43Z'),
  (3112, 466, 9, -1, 'phenomenal song, but deeply disappointed that you didn’t choose the Linda Ronstadt/James Ingram version…', '2025-11-16T02:46:43Z'),
  (3113, 467, 9, 1, NULL, '2025-11-16T02:46:43Z'),
  (3114, 468, 9, 1, NULL, '2025-11-16T02:46:43Z'),
  (3115, 469, 9, 0, 'I’m going to give you the benefit of the doubt and assume that this was submitted by someone who wasn’t in the league when this was submitted', '2025-11-16T02:46:43Z'),
  (3116, 459, 5, 1, NULL, '2025-11-17T12:36:03Z'),
  (3117, 461, 5, 1, NULL, '2025-11-17T12:36:03Z'),
  (3118, 463, 5, -1, 'I hate to downvote based on preference! I''m sorry! It''s not you; it''s me!!! :(', '2025-11-17T12:36:03Z'),
  (3119, 464, 5, 1, NULL, '2025-11-17T12:36:03Z'),
  (3120, 470, 5, 1, NULL, '2025-11-17T12:36:03Z'),
  (3121, 458, 4, 0, 'I really liked this song a lot. One thing I realized through this playlist is that (and I think this is fair) a lot of people saw songs reflecting on loss as "yearning". Which I just don''t. It''s very very similar but the specific reality/context from which they sing impacts it in certain ways imo. My votes don''t perfectly reflect this, but I was biased against songs that were about loss. ', '2025-11-17T14:09:42Z'),
  (3122, 459, 4, -1, 'Just don''t like it. Never been an Eric Clapton fan', '2025-11-17T14:09:42Z'),
  (3123, 460, 4, 0, 'I feel like there needs to be an element of pathetic-ness to capture the true essence of the category.', '2025-11-17T14:09:42Z'),
  (3124, 461, 4, 1, 'A beautiful read on the category. Men can only truly yearn for 2 things: women and the sea. ', '2025-11-17T14:09:42Z'),
  (3125, 462, 4, 0, 'Cool song but didn''t really stand out to me', '2025-11-17T14:09:42Z'),
  (3126, 463, 4, 0, 'The song needs to speak for itself. ', '2025-11-17T14:09:42Z'),
  (3127, 464, 4, 1, 'Sammy told me "there''s a song on this playlist that is powerful Eddie bait." It was this one, and he was right. Could not love this more. I also think it gets the category as I envisioned it. You can''t really "yearn" for something you''ve already had. Too many of the songs are about that.That''s a different emotion. Very similar, but different in meaningful ways. ', '2025-11-17T14:09:42Z'),
  (3128, 465, 4, 1, '"I''m yearning for a man I rejected." Women, amirite? 
This is one of the most beautiful songs I can recall hearing in a long time. ', '2025-11-17T14:09:42Z'),
  (3129, 466, 4, 0, 'Sorry Richard or Alex, not gonna work', '2025-11-17T14:09:42Z'),
  (3130, 467, 4, 0, 'To me, a great yearning song needs to be pathetic, slightly cloying, and generally unattainable. To me this captures the "so hypothetical and unrealistic it''s creepy" vibe which men can tend towards. Also a banger and a perfect album ender.', '2025-11-17T14:09:42Z'),
  (3131, 468, 4, 0, 'This was beautiful! But again I''m biased against songs that are about loss.', '2025-11-17T14:09:42Z'),
  (3132, 469, 4, 1, 'I figure this is Brad, and on that chance I gave it a vote, even though it''s been submitted before. It really is a perfect submission, especially because it is about something not yet attained. I think yearning has to be about something you haven''t had yet. ', '2025-11-17T14:09:42Z'),
  (3133, 470, 4, 0, 'Bob Dylan original is better and better captures the yearning feeling imo', '2025-11-17T14:09:42Z'),
  (3134, 471, 4, 0, 'This is so beautiful! But it just missed the top 4 for me. I really liked it tho.', '2025-11-17T14:09:42Z'),
  (3135, 460, 12, 2, NULL, '2025-11-17T14:21:23Z'),
  (3136, 461, 12, 2, NULL, '2025-11-17T14:21:23Z'),
  (3137, 466, 12, -1, 'I don''t necessarily have a point against this song, but it had to go somewhere. Forgive me.', '2025-11-17T14:21:23Z'),
  (3138, 458, 1, 0, 'I like this but I usually go for songs that have sad music in addition to lyrics but thanks for showing me this song or reminding me about it ', '2025-11-17T14:47:10Z'),
  (3139, 459, 1, 0, 'Thanks for making me sad asf 
I’m glad there’s hope in the song tho ', '2025-11-17T14:47:10Z'),
  (3140, 461, 1, -1, NULL, '2025-11-17T14:47:10Z'),
  (3141, 462, 1, 2, NULL, '2025-11-17T14:47:10Z'),
  (3142, 463, 1, 1, NULL, '2025-11-17T14:47:10Z'),
  (3143, 468, 1, 1, NULL, '2025-11-17T14:47:10Z'),
  (3144, 469, 1, 0, 'A repeat so I’m gonna not vote for it but obviously a classic banger ', '2025-11-17T14:47:10Z'),
  (3145, 458, 11, 1, 'Yeah this is yearning for sure', '2025-11-17T18:55:52Z'),
  (3146, 459, 11, 0, 'This is so tragic, and I perhaps one could describe it as yearning, but it just seems like a different sort of emotion/experience than what I’m taking this category to be about', '2025-11-17T18:55:52Z'),
  (3147, 461, 11, 0, 'I love this version of the song. But this just wasn’t the kind of yearning I was looking for. Hard to explain', '2025-11-17T18:55:52Z'),
  (3148, 462, 11, 0, 'This is on theme for sure but just didn’t hit quite as hard as other songs of a similar genre on this list', '2025-11-17T18:55:52Z'),
  (3149, 463, 11, 1, 'Yeah this is big yearning hours', '2025-11-17T18:55:52Z'),
  (3150, 465, 11, -1, 'This has such an upbeat vibe musically that it doesn’t really feel yearn-y enough. Maybe that contrast is intentional and meant to be deep, but it didn’t work for me', '2025-11-17T18:55:52Z'),
  (3151, 466, 11, 1, 'Okay this is kinda corny but I like it. I’ve only seen a couple episodes of community so I have zero idea what the context is. Tbh I’m also just really pleased to see Donald Glover on a ML playlist ', '2025-11-17T18:55:52Z'),
  (3152, 467, 11, 1, 'Love this song—automatic upvote from me. When I saw this on the playlist I immediately thought of the Hillsdale forum article about the blue album featuring Dwight Lindley. Idk what that says about me', '2025-11-17T18:55:52Z'),
  (3153, 468, 11, 0, 'It’s a great song but feels like kind of stereotypical pull for this category. Maybe that’s me being too harsh. Idk', '2025-11-17T18:55:52Z'),
  (3154, 469, 11, 0, 'So first off: this is one of my favorite songs ever. I know the category doesn’t specify that the yearning in question has to be romantic, but I do think that I’m looking for songs with a sort of pathetic valence. Maybe it’s the CL talking, but this song is about something different to me: there’s a recognition that there’s something right and good about these longings not being fulfilled, and there’s a further truth that this reveals. So sadly it doesn’t get a vote from me (don’t tell Colin)', '2025-11-17T18:55:52Z'),
  (3155, 470, 11, 0, 'Obviously very yearning lyrics. But this version didn’t do it for me, idk', '2025-11-17T18:55:52Z'),
  (3156, 460, 16, -1, NULL, '2025-11-17T22:38:24Z'),
  (3157, 461, 16, 2, 'Yearning is in the voice. And this voice yearns', '2025-11-17T22:38:24Z'),
  (3158, 466, 16, 2, 'This gave me goosebumps, goosebumps of yearning. ', '2025-11-17T22:38:24Z'),
  (3159, 458, 13, 1, 'Toe-tapping.  The bridge of this song was tremendously encapsulating of longing in its simplicity:  "It was kiss kiss/ then it was bliss bliss/ then it was miss miss"  Beautifully simple and longing.', '2025-11-18T01:24:55Z'),
  (3160, 459, 13, 0, 'I know this song is memeable, but only because it''s so vulnerable.  I''m not sure this is longing as much as it is mourning.  Though the two are close, i think there''s a significant difference.', '2025-11-18T01:24:55Z'),
  (3161, 460, 13, 0, 'Young love longing.  Lover''s remorse isn''t quite longing IMO.', '2025-11-18T01:24:55Z'),
  (3162, 461, 13, 1, 'That guy in the background (you know exactly which one I''m talking about) is really doing all the work to cultivate an atmosphere of longing.

An interesting take on the category.  Most are about vague desire or longing for a lover.  This is about longing to explore for one born too late to explore the world.  I like the creativity of the pick.', '2025-11-18T01:24:55Z'),
  (3163, 462, 13, 0, 'Lover''s remorse is not quite longing IMO.', '2025-11-18T01:24:55Z'),
  (3164, 463, 13, 0, 'It''s not about longing.  At least the lyrics are hard to parse as those of longing.  Voice does all the work there.', '2025-11-18T01:24:55Z'),
  (3165, 464, 13, 1, 'Man what a fun song.  This might be the only one that I''ve added to my liked songs in all of these playlists so far.  Right up my alley.  It perfectly encapsulates the simplicity and bigness of 8th grade longing.

Citronella is definitely a name that someone gave to their child only because they don''t know what citronella is.', '2025-11-18T01:24:55Z'),
  (3166, 465, 13, 0, 'Musically very interesting and fun.  Lyrically lacking, and way too much reverb.', '2025-11-18T01:24:55Z'),
  (3167, 466, 13, 1, 'Man, what a pick.  Saw this on the list and couldn''t wait to get to it.  Knowing someone''s out there loving you and the eagerness to meet them definitely constitutes longing.', '2025-11-18T01:24:55Z'),
  (3168, 467, 13, -1, 'Only in dreams would this song be shorter or more interesting.', '2025-11-18T01:24:55Z'),
  (3169, 468, 13, 0, 'Lo''er, you should''ve come o''er', '2025-11-18T01:24:55Z'),
  (3170, 471, 13, 0, 'Her voice is perfectly longing. 5th place for me.', '2025-11-18T01:24:55Z'),
  (3171, 459, 10, 1, NULL, '2025-11-18T03:13:39Z'),
  (3172, 460, 10, 1, NULL, '2025-11-18T03:13:39Z'),
  (3173, 461, 10, -1, NULL, '2025-11-18T03:13:39Z'),
  (3174, 462, 10, 1, NULL, '2025-11-18T03:13:39Z'),
  (3175, 465, 10, 1, NULL, '2025-11-18T03:13:39Z'),
  (3176, 460, 2, 1, 'I don’t doubt that others will comment the same thing, that “yearning” and “break up pain” are certainly not the same thing. All the same, there’s something so definitive and deeply cutting about this song. It’s beautiful, so earnest and unbelievably painful. After a full listen to this playlist, Tom DeLonge and Mark Hoppus are still lingering as a voice inside my yed. ', '2025-11-18T05:05:10Z'),
  (3177, 461, 2, 1, 'Yup this counts. This is certainly a kind of yearning ', '2025-11-18T05:05:10Z'),
  (3178, 462, 2, 1, 'this is wonderful. Totally new discovery but this is beautiful and painful. The mountains are taller than ever before ', '2025-11-18T05:05:10Z'),
  (3179, 463, 2, 0, 'musically this is phenomenal. Instant add to a playlist of mine. Lyrically/thematically I think I got filtered a bit, didn’t seem as resonant as other entries.  ', '2025-11-18T05:05:10Z'),
  (3180, 464, 2, 1, 'bruh this is so good. That opening hook is pure honey. This is good old fashioned non weird non incel yearning. Irresistible ', '2025-11-18T05:05:10Z'),
  (3181, 466, 2, 0, 'wait this is perfect actually ', '2025-11-18T05:05:10Z'),
  (3182, 467, 2, 0, 'wow this playlist is so good. Shout out to one of the greatest albums ever made ', '2025-11-18T05:05:10Z'),
  (3183, 469, 2, 0, 'This is a great song and really is perfect for this theme. I guess it just sticks out to me less than some of the other submissions for reasons I can’t fully explain, maybe because it’s too general', '2025-11-18T05:05:10Z'),
  (3184, 471, 2, -1, 'Stacked playlist and this was simply the most forgettable song ', '2025-11-18T05:05:10Z'),
  (3185, 475, 8, 0, 'Good but unmemorable', '2025-11-20T04:02:17Z'),
  (3186, 485, 8, 0, 'Who names their kid mullato', '2025-11-20T04:02:17Z'),
  (3187, 484, 8, 0, 'My best friend''s uncle was hitchhiking, and after this one guy picked him up, he popped in a tape where this started playing. His uncle jumped out of the moving car.', '2025-11-20T04:02:17Z'),
  (3188, 483, 8, 0, 'Really tried hard one with this one, didn''t ya? Really dug deep, huh? ', '2025-11-20T04:02:17Z'),
  (3189, 482, 8, 2, 'Ooh, yes, yes, this is quite nice, yes!', '2025-11-20T04:02:17Z'),
  (3190, 481, 8, 0, 'Typical ', '2025-11-20T04:02:17Z'),
  (3191, 480, 8, 0, 'Good, not great', '2025-11-20T04:02:17Z'),
  (3192, 479, 8, 1, 'The Japanese love trumpets and other brass instruments', '2025-11-20T04:02:17Z'),
  (3193, 478, 8, -1, 'Shitty and annoying', '2025-11-20T04:02:17Z'),
  (3194, 477, 8, 1, 'Vangelis is Sammy bait', '2025-11-20T04:02:17Z'),
  (3195, 476, 8, 0, 'Slop but Honest Slop. Reminds me of the Squirtle meme. Sam?', '2025-11-20T04:02:17Z'),
  (3196, 472, 8, 0, 'December 27, 2013, for instance. Driving home at night in Louisville, KY. Delilah on the radio. This song is playing. Such good memories.', '2025-11-20T04:02:17Z'),
  (3197, 473, 8, 0, 'Good but unmemorable', '2025-11-20T04:02:17Z'),
  (3198, 474, 8, 0, 'Good but unmemorable', '2025-11-20T04:02:17Z'),
  (3199, 472, 1, 0, 'Ehhh', '2025-11-20T04:10:41Z'),
  (3200, 485, 1, 0, 'Sophisticated ', '2025-11-20T04:10:41Z');
INSERT INTO votes (id, submission_id, voter_id, points, comment, created_at) VALUES
  (3201, 484, 1, 0, 'Sure ', '2025-11-20T04:10:41Z'),
  (3202, 483, 1, 0, 'I mean yeah ', '2025-11-20T04:10:41Z'),
  (3203, 482, 1, 1, 'Ooh ', '2025-11-20T04:10:41Z'),
  (3204, 481, 1, 0, 'Sure ', '2025-11-20T04:10:41Z'),
  (3205, 480, 1, 1, 'Yes ', '2025-11-20T04:10:41Z'),
  (3206, 479, 1, 2, 'Reminds me of The Dance at the Gym from West Side Story ', '2025-11-20T04:10:41Z'),
  (3207, 478, 1, -1, 'Noo ', '2025-11-20T04:10:41Z'),
  (3208, 477, 1, 0, 'Yeah ', '2025-11-20T04:10:41Z'),
  (3209, 476, 1, 0, 'No', '2025-11-20T04:10:41Z'),
  (3210, 475, 1, 0, 'Ooh hm', '2025-11-20T04:10:41Z'),
  (3211, 474, 1, 0, 'Eh more unique than some tho ', '2025-11-20T04:10:41Z'),
  (3212, 473, 1, 0, 'fun fact I played alto sax in band, just wanted to share that ', '2025-11-20T04:10:41Z'),
  (3213, 484, 15, 1, 'It''s a classic for a reason.', '2025-11-20T04:32:41Z'),
  (3214, 472, 15, 0, 'Good.', '2025-11-20T04:32:41Z'),
  (3215, 473, 15, 0, 'Very good. I wish I had more upvotes to give.', '2025-11-20T04:32:41Z'),
  (3216, 474, 15, 1, 'Delicious.', '2025-11-20T04:32:41Z'),
  (3217, 476, 15, 0, 'Wonderful saxophone. Not a fan of that vocal style.', '2025-11-20T04:32:41Z'),
  (3218, 478, 15, -1, 'Obnoxious. This makes me want to cull the local simian population. ', '2025-11-20T04:32:41Z'),
  (3219, 479, 15, 0, 'Now I want to be a cowboy 🤠', '2025-11-20T04:32:41Z'),
  (3220, 481, 15, 0, 'Great. ', '2025-11-20T04:32:41Z'),
  (3221, 483, 15, 2, 'Fantastic intro. Everything works together fantastically.', '2025-11-20T04:32:41Z'),
  (3222, 485, 15, 0, 'Chill as frick.  Wish I had more upvotes to give.', '2025-11-20T04:32:41Z'),
  (3223, 480, 3, 0, 'The sax is not important enough to this. ', '2025-11-20T18:23:31Z'),
  (3224, 478, 3, 0, 'This song features a saxophone part', '2025-11-20T18:23:31Z'),
  (3225, 477, 3, 2, 'Stunning. I could fall in love to this, easily. Gorgeous, expressive, longing sax part that is actually memorable. This is especially great because the rest of the arrangement is as beautiful as the sax melody. ', '2025-11-20T18:23:31Z'),
  (3226, 476, 3, 0, 'Sounds messy and amateur. Still some nasty sax sounds though. ', '2025-11-20T18:23:31Z'),
  (3227, 475, 3, 0, 'This is cool in the same way the Bladerunner track is cool but that one is way cooler, sorry. This is really pretty though. ', '2025-11-20T18:23:31Z'),
  (3228, 473, 3, 0, 'I wish I had an ability to appreciate this, which I have to assume is an all-time great. To me, this sounds like random jazzy noodling. None of these melodies stick except for the vocals. Why do these jazz classics almost always have boring generic lyrics?', '2025-11-20T18:23:31Z'),
  (3229, 472, 3, 0, 'This was a lovely song. I wish the saxophone were more prominent, but that part at the end is lovely ', '2025-11-20T18:23:31Z'),
  (3230, 485, 3, 0, '😴 underwhelming musicianship, recording quality, writing.', '2025-11-20T18:23:31Z'),
  (3231, 484, 3, -1, 'I’m going to punish the obvious choice here. Every one of us thought about submitting this, so this just feels lazy. The sax equivalent of the stairway to heaven intro. Great, but ubiquitous and thus uninteresting. Honestly, aside from the iconic sax part, this song is utterly forgettable which would tank it anyways', '2025-11-20T18:23:31Z'),
  (3232, 483, 3, 0, 'Close but no 🚬', '2025-11-20T18:23:31Z'),
  (3233, 482, 3, 2, 'This is so good. The sax melody is both interesting and the centerpiece of the song, which is what I’m looking for this round. The rest of the song is also great. ', '2025-11-20T18:23:31Z'),
  (3234, 481, 3, 0, 'Absolute masterpiece. Packed with memorable parts, awesome singing, and with a phenomenal mix. However, the sax is very much just one part of the arrangement here and doesn’t stand out as a lead instrument. I’m going to reward songs where the sax part carries the song. ', '2025-11-20T18:23:31Z'),
  (3235, 479, 3, 0, 'Obviously very impressive. Could I hum back any part of this solo? Absolutely not. I’m just not a shred fan, I want a good memorable melody which this is not.', '2025-11-20T18:23:31Z'),
  (3236, 473, 6, 2, NULL, '2025-11-20T18:28:03Z'),
  (3237, 478, 6, 1, NULL, '2025-11-20T18:28:03Z'),
  (3238, 472, 6, -1, NULL, '2025-11-20T18:28:03Z'),
  (3239, 481, 6, 1, NULL, '2025-11-20T18:28:03Z'),
  (3240, 476, 9, 0, 'I may or may not have shouted when the saxophone started growling', '2025-11-21T20:27:43Z'),
  (3241, 474, 9, 1, 'I may or may not have shouted when the saxophone started growling', '2025-11-21T20:27:43Z'),
  (3242, 480, 9, -1, 'As a Michigander, I hate to downvote Bob Seager, but the saxophone in this song just didn’t stand out to me￼', '2025-11-21T20:27:43Z'),
  (3243, 479, 9, 1, NULL, '2025-11-21T20:27:43Z'),
  (3244, 477, 9, 0, 'This made me chuckle', '2025-11-21T20:27:43Z'),
  (3245, 473, 9, 1, 'yes', '2025-11-21T20:27:43Z'),
  (3246, 472, 9, 1, 'Normally, I don’t like breakup songs (or breakup-adjacent songs). I can’t really relate to them, and I just don’t quite understand why people like listening to them. 

BUT THIS SONG CHANGED MY ******* BRAIN CHEMISTRY

I will never be the same', '2025-11-21T20:27:43Z'),
  (3247, 485, 4, 0, 'I really love this, but it just missed a vote. In a packed field, it wins the cool factor, but not the musical factor.', '2025-11-22T00:36:11Z'),
  (3248, 481, 4, 0, 'I feel like to win a vote from me, the saxophone needs to stand out more, whereas this is mostly a combination of horns. Still one of my all time fave songs. ', '2025-11-22T00:36:11Z'),
  (3249, 482, 4, 1, 'This is so smooth and delectable and tasty. 10/10 ', '2025-11-22T00:36:11Z'),
  (3250, 483, 4, 0, 'I have just never liked this song all that much, despite the great sax part ', '2025-11-22T00:36:11Z'),
  (3251, 484, 4, 0, 'Listening to this again, of course I was struck by how good the saxophone is. But I think the real stand out of the song is George Michael’s incredible voice. Also hard to not hear it as a meme.', '2025-11-22T00:36:11Z'),
  (3252, 472, 4, -1, 'This song is a banger, and I liked it a lot more than I thought I would. But I don’t think the saxophone is a major component of it . Probably the song where the saxophone does the least for the overall vibe. Hence my downvote. ', '2025-11-22T00:36:11Z'),
  (3253, 473, 4, 0, 'I have to be honest, I think this is a very weak John Coltrane pick. ', '2025-11-22T00:36:11Z'),
  (3254, 474, 4, 0, 'This is my favorite of the jazzy songs. Really good stuff and varied. I just feel like my votes were drawn more towards things that were not just saxophone alone.', '2025-11-22T00:36:11Z'),
  (3255, 475, 4, 0, 'This is my favorite of the instrumental picks. ', '2025-11-22T00:36:11Z'),
  (3256, 477, 4, 1, 'There’s something so perfect about sci-fi futurism and saxophone. You get it here and in the Cowboy Bebop song. They create such an incredible atmosphere.', '2025-11-22T00:36:11Z'),
  (3257, 478, 4, 0, 'Absolute banger in every way, and I’m tempted to vote for it simply because Sammy hated on it in the chat. Probably my next vote if I had one more to give. ', '2025-11-22T00:36:11Z'),
  (3258, 479, 4, 2, 'The Japanese are true craftsman. They take everything that we have created (jazz, baseball, automobile manufacturing, financial markets, imperialism) and become the true masters of them. Only they could have crafted one of the most perfect jazz songs of all time as the intro to a space mystery anime that was originally created to sell toys. ', '2025-11-22T00:36:11Z'),
  (3259, 480, 4, 0, 'I felt like the saxophone lick here is supplemental but not load bearing. It’s amazing, but is actually pretty marginal in the song. ', '2025-11-22T00:36:11Z'),
  (3260, 484, 13, 0, 'The most obvious pick for this category IMO.  But I don''t think it''s actually the best saxophone part.', '2025-11-22T15:56:36Z'),
  (3261, 480, 13, 0, 'Pretty great song, but sax part didn''t wow me.', '2025-11-22T15:56:36Z'),
  (3262, 481, 13, 1, 'I LOVE this song.  However, there''s nothing really standout about the saxophone part.  All the instruments are playing in unison.  Nonetheless, it has a cool enough unison sound to win a vote.', '2025-11-22T15:56:36Z'),
  (3263, 483, 13, 0, 'Almost submitted this one, but chose not to because there''s only one sax riff.  It''s cool and memorable.  But it''s just one riff over and over.  Wouldn''t call that the "best" saxophone part. "Iconic" but not "best"', '2025-11-22T15:56:36Z'),
  (3264, 485, 13, 0, 'Had high hopes for this one, but it just didn''t blow me away (sorry Eddie if you''re reading this).  I think I liked the piano part more, tbh.', '2025-11-22T15:56:36Z'),
  (3265, 472, 13, -1, 'I could barely hear the sax and I don''t really ', '2025-11-22T15:56:36Z'),
  (3266, 473, 13, 1, NULL, '2025-11-22T15:56:36Z'),
  (3267, 474, 13, 0, 'Accidentally seduced my wife when I played this in the car.', '2025-11-22T15:56:36Z'),
  (3268, 478, 13, 0, 'Licensed to make me ill.', '2025-11-22T15:56:36Z'),
  (3269, 479, 13, 2, 'Yessss.', '2025-11-22T15:56:36Z'),
  (3270, 483, 12, 1, 'I have fond memories of the song, it reminds me of looking at sports stats over a lazy summer.', '2025-11-22T20:57:32Z'),
  (3271, 479, 12, 1, NULL, '2025-11-22T20:57:32Z'),
  (3272, 478, 12, -1, 'I really, really didn''t want to do this, but I had to put it somewhere. If it''s any consolation, this was one of my favorite songs in middle school.', '2025-11-22T20:57:32Z'),
  (3273, 477, 12, 2, NULL, '2025-11-22T20:57:32Z'),
  (3274, 477, 11, 0, 'Didn’t make my top 4 but I really love this track', '2025-11-23T10:42:42Z'),
  (3275, 472, 11, 1, 'Great song, and the sax really enhances the poignant angsty vibes ', '2025-11-23T10:42:42Z'),
  (3276, 478, 11, 1, 'It’s a fun innovative use of sax in a different genre than you’d expect. Sorry chat, it’s a yes from me', '2025-11-23T10:42:42Z'),
  (3277, 479, 11, 0, 'The cut of this song they use in the title sequence doesn’t include the sax solo—I already loved this song but the first time I heard the full version I was blown away. One of the best tv show theme songs of all time', '2025-11-23T10:42:42Z'),
  (3278, 480, 11, 1, 'Again, here, the sax is a part of the storytelling', '2025-11-23T10:42:42Z'),
  (3279, 481, 11, 0, 'Didn’t make my top 4 but I love this song dearly. Hearing it always takes me back to freshman year of college dances. Respect to whoever submitted', '2025-11-23T10:42:42Z'),
  (3280, 482, 11, 1, 'The sax really complements and heightens the storytelling here', '2025-11-23T10:42:42Z'),
  (3281, 484, 11, -1, 'It’s an iconic sax part. I don’t know how it manages to capture such intense, campy angst. I love it for that reason. But it’s a iconic sax part, not a *great* sax part. ', '2025-11-23T10:42:42Z'),
