  (3440, 505, 3, 0, 'I am unable to receive what this song has to give', '2025-12-02T15:34:00Z'),
  (3441, 506, 3, 0, 'Amateurish. This guy needs to learn how to sing. And stop whining ', '2025-12-02T15:34:00Z'),
  (3442, 507, 3, 0, 'Beautiful song. Not sufficiently “it’s so over”', '2025-12-02T15:34:00Z'),
  (3443, 508, 3, 1, 'An awesome extended metaphor. The production and writing on this song are so cool and so far above what you’d expect for indie acoustic pop. Tons of interesting twists and turns, well done Lizzy (and Fiona)', '2025-12-02T15:34:00Z'),
  (3444, 509, 3, -1, 'Nails on chalkboard vocal phrasing', '2025-12-02T15:34:00Z'),
  (3445, 510, 3, 0, 'Not a fit for category', '2025-12-02T15:34:00Z'),
  (3446, 511, 3, 0, 'Obviously Erivo’s vocals are great, but this sounds like a song written by AI. There’s no flow to the melody despite some very bright moments', '2025-12-02T15:34:00Z'),
  (3447, 512, 3, 2, 'Gobsmacking. The intensity in the climax of this song is really incredible. Amazing read on the category, though it pains me to vote for my arch ML enemy, Brad', '2025-12-02T15:34:00Z'),
  (3448, 513, 3, 0, 'This lady is a Radiohead fan for sure. I questioned whether she was singing in English at a couple points though ', '2025-12-02T15:34:00Z'),
  (3449, 502, 15, 0, 'Surprised how much I enjoyed this one. ', '2025-12-03T22:42:43Z'),
  (3450, 504, 15, 1, 'Classic for a reason. ', '2025-12-03T22:42:43Z'),
  (3451, 506, 15, 0, 'Listening to this as I drive down the Pacific Coast Highway. It''s 70 degrees and sunny. I grin. A single word escapes my lips: ''schadenfreude''.', '2025-12-03T22:42:43Z'),
  (3452, 507, 15, 2, 'Oddly I never heard this before . Very pleasant surprise. I know it''s a normie song, but her singing is genuinely moving. ', '2025-12-03T22:42:43Z'),
  (3453, 508, 15, 0, 'Talented artist, but not a huge fan of the vocal style.', '2025-12-03T22:42:43Z'),
  (3454, 509, 15, 0, 'Was the song supposed to be funny? I thought it was funny. "I hope the junkyard burns down" is an amazing line.', '2025-12-03T22:42:43Z'),
  (3455, 510, 15, 1, 'Certainly didn''t expect to enjoy this, but I did. The background stuff is amazing.', '2025-12-03T22:42:43Z'),
  (3456, 511, 15, 0, 'Yet again, great talent that seems wasted to me. ', '2025-12-03T22:42:43Z'),
  (3457, 512, 15, 0, 'Enjoyable. Great theme.', '2025-12-03T22:42:43Z'),
