  (3518, 500, 2, -1, 'My criteria for this round is that to be truly a song about failure and despair, there’s gotta be no silver lining. This song has too much residual hope, as though too far along in the stages of grief. A little too upbeat, therapeutic, forward-looking', '2025-12-05T13:38:47Z'),
  (3519, 502, 2, 0, 'Really enjoyed this ', '2025-12-05T13:38:47Z'),
  (3520, 507, 2, 1, 'Beautiful', '2025-12-05T13:38:47Z'),
  (3521, 508, 2, 1, 'This is a great shout ', '2025-12-05T13:38:47Z'),
  (3522, 509, 2, 1, 'calculated Judd bait. John Darnielle has a voice perfectly calibrated for despair ', '2025-12-05T13:38:47Z'),
  (3523, 510, 2, 0, 'The chorus and the riff at 2:55 in this are excellent. But it’s not really giving “failure and despair” so much as just talking about the consequences of a life of dissipation ', '2025-12-05T13:38:47Z'),
  (3524, 511, 2, 0, 'The lyrics without the context from a movie I didn’t see make this much less resonant than other submissions ', '2025-12-05T13:38:47Z'),
  (3525, 512, 2, 1, 'This is the money. This is exactly the sort of thing I’m picturing when I think of a song about failure. Brad, I kneel', '2025-12-05T13:38:47Z'),
  (3526, 513, 2, 0, 'I really want to upvote Adrianne Lenker every time, but lyrically this song is almost too murky and vague to me. To really be a song about despair, it’s gotta sound like crying and screaming at the moon', '2025-12-05T13:38:47Z'),
