  (3620, 532, 3, 0, '🥈Blahhh. Hate the message but musically it’s basically ok. Not something that makes me want to crawl out of my skin. This doesn’t deserve second but there’s not much truly heinous on here I’m afraid', '2026-01-08T20:59:20Z'),
  (3621, 534, 3, 0, 'This is not a song I enjoy listening to, but that’s the whole point. It accomplishes its goal absolutely perfectly. I prefer more order with my dissonance, but there is a (limited) place for stuff like this. ', '2026-01-08T20:59:20Z'),
  (3622, 538, 3, 0, 'This is a well done pop song, memorable if quite basic, and brings back swimming carpool memories. No hate', '2026-01-08T20:59:20Z'),
  (3623, 536, 3, 0, 'Genres I don’t usually listen to != songs I hate. This is nice enough and the super strong accent makes it interesting. Would happily spin again', '2026-01-08T20:59:20Z'),
  (3624, 526, 3, 0, '🥉 Would be merely a blah pop song without the grating liberal platitudes thrown in. Still a somewhat fun concept, though irritating in execution. AJR somehow have a sound at once instantly identifiable and utterly generic. ', '2026-01-08T20:59:20Z'),
  (3625, 527, 3, 0, 'Richard came to ML to late to learn my appreciation of girl pop. There is (almost) nothing objectionable here', '2026-01-08T20:59:20Z'),
  (3626, 528, 3, 3, '🏆 The only submission (besides my own) that rises to the level of travesty. Degenerate, repetitive, utterly boring, and yet catchy enough to stay stuck in your head. I hate this kind of vapid major key rock and roll and this is an especially egregious example. ', '2026-01-08T20:59:20Z'),
  (3627, 529, 3, 0, 'This song is a great moral lesson in not being led by your passions and earns its length with meaningful development and storytelling interest. The baseball interlude is clever. Some moments are downright theatrical and the vocals are great. What’s to hate?', '2026-01-08T20:59:20Z'),
