  (4180, 613, 3, 1, 'Hard to argue. Also pretty good submission for next round', '2026-02-23T22:54:43Z'),
  (4181, 601, 4, 0, 'A classic and a good choice. Was not played, but also doesn''t rise to the top. ', '2026-02-24T16:25:18Z'),
  (4182, 611, 4, 0, 'No, but you have just identified the opening title scroll song for Wes Anderson''s "Friends in the Bend". Eddie, departing from Hangar shed, rides his road bike slowly through various South Bend locales. We pass Joe Torma, in the Club Blue backyard, minutely trimming leaves on the various plants flowering from Cynthia the aquatic tower garden. The rectory, a car on blocks. Top down angle over the car, one after another Chris, then Corey, then Judd, then George, then Teddy, then Gabe on rolling boards each pop their heads out from underneath. Along the riverwalk, Brad and Richard emerge in scuba gear with treasure chest in hand. The Fort, Sammy and Joseph moving furniture inside while Shea, Regina, and Fiona sip lemonade on the porch wearing oversized sunglasses. It writes itself. ', '2026-02-24T16:25:18Z'),
  (4183, 612, 4, 1, 'Richard will disagree, but the millennial contingent would have rocked with this', '2026-02-24T16:25:18Z'),
  (4184, 606, 4, 0, 'Banger, but too obvious', '2026-02-24T16:25:18Z'),
  (4185, 607, 4, 0, 'Seems a bit of a weird theme for a wedding song', '2026-02-24T16:25:18Z'),
  (4186, 608, 4, -1, 'This might be the worst song I have ever heard in my entire life', '2026-02-24T16:25:18Z'),
  (4187, 609, 4, 0, 'Cute but not in the way that gets a vote', '2026-02-24T16:25:18Z'),
  (4188, 610, 4, 2, 'This is deep Richard knowledge. And also I forgot how incredibly great this song is. I must reward. ', '2026-02-24T16:25:18Z'),
  (4189, 604, 4, 1, 'Given that there was a french pop song played that the entire Storey Family had a choreographed dance to, this fits in a weird way for me. ', '2026-02-24T16:25:18Z'),
  (4190, 603, 4, 0, 'Richard will hate me saying this, but it fits the theme and the general atmosphere that was cultivated.', '2026-02-24T16:25:18Z'),
  (4191, 602, 4, 0, 'This is such a banger, thank you Joseph for submitting. But no vote. ', '2026-02-24T16:25:18Z'),
  (4192, 613, 4, 0, 'A classic and would fit, but just outside the top for me', '2026-02-24T16:25:18Z'),
  (4193, 614, 4, 0, 'Meh - not for the category', '2026-02-24T16:25:18Z'),
  (4194, 608, 16, 0, 'This is the greatest song I’ve ever heard. ', '2026-02-25T01:25:27Z'),
  (4195, 601, 16, 0, 'Wrong. Terrible choice of a stupid song. ', '2026-02-25T01:25:27Z'),
  (4196, 602, 16, 0, 'How in the hell would you dance to this at a wedding reception?', '2026-02-25T01:25:27Z'),
  (4197, 603, 16, -1, 'Insulting. Do you take for your unmarried 60 year old aunt?!', '2026-02-25T01:25:27Z'),
  (4198, 604, 16, 1, 'Don’t know what this is, but I love it. ', '2026-02-25T01:25:27Z'),
