“Songs that people sing to babies that are morbid” is its own category within this lowkey ', '2026-03-05T19:24:09Z'),
  (4385, 630, 1, -1, 'Not really sad in the way I was looking for here. I think the music goes with the meaning.', '2026-03-05T19:24:09Z'),
  (4386, 631, 1, 0, 'There’s a version of this from The Voice Holland that she sings it sadly too. I recommend.', '2026-03-05T19:24:09Z'),
  (4387, 636, 1, 0, 'I liked this take but doesn’t seem sad enough ', '2026-03-05T19:24:09Z'),
  (4388, 638, 1, 1, 'I have heard this lmao I think mens choir did it in college and I didn’t know the context which is indeed sad. Me gusta the song.', '2026-03-05T19:24:09Z'),
  (4389, 639, 1, 0, 'I liked this angle but the song itself is sorta insufferable so I can’t vote for it from a musical standpoint ', '2026-03-05T19:24:09Z'),
  (4390, 627, 4, 0, 'To me this song sounds upbeat, but not happy. I have a lot of arbitrary conditions for this round, and you''re gonna have to deal with them. I think the vibe here makes it clear it''s not happy, truly. ', '2026-03-05T21:33:02Z'),
  (4391, 628, 4, 1, 'This is the only one of the ones I had heard where I had no idea it was a sad song. To be fair, that''s mostly because you can''t understand a single thing they''re saying. But, I would never have guessed for many reasons. It wins the vote easily. ', '2026-03-05T21:33:02Z'),
  (4392, 629, 4, 0, 'A great pick I just liked others more. I feel like people know this is sad but they forget anyway, which is a good hallmark for the round.  ', '2026-03-05T21:33:02Z'),
  (4393, 630, 4, 0, 'I love to hate and hate to love this song. It fits though, I can''t argue with that. ', '2026-03-05T21:33:02Z'),
  (4394, 631, 4, 1, 'The archetypal submission. I think this fits in a particular way because it''s self aware. Literally critiquing that you can make a beat so good people ignore the message, or, as they say "Y''all don''t want to hear me, you just wanna dance."', '2026-03-05T21:33:02Z'),
  (4395, 632, 4, 1, 'Perfect submission, stolen from me. Congrats Sammy. Truly one of the best songs of the 2010s. I used to listen to this on repeat in my dorm senior year. To me, this song is like Jimmy Johns. Sometimes you think you don''t want it, but then as soon as you take the first bite, you realize you were wrong. I have never listened to this without enjoying it. ', '2026-03-05T21:33:02Z'),
  (4396, 633, 4, 1, 'Again, a perfect song. Doesn''t get better than this. Should be in a time capsule of the 90s. Similar to Hey Ya, you can hear the whole thing, and never even think about the actual lyrics. ', '2026-03-05T21:33:02Z'),
  (4397, 634, 4, -1, 'This didn''t sound all that happy to me...', '2026-03-05T21:33:02Z'),
  (4398, 635, 4, 0, 'I have heard this song maybe 100+ times and it was only deep in my review for this round that it even hit me that it''s actually sad. Obvious on a re-listen, but I think that''s what makes it great. You don''t even care enough to notice, because it''s so happy-sounding. ', '2026-03-05T21:33:02Z'),
  (4399, 636, 4, 0, 'If you made this song today with the same "age gap" between it''s release and 1985, it would be about 2007. Inspired pick, just so very narrowly beat by Hey Ya for me.', '2026-03-05T21:33:02Z'),
  (4400, 637, 4, 0, 'I like the instrumentals in this, but otherwise didn''t speak to me', '2026-03-05T21:33:02Z');
INSERT INTO votes (id, submission_id, voter_id, points, comment, created_at) VALUES
  (4401, 638, 4, 0, 'I ain''t translating that. Banger though. 
There''s something deeper here though, similar to American slave songs.', '2026-03-05T21:33:02Z'),
  (4402, 639, 4, 0, 'This one is a bit too obvious. I like when the title doesn''t give it away. Did briefly consider submitting "Sell Out" tho. ', '2026-03-05T21:33:02Z'),
  (4403, 627, 11, 1, 'Listening to the lyrics closely this go around, I was struck by this one. It’s more bleak than I think I’d realized previously ', '2026-03-06T03:52:35Z'),
  (4404, 629, 11, 1, 'Yeah, okay, this one is a good fit', '2026-03-06T03:52:35Z'),
  (4405, 631, 11, 0, 'I feel like this is the obvious example of this category that everyone knows about, and therefore I have deemed it too obvious for a vote even though it’s a generational track ', '2026-03-06T03:52:35Z'),
  (4406, 632, 11, 1, 'Feels like an Eddie pick? This was perhaps the one this round I was most surprised by—that is, I really hadn’t ever listened to the lyrics carefully so I had no idea how sad it was', '2026-03-06T03:52:35Z'),
  (4407, 633, 11, 1, 'It’s just such a phenomenal fit for the category, not to mention an incredible song. Would’ve submitted it myself if I hadn’t been beaten to the punch. A part of me thinks that if this really is the same one everyone else wanted to submit, maybe it’s too obvious a choice. But it’s too perfect not to vote', '2026-03-06T03:52:35Z'),
  (4408, 636, 11, 0, 'I’ve loved this song for decades and tbh I’ve never actually found it super sad. I feel like it’s okay to be a little too fond of the movies and music of your youth. But I almost want to give it a vote just for the massive serotonin hit I got when it came on', '2026-03-06T03:52:35Z'),
  (4409, 637, 11, -1, 'Sorry, this just isn’t distinctly happy sounding enough imo. A couple chords in I was already pretty sure this was gonna be my downvote', '2026-03-06T03:52:35Z'),
  (4410, 628, 2, 0, 'Indeed I just assumed this song was about something happy and never paid any attention to the lyrics ', '2026-03-06T06:17:03Z'),
  (4411, 629, 2, 0, 'Does not sound happy (except maybe the chorus)', '2026-03-06T06:17:03Z'),
  (4412, 630, 2, 1, 'I almost skipped voting for this because it seems like perhaps the most obvious submission for the category (it was the first one I thought of but it was already swiped). But upon relisten I can’t resist voting, it really is perfect for this. Such an incredible bop and it’s funny because it doesn’t even try to disguise how agonized the lyrics are, it wears the discordance on its sleeve ', '2026-03-06T06:17:03Z'),
  (4413, 631, 2, 1, 'This is a brilliant submission. The very first listen sort of made me do a double take because I was confused what it was doing on this playlist, has to be rewarded.', '2026-03-06T06:17:03Z'),
  (4414, 632, 2, 0, 'Does not sound distinctly happy. However Eddie you never fail to remind me of totally forgotten songs I used to hear on Atlanta’s mid-2010s alternative rock radio station, and for that I thank you ', '2026-03-06T06:17:03Z'),
  (4415, 635, 2, 1, NULL, '2026-03-06T06:17:03Z'),
  (4416, 636, 2, -1, 'Up-tempo is not the same thing as sounding happy and this song actually sounds somewhat tortured ', '2026-03-06T06:17:03Z'),
