  (4770, 669, 2, -1, 'Basically inexplicable submission. Is there something I’m missing? 17 long minutes and the one part that has lyrics is extremely decipherable.', '2026-03-18T23:06:31Z'),
  (4771, 671, 2, 1, 'Pearl Jam/grunge in general is a great shout for this category. They all sound like this. ', '2026-03-18T23:06:31Z'),
  (4772, 672, 2, 0, 'Maybe I’ve known this song for too long but these lyrics are really familiar to me ', '2026-03-18T23:06:31Z'),
  (4773, 673, 2, 1, 'I am so delighted to see R.E.M. here. In addition to being a great song, this one and almost everything on their first EP and full record could work for this category. Michael Stipe had a magic skill for murky songwriting. I’ve known this song for probably 20 years and I still, to this day, do not know all the words. Never looked them up. Maybe never will. It’s like a beautiful piece of just-barely-discernible nonsense that I can happily mumble along to. ', '2026-03-18T23:06:31Z'),
  (4774, 674, 2, 0, 'Would have been a great pick for Scary Songs if we had done that round. This is horrible', '2026-03-18T23:06:31Z'),
  (4775, 675, 2, 1, 'I liked this. Sort of classic “he’s not trying to sound indecipherable, it just is”', '2026-03-18T23:06:31Z'),
  (4776, 676, 2, 1, 'Not a dang word (well except “serenity”)', '2026-03-18T23:06:31Z'),
  (4777, 678, 2, 0, 'Ehhh this is pretty decipherable', '2026-03-18T23:06:31Z'),
