  (4786, 680, 15, 0, 'A creative interpretation of the category. I just dislike the song. ', '2026-03-21T21:39:50Z'),
  (4787, 681, 15, 0, 'Fun.', '2026-03-21T21:39:50Z'),
  (4788, 682, 15, 1, 'Very folksy, Americana, yet authentic. Dig it.', '2026-03-21T21:39:50Z'),
  (4789, 683, 15, 0, 'This reminds me that I need to listen to more Tchaikovsky. Very beautiful. Unfortunately there were many other strong contenders.', '2026-03-21T21:39:50Z'),
  (4790, 684, 15, 2, 'Fantastic. ', '2026-03-21T21:39:50Z'),
  (4791, 685, 15, 0, 'I''m not sure if the guy who wrote this has ever died.', '2026-03-21T21:39:50Z'),
  (4792, 686, 15, 0, 'I wanted to give this a vote just to make Brad mad. ', '2026-03-21T21:39:50Z'),
  (4793, 688, 15, 1, 'The goods.', '2026-03-21T21:39:50Z'),
  (4794, 690, 15, 0, 'If I had five votes, this would get one.', '2026-03-21T21:39:50Z'),
  (4795, 692, 15, -1, 'Dislike the style.', '2026-03-21T21:39:50Z'),
  (4796, 685, 13, 0, 'I was jammin to this one.  Not sure if it''s the best song to die to, though.', '2026-03-21T22:15:55Z'),
  (4797, 680, 13, 0, 'I get what this is going for (entering into the beatific vision), but I don''t really think it works.', '2026-03-21T22:15:55Z'),
  (4798, 683, 13, 1, 'Beautifully selected.', '2026-03-21T22:15:55Z'),
  (4799, 684, 13, 1, 'Man, this is also a really beautiful song.', '2026-03-21T22:15:55Z'),
  (4800, 686, 13, 0, 'Songs NOT to die to.  The song is undeniably a bop though.', '2026-03-21T22:15:55Z');
INSERT INTO votes (id, submission_id, voter_id, points, comment, created_at) VALUES
  (4801, 688, 13, 1, 'Another O Brother song, eh? (Mine played during the credits, I believe).  A great movie to meditate on death.

But this song speaks: death is not something someone else can do for you; you''ve got to go through it yourself (and hopefully in right relationship with the Lord).  And for that reason I find it really appropriate.', '2026-03-21T22:15:55Z'),
  (4802, 689, 13, -1, 'This was the least compelling of the list.  It wasn''t a bad song, but I just didn''t see it.', '2026-03-21T22:15:55Z'),
  (4803, 692, 13, 1, 'I see it. Well picked.', '2026-03-21T22:15:55Z'),
  (4804, 688, 9, 2, NULL, '2026-03-22T02:08:29Z'),
  (4805, 690, 9, 1, NULL, '2026-03-22T02:08:29Z'),
  (4806, 680, 9, -1, NULL, '2026-03-22T02:08:29Z'),
  (4807, 682, 9, 1, NULL, '2026-03-22T02:08:29Z'),
  (4808, 680, 5, -1, NULL, '2026-03-22T02:33:57Z'),
  (4809, 692, 5, 1, 'WAS LITERALLY GOING TO SUBMIT THIS haha! So crazy. Great pick!!', '2026-03-22T02:33:57Z'),
  (4810, 681, 5, 1, 'I love this song ❤️', '2026-03-22T02:33:57Z'),
  (4811, 684, 5, 2, 'A perfect submission. Wow. 100/10.', '2026-03-22T02:33:57Z'),
  (4812, 691, 3, 0, 'I see the vision', '2026-03-22T03:05:01Z'),
  (4813, 692, 3, 0, 'No', '2026-03-22T03:05:01Z'),
  (4814, 680, 3, -1, 'Bizarre choice. No gravitas', '2026-03-22T03:05:01Z'),
  (4815, 681, 3, 0, 'Songs about death != songs to die to', '2026-03-22T03:05:01Z'),
  (4816, 682, 3, 2, 'Would harmonize to this with my dying breath', '2026-03-22T03:05:01Z'),
  (4817, 684, 3, 0, 'Trying way too hard', '2026-03-22T03:05:01Z'),
  (4818, 686, 3, 1, 'Theme didn’t say anything about “songs you ought to die to”', '2026-03-22T03:05:01Z'),
  (4819, 688, 3, 1, 'Just a little on the nose, but this is so good', '2026-03-22T03:05:01Z'),
  (4820, 690, 3, 0, 'I’d fall asleep before dying listening to this ', '2026-03-22T03:05:01Z'),
  (4821, 682, 2, 1, 'A++. My favorite submission on the list. Instantly painted a picture as soon as that opening chord progression started. ', '2026-03-22T03:05:37Z'),
  (4822, 680, 2, 1, 'I am not certain I quite see the vision but I cannot downvote a brave and unexpected submission like this. And in a playlist I thought was a little on the weak side, I want to reward a really novel read of the category ', '2026-03-22T03:05:37Z'),
  (4823, 681, 2, 1, 'I love this song and this band. This is a cool read ', '2026-03-22T03:05:37Z'),
  (4824, 684, 2, -1, 'I did not enjoy this version at all. And being from the 1917 soundtrack, I can only assume someone has in fact already died to this song', '2026-03-22T03:05:37Z'),
  (4825, 685, 2, 1, 'Listening to this in the car with Joseph en route to Dangriga, Belize and it is funny how instantly our opinions on it diverged. I loved this though. It’s a little too long but I can imagine the whole song isn’t going to play during the death scene. The opening and the overall vibe of the song is perfect for this. Quite enjoyed ', '2026-03-22T03:05:37Z'),
  (4826, 688, 2, 0, 'This is a great song but I don’t feel compelled to upvote submissions that are this overtly about death ', '2026-03-22T03:05:37Z'),
  (4827, 690, 2, 0, 'I found this very boring', '2026-03-22T03:05:37Z'),
  (4828, 691, 2, 0, 'I was amused to see this here. I can see it as a death song but it’s just not particularly interesting ', '2026-03-22T03:05:37Z'),
  (4829, 692, 2, 0, 'An absolutely phenomenal song but did not land for me in this category. I can kind of imagine it conceptually as a death song but it doesn’t sound like that would actually play during a death scene ', '2026-03-22T03:05:37Z'),
  (4830, 680, 11, 1, 'I feel like this would be a good song to die to in a similar way to mmmbop. The lyrics aren’t as obviously existential but the bright upbeat melody would give a nice touch of irony', '2026-03-22T05:48:52Z'),
  (4831, 683, 11, 1, 'Epic. Never thought of this as a death song before but I see the vision', '2026-03-22T05:48:52Z'),
  (4832, 684, 11, 0, 'Feels more “memento mori” than “songs to die to” for me', '2026-03-22T05:48:52Z'),
  (4833, 685, 11, 0, 'I kinda sorta see the vision but only kinda sorta?', '2026-03-22T05:48:52Z'),
  (4834, 686, 11, 0, 'Brad ragebait? This could for sure work as a death song, but like, for a villain or mafia boss?', '2026-03-22T05:48:52Z'),
  (4835, 687, 11, 1, 'This is the vibe. 10/10 would die to this', '2026-03-22T05:48:52Z'),
  (4836, 688, 11, 0, 'This works so perfectly in the movie scene but I feel like that’s largely because it fits the movie’s particular genre and tone and it’s hard for me to see it working in a more general way. Memento mori for sure but I don’t feel like the song screams “soundtrack for death” outside the context of the movie', '2026-03-22T05:48:52Z'),
  (4837, 689, 11, 1, 'Bracketing the association with tiktok that this song has in my mind, it’s a cool song and a cool read for the category  ', '2026-03-22T05:48:52Z'),
  (4838, 692, 11, -1, 'I love this song but despite the fact that the word “die” is in the song, it doesn’t feel like a dying vibe lyrically or musically for me. Maybe I’m just not getting something', '2026-03-22T05:48:52Z'),
  (4839, 681, 10, -1, NULL, '2026-03-22T17:50:15Z'),
  (4840, 682, 10, 1, 'Tried submitting this but this person already did, good choice.', '2026-03-22T17:50:15Z'),
  (4841, 684, 10, 1, NULL, '2026-03-22T17:50:15Z'),
  (4842, 686, 10, 1, NULL, '2026-03-22T17:50:15Z'),
  (4843, 692, 10, 1, NULL, '2026-03-22T17:50:15Z'),
  (4844, 680, 1, -1, NULL, '2026-03-22T21:41:54Z'),
  (4845, 683, 1, 0, 'That sort of moment transcends words to me ', '2026-03-22T21:41:54Z'),
  (4846, 684, 1, 1, NULL, '2026-03-22T21:41:54Z'),
  (4847, 686, 1, 0, 'Second downvote would be here ', '2026-03-22T21:41:54Z'),
  (4848, 688, 1, 1, NULL, '2026-03-22T21:41:54Z'),
  (4849, 689, 1, 2, NULL, '2026-03-22T21:41:54Z'),
  (4850, 691, 1, 0, 'Not quite it for me but movie themes are indeed my taste for this category ', '2026-03-22T21:41:54Z'),
  (4851, 692, 1, 0, 'I love the avett bros but I think they fall into the category of things that make me ponder important things vs a song I’d literally choose to be listening to as I pass from this life to the next.', '2026-03-22T21:41:54Z'),
  (4852, 680, 16, -1, 'Are you kidding? Ya know what would happen if you tried dying to this song? Your heartbeat would rise, your foot would start tapping, you’d starting singing along in and you’d finish bleed ingout before hearing the word sunshine. You’ve clearing never died before', '2026-03-23T16:56:19Z'),
  (4853, 684, 16, 3, NULL, '2026-03-23T16:56:19Z'),
  (4854, 686, 16, 1, NULL, '2026-03-23T16:56:19Z'),
  (4855, 680, 4, -1, 'Funniest submission to think about in terms of Sammy''s scenario described in the chat. Sadly it''s the least on point for theme imo. ', '2026-03-23T17:05:32Z'),
  (4856, 681, 4, 0, 'This is a beautiful reflective piece but for that reason I think it''s not the one I''d want to die to. I don''t want to be melancholic reflective. But joyful reflective. I guess this could be either, but doesn''t get a vote. ', '2026-03-23T17:05:32Z'),
  (4857, 682, 4, 0, 'Good submission but do', '2026-03-23T17:05:32Z'),
  (4858, 683, 4, 1, 'I have a deep affinity and nostalgia for the Nutcracker, having seen it so many times and been in it once. I listen to it around Christmas each year. This is something that would make me feel right if the end was nigh. ', '2026-03-23T17:05:32Z'),
  (4859, 684, 4, 1, 'I wanted to dislike this scene when it started in 1917 because it felt so out of place and sudden, but then it was so beautiful that I think they wanted it to pull you entirely out of the movie and reflect on the absurdity of it all before you''re just plunged back into the chaos and nonsense. ', '2026-03-23T17:05:32Z'),
  (4860, 685, 4, 0, 'Dozens of loving family members pressing close in......granddaughter leans in....
"Papa....what do you want to hear....one last time?"
"Please....just one more time.......play me some.....Kurt Vile and the Violators"', '2026-03-23T17:05:32Z'),
  (4861, 686, 4, 1, 'I know it''s fun and trendy to point out the individualistic read of this song, but that''s not the only read of it imo. I do think there''s a very real sense in it of the pride of feeling you''ve done what you could and you did it in a way you can look back on without shame, etc. I think this is a fine choice. ', '2026-03-23T17:05:32Z'),
  (4862, 687, 4, 0, 'This is the song Judd would request before Sammy''s scenario plays out', '2026-03-23T17:05:32Z'),
  (4863, 688, 4, 0, 'Good for a movie scene (like the movie scene it''s from) but I read this theme as songs I would die to, and this doesn''t seem very comforting lol ', '2026-03-23T17:05:32Z'),
  (4864, 689, 4, 1, 'Peaceful, beautiful, reflective, transcendent ', '2026-03-23T17:05:32Z'),
  (4865, 690, 4, 0, 'Dead Man''s Gun from RDR1 would be my choice in this genre. A great pick, but for my read of theme I am primarily rewarding songs I would want playing. ', '2026-03-23T17:05:32Z'),
  (4866, 691, 4, 0, 'Has been my pick for 10+ years and I stand by it', '2026-03-23T17:05:32Z'),
  (4867, 692, 4, 0, 'I see the vision but it doesn''t compel me. I can see how it would tho. ', '2026-03-23T17:05:32Z'),
