  (4947, 704, 1, 0, 'Lyrically this is good; Franciscan and faith filled which is not particular to Shea but I can see this touching her and her liking the repetition at the end. Ultimately not strong enough in this lineup.', '2026-04-20T21:59:02Z'),
  (4948, 705, 1, 0, 'Moses vibes? Wasn''t feeling this overall', '2026-04-20T21:59:02Z'),
  (4949, 706, 1, 0, 'Musically this is a cute one but idk if she would find the lyrics impressive enough with this competition', '2026-04-20T21:59:02Z'),
  (4950, 707, 1, -1, 'There are a couple I think she may have heard before but this seems like the one that is most commonly known and least likely to be her submission. And I find it the laziest submission for that reason (Darcy''s Donkey was also on my chopping block I will say)', '2026-04-20T21:59:02Z'),
  (4951, 708, 1, 1, 'Can defs see her liking this and praying with it, especially the twist (it''s not a race. you''re free!). And I find it pleasant melodically. This is a more surface level/stereotypical Shea category but an intentional pick within that.', '2026-04-20T21:59:02Z'),
  (4952, 709, 1, 0, 'This is fun but I find it more like a song everyone in the chat would find fun and amusing vs Shea specifically', '2026-04-20T21:59:02Z'),
  (4953, 710, 1, 0, 'This is vocally a Lizzy lookalike or maybe Phoebe Bridgers. This song is cool and I am interested to hear what Shea thinks', '2026-04-20T21:59:02Z'),
  (4954, 711, 1, 2, 'Assuming she doesn''t already know this, this is both musically and lyrically perf. (Shea is this u??)', '2026-04-20T21:59:02Z'),
  (4955, 712, 1, 0, 'Not hitting me as a Shea vibe enough for a vote, but I like the voice and instrumental. I think I will check this guy out!', '2026-04-20T21:59:02Z'),
  (4956, 713, 1, 0, 'This is cool but it isn''t strong enough in this batch', '2026-04-20T21:59:02Z'),
  (4957, 714, 1, 0, 'I think she probably already knows this but I do think this is a good ZB pick for Shea. I don''t think it''s her submission though. I think ZB is adjacent of "Shea would love" territory.', '2026-04-20T21:59:02Z'),
  (4958, 715, 1, 0, 'idk if y''all knew of Shea''s love for NY. She also likes S&G. This live version is so special.

Also I just have to say, my aunt Lorraine was at this concert (possibly also my Uncle Henry and Aunt Rosemary).', '2026-04-20T21:59:02Z'),
  (4959, 716, 1, 1, 'Shea and I were both praying and talking about fragrance during Holy Week <3

She may know this or this may be her? Or maybe neither. But I think she would like this.', '2026-04-20T21:59:02Z'),
  (4960, 705, 8, 3, 'This got me at 6:15AM on the way to work--why would you do this to me, Peter? This is such a good album, Alison Krauss is one of the best to ever do it.', '2026-04-20T22:25:44Z'),
  (4961, 704, 8, 1, 'Man I really loved this one. Of the explicitly religious songs, this is the best
', '2026-04-20T22:25:44Z'),
  (4962, 706, 8, 0, 'Get a new artist besides the same 5 mid string bands you post, Alex ', '2026-04-20T22:25:44Z'),
  (4963, 707, 8, 0, 'Shea strikes me as a Napoleon Dynamite enjoyer, Eddie, so she''s probably heard this before.', '2026-04-20T22:25:44Z'),
  (4964, 708, 8, 0, 'Sorry, Fiona, not gonna cut it. Ironic: you have longed for this round more than most, yet you post dreck in main. Do better.', '2026-04-20T22:25:44Z'),
