  (5137, 738, 1, 0, 'Good one -- I wish someone had submitted Teenage Dirtbag haha, but maybe this is better than that would have been (too redemptive of an ending)', '2026-05-04T20:27:32Z'),
  (5138, 739, 1, 0, 'This was lacking for me, hard as it is to say. It was almost too on the nose but also not on the nose enough? Not as authentic as some?', '2026-05-04T20:27:32Z'),
  (5139, 740, 1, -1, 'Needed this to just end sooner.', '2026-05-04T20:27:32Z'),
  (5140, 735, 1, 1, 'Great one -- this was on my maybe playlist', '2026-05-04T20:27:32Z'),
  (5141, 734, 1, 0, 'As soon as I thought of this I felt I had to submit.
This was probably the first Weird Al song I ever heard.', '2026-05-04T20:27:32Z'),
  (5142, 733, 1, 0, 'This was really close for me but I tried to see past the sentimental familiarity with the sound and found others to be stronger ', '2026-05-04T20:27:32Z'),
  (5143, 732, 1, 1, 'Ah this was very good. ', '2026-05-04T20:27:32Z'),
  (5144, 731, 1, 1, 'This smacks of Eddie? Maybe. I like this take, matches the bindle/steinbeck aesthetic well in its music and lyrics.', '2026-05-04T20:27:32Z'),
  (5145, 730, 1, 0, 'I like this read. I have never read these lyrics before; wow. 

Well done, Sammy. I''m p sure I have never not voted for an LotR submission; it is just such an all-time soundtrack. However, it was displaced from my podium by a couple of songs that matched the aesthetic better which I suppose I decided was a priority for me, clever as this may have been.', '2026-05-04T20:27:32Z'),
  (5146, 729, 1, 0, 'the aesthetic is definitely there but lyrically, others were stronger to me', '2026-05-04T20:27:32Z'),
  (5147, 737, 15, -1, 'They sounded like they were about to break into "One night in Bangkok", but never did. ', '2026-05-05T00:13:21Z'),
  (5148, 729, 15, 1, 'Very enjoyable ', '2026-05-05T00:13:21Z'),
  (5149, 730, 15, 0, 'Anything sung in persona Gollum must be sung by a whiny teenage boy. Having it sung by a skilled woman just doesn''t work. ', '2026-05-05T00:13:21Z'),
  (5150, 731, 15, 2, 'This is the background music for a film in which Eddie, Judd and the ghost of Bobby Kennedy take a road trip to find the soul of America. ', '2026-05-05T00:13:21Z'),
  (5151, 732, 15, 0, 'I love Janis Joplin, but her version of the song does not cohere. The original is better. ', '2026-05-05T00:13:21Z'),
  (5152, 733, 15, 1, 'Don''t know if this fits the theme, but it''s the best song on the list ', '2026-05-05T00:13:21Z'),
  (5153, 739, 15, 0, '2-3 minutes of this would have been great. 8 is brutal. No justification for the length. ', '2026-05-05T00:13:21Z'),
  (5154, 740, 15, 0, 'The band name makes me think of the supplicia canum (unfortunately, the listeners are the dogs in this scenario). ', '2026-05-05T00:13:21Z'),
  (5155, 734, 11, 1, 'Okay this one is actually quite fitting imo', '2026-05-05T02:38:48Z'),
  (5156, 737, 11, 1, 'The image of just standing bc you sold your chair is very bindlecore', '2026-05-05T02:38:48Z'),
  (5157, 738, 11, 0, 'A generational track and definitely partakes of bindlecore but not as much as other submissions', '2026-05-05T02:38:48Z'),
  (5158, 739, 11, -1, '1. I need to read the grapes of wrath. 
2. This song is cool. Epic guitar at the end
3. I feel, however, like this doesn’t quite fit with bindlecore as I understand it bc the misfortune it talks about seems caused by a system that is beyond our control rather than being in some way caused by oneself ', '2026-05-05T02:38:48Z'),
  (5159, 740, 11, 0, 'This definitely feels angsty but not necessarily in a bindle specific way (I guess it does talk about running away, and bindles are used when you’re running away from home ig, but that’s taking bindle in the literal sense)', '2026-05-05T02:38:48Z'),
  (5160, 731, 11, 0, 'Kankakee mentioned?!?

But I’m not sure I see how this fits the theme ', '2026-05-05T02:38:48Z'),
  (5161, 730, 11, 0, 'Maybe this is a heretical take but I don’t actually like this song very much. And it’s almost too genuinely despairing to fit the theme imo', '2026-05-05T02:38:48Z'),
  (5162, 732, 11, 1, 'I feel like the wistful sadness of this song isn’t quite the same as the pathos that the bindle has come to signify. It gets a vote, however because 1) for some reason I’m being really picky in my judgment of this round and 2) it actually mentions a bindle', '2026-05-05T02:38:48Z'),
  (5163, 733, 11, 1, 'I like this pull a lot. Never would’ve thought of it for this round but I think it’s an earnest portrayal of the sort of emotion that the bindle captures in a more comical way', '2026-05-05T02:38:48Z'),
  (5164, 736, 16, -1, NULL, '2026-05-06T01:32:27Z'),
  (5165, 734, 16, 4, NULL, '2026-05-06T01:32:27Z'),
  (5166, 729, 3, 1, 'This feels spiritually bindle', '2026-05-06T02:25:46Z'),
  (5167, 731, 3, -1, 'Not really bad or anything just didn’t seem strong for the category ', '2026-05-06T02:25:46Z'),
  (5168, 730, 3, 0, 'Ha. Amusing read but not quite', '2026-05-06T02:25:46Z'),
  (5169, 737, 3, 0, 'Tiresome', '2026-05-06T02:25:46Z'),
  (5170, 736, 3, 1, '10/10 brilliant submission. Any instrumental submission has to work extra hard to grab my attention and vote, and this knocked it out of the park', '2026-05-06T02:25:46Z'),
  (5171, 735, 3, 1, 'Banger', '2026-05-06T02:25:46Z'),
  (5172, 734, 3, 1, 'Any parody song is working uphill for me, so I have to upvote this because I did laugh out loud and it is indeed very bindle, especially the bit about dating his cousin', '2026-05-06T02:25:46Z'),
  (5173, 733, 13, 0, 'This is Billy Joel''s favorite song that he wrote', '2026-05-06T02:44:21Z'),
  (5174, 732, 13, 0, 'Needs to be more than just a regret song IMO.  Where''s the self-sabotage?', '2026-05-06T02:44:21Z'),
  (5175, 731, 13, 1, 'Superb take on this playlist.  Train bros unite.', '2026-05-06T02:44:21Z'),
  (5176, 730, 13, 0, '2q2www', '2026-05-06T02:44:21Z'),
  (5177, 739, 13, -1, 'This was the furthest from bindledom of the songs on the list.', '2026-05-06T02:44:21Z'),
  (5178, 738, 13, 1, 'Yep.', '2026-05-06T02:44:21Z'),
  (5179, 737, 13, 1, 'Bindledom has a bit of a comic edge to it and this captures that.', '2026-05-06T02:44:21Z'),
