  (5259, 744, 15, 0, 'He does kind of sound like a shake I guess', '2026-05-11T22:06:36Z'),
  (5260, 745, 15, 0, 'I like what this is going for. Here''s the problem: "On the Whiteness of the Whale", specifically the footnote on the albatross, is some of the finest prose ever. Needless to say, the lyrics to this song pale by comparison. ', '2026-05-11T22:06:36Z'),
  (5261, 746, 15, 0, '3 minute of this would be great. 5 minutes tolerable. 8 minutes is cruel and unusual ', '2026-05-11T22:06:36Z'),
  (5262, 747, 15, 3, 'A true classic. Stan Rogers has a beautiful voice and his lyrics are unique. Who else could make such a bittersweet song about economic decline (which does benefit the whales)? For that matter who else sings about economic decline and whales in the same song?', '2026-05-11T22:06:36Z'),
  (5263, 748, 15, 0, 'Hilarious Joseph bait ', '2026-05-11T22:06:36Z'),
  (5264, 751, 15, 0, 'Beautifully sung, but has about as much subtlety as a dynamited whale. I get that it''s trying to make a point (and for what it''s worth, I agree with it), but it feels like they thought the listener was dumb and or heartless and incapable of inference. ', '2026-05-11T22:06:36Z'),
  (5265, 752, 15, 1, NULL, '2026-05-11T22:06:36Z'),
  (5266, 741, 11, 0, 'Takes me back to watching the veggie tales Jonah movie on the dvd player in our 2007 Honda odyssey', '2026-05-11T23:08:03Z'),
