  (5466, 779, 1, 0, '🫠 I mean yeah ', '2026-05-27T03:29:02Z'),
  (5467, 782, 1, 1, NULL, '2026-05-27T03:29:02Z'),
  (5468, 778, 1, -1, 'I’ve never thought of this that way and I still don’t', '2026-05-27T03:29:02Z'),
  (5469, 777, 1, 0, 'This was a similar vibe to my submission but a less iconic song. It felt a bit like they could have cut a minute and a half from the middle and been better for it', '2026-05-27T03:29:02Z'),
  (5470, 786, 1, 1, NULL, '2026-05-27T03:29:02Z'),
  (5471, 785, 1, 2, 'A bop', '2026-05-27T03:29:02Z'),
  (5472, 785, 4, 0, 'This is not a bad pick I just didn''t like it as much. ', '2026-05-27T17:37:55Z'),
  (5473, 786, 4, 1, 'Perfect choice going with the Live Lounge version. ', '2026-05-27T17:37:55Z'),
  (5474, 784, 4, 0, 'Idk this one seems pretty white to me. ', '2026-05-27T17:37:55Z'),
  (5475, 783, 4, 0, 'I know I''m typecast as the Tom Waits submitter, but I had heard this song like 10 times and had no idea it was Tom Waits. I thought it was a black bluesman, until it came on shuffle on "Tom Waits Essentials" a while back. ', '2026-05-27T17:37:55Z'),
  (5476, 782, 4, 1, 'I like it. I think it fits musically, vocally, and stylistically. I think this is one of the more unique picks so I''m peeling a vote away from others for it. ', '2026-05-27T17:37:55Z'),
  (5477, 781, 4, 0, 'In many ways yes, but also no. So many Led Zeppelin songs are just them wanting to be black blues musicians. I think this one is not the best example of this imo. ', '2026-05-27T17:37:55Z'),
  (5478, 780, 4, 0, 'I really liked this, similar answer to Boz Scaggs though, I decided to just give one vote for this "style" and it went to Bobby Caldwell', '2026-05-27T17:37:55Z'),
  (5479, 779, 4, 0, 'I will leave as my comment one of the comments from the YouTube version I watched:

"i love the song but why is their only white people. Like a damn bowl of UNFLAVORED rice! Bland. Lol they tried though."', '2026-05-27T17:37:55Z'),
  (5480, 778, 4, -1, 'Sounds black is NOT the same as black music. 
This song is SO WHITE', '2026-05-27T17:37:55Z'),
  (5481, 777, 4, 0, 'Absolute bop. In the neck and neck race between this, "A Love of Your Own", and "What You Won''t Do for Love" for soulful 70s style, I have to say this one falls slightly behind. Boz Scaggs sounds black and his music is deeply influenced for sure, but his melodies are pure 70s white guy yacht rock. ', '2026-05-27T17:37:55Z'),
  (5482, 788, 4, 1, 'This is the best submission imo. Never in a million years would I have thought this was a white dude. Listening again now, I can see it. But he really got me tricked. Iconic song too. ', '2026-05-27T17:37:55Z'),
  (5483, 787, 4, 1, 'WOW this is so phenomenally good. I''ve heard this before and definitely thought it was a black guy. It also musically has some stylistic components that I think match that assumption better than the other 70s/smooth/soul entries. Perfect choice imo.  ', '2026-05-27T17:37:55Z'),
  (5484, 786, 3, 1, 'Phenomenal submission because it’s a song we all know that I would never have thought of for this. Nice', '2026-05-28T22:32:29Z'),
  (5485, 778, 3, 0, 'Not the strongest contender', '2026-05-28T22:32:29Z'),
  (5486, 779, 3, 0, 'Clever read', '2026-05-28T22:32:29Z'),
  (5487, 780, 3, 1, 'Clearly self conscious but man this is so tasty', '2026-05-28T22:32:29Z'),
  (5488, 782, 3, 1, 'I didn’t know white people were allowed to do this ', '2026-05-28T22:32:29Z'),
  (5489, 783, 3, 1, 'Very cool interpretation in style, delivery, and lyrical substance ', '2026-05-28T22:32:29Z'),
  (5490, 784, 3, 0, 'Is it just me or do they just not do rap with this much attitude anymore? I say this as someone who never listens to rap ', '2026-05-28T22:32:29Z'),
  (5491, 785, 3, 0, 'This is a premium Belize-era Judd submission. The kind of submission that makes me go to the artist profile to double check', '2026-05-28T22:32:29Z'),
  (5492, 787, 3, 0, 'Wish I had more upvotes ', '2026-05-28T22:32:29Z'),
  (5493, 788, 3, -1, 'Not even the tiniest part of me questioned whether this was a white person', '2026-05-28T22:32:29Z'),
  (5494, 778, 11, -1, 'Apparently some people think he sounds black but tbh I don’t really get that, unless you think white people can’t have deep voices. In any case, as mentioned above, “wait that’s a white guy?” isn’t exactly the same thing as “white people doing black people music.” As for the latter category, I guess he has folk and blues influences, but tbh it still reads more as 2014 millennial slop to me than anything else', '2026-05-28T23:30:02Z'),
  (5495, 779, 11, 1, 'I think there are better picks from this subgenre (ie folk choir esque attempts at African music) but the choice of this subgenre is inspired. Kicking myself that I didn’t think of it. ', '2026-05-28T23:30:02Z'),
  (5496, 780, 11, 1, 'Hell yeah', '2026-05-28T23:30:02Z'),
  (5497, 784, 11, 0, 'I love Eminem but imma be honest, it doesn’t feel like he’s doing “black people music” unless by that you just mean “rap”. But the line “a minimal swap to cop millions of Pac listeners” is right on theme and saved this from my downvote', '2026-05-28T23:30:02Z'),
  (5498, 785, 11, 0, 'I like this pull genre wise but the song itself felt aggressively meh ', '2026-05-28T23:30:02Z'),
  (5499, 787, 11, 1, 'Thought about submitting this one. Some have said that “wait that’s a white guy?!?” =/= “white people doing black people music” and while it’s true that those are two distinct categories, I think this song fits both', '2026-05-28T23:30:02Z'),
  (5500, 788, 11, 0, 'Mike Shinoda I love you but your music still feels extremely white  ', '2026-05-28T23:30:02Z');
