  (5565, 791, 11, 1, 'Maybe this wouldn’t have affected me as much a year ago but the wistfulness and melancholy in this one really worked. I miss being on the porch with you guys ', '2026-07-17T04:50:01Z'),
  (5566, 792, 11, 1, 'Damn. Teared up a little', '2026-07-17T04:50:01Z'),
  (5567, 793, 11, 0, 'Obviously good vibe but weirdly almost feels too upbeat for this specific purpose ', '2026-07-17T04:50:01Z'),
  (5568, 794, 11, 1, 'This isn’t to necessarily say that Alex submitted this, but this is a song Alex would queue during this porch sit ', '2026-07-17T04:50:01Z'),
  (5569, 795, 11, 0, 'Experimental indeed', '2026-07-17T04:50:01Z'),
  (5570, 789, 11, -1, 'Feels like it goes on just a tad too long to work in this context (ik the Dylan is longer but it’s longer in an ambient way that works better somehow)', '2026-07-17T04:50:01Z'),
  (5571, 790, 11, 1, 'His voice in this annoys me and yet it feels fitting for the porch sit', '2026-07-17T04:50:01Z'),
  (5572, 792, 2, 1, 'Practically half this album works as a Hangar Porch Sit soundtrack. Daylight Fading was a previous submission (my submission, in fact) but this one works just as well and I’ll choose not to penalize a song from the same album since I think it works so well. ', '2026-07-17T20:06:08Z'),
  (5573, 794, 2, 1, 'This feels very Hangarite. ', '2026-07-17T20:06:08Z'),
  (5574, 795, 2, 0, 'I did not really enjoy this personally and I’m not sure I could envision hearing it at a porch sit. But it’s an out of the box submission, not obvious, downvoting feels too cruel. I am ambivalent ', '2026-07-17T20:06:08Z'),
  (5575, 796, 2, 1, 'Sammycore submission in the best way. Would 100% down a Fat Tire and watch the dying embers of a July sun to the strains of “I hear you singing in the wire…”', '2026-07-17T20:06:08Z'),
  (5576, 798, 2, 1, 'It’s not a slam dunk but it’s such a great song, just recently discovered it (overheard playing in a Belizean coffee shop) and immediately liked it. I’m feeling generous', '2026-07-17T20:06:08Z'),
  (5577, 789, 2, 0, 'One of my all time favorite songs, but I don’t think it really fits the vibe of a porch sit. Maybe if I have the aux, but if I have the aux is it really doing justice to the porch sit?', '2026-07-17T20:06:08Z'),
  (5578, 793, 2, -1, 'Steely Dan feels like low hanging fruit, and this song even moreso. I even think there’s much better Steely Dan submissions for the category. ', '2026-07-17T20:06:08Z'),
