  (5675, 809, 11, 0, 'Feels more like “unintentionally about the Christian life” than “unintentionally about Jesus.” Nitpicky? Perhaps. I see what you’re doing here but doesn’t make podium for me', '2026-07-28T03:40:56Z'),
  (5676, 810, 11, 1, 'I see the vision. Part of me feels like it’s so short and simple that it’s not actually that impressive. But what lyrics there are are pretty on target ', '2026-07-28T03:40:56Z'),
  (5677, 811, 11, 0, 'I wanted to be super into this. The lyrics are just so odd that it’s hard to see what the Jesus read of them would be bc it’s hard to know what they’re saying in the first place? Idk, it just didn’t fully click for me', '2026-07-28T03:40:56Z'),
  (5678, 812, 11, -1, 'This might be me misunderstanding the song, but I feel like the religious allusions are intentional. So while they’re being used to talk about someone who’s not Jesus, I think this isn’t quite the right fit for this round bc the way in which the lyrics can be taken religiously was both foreseen and intended', '2026-07-28T03:40:56Z'),
  (5679, 813, 11, 1, 'There are some lines that don’t quite work which is fine—but the hook works, pretty well imo', '2026-07-28T03:40:56Z'),
  (5680, 814, 11, 1, 'Maybe my inner theatre kid is just unable to resist but I like this take. Even if the lyrics aren’t explicitly Jesus esque, this really is how Jesus looks at you', '2026-07-28T03:40:56Z'),
  (5681, 815, 11, 0, 'I see the read here, it just didn’t strike me as much as others ', '2026-07-28T03:40:56Z'),
  (5682, 816, 11, 1, 'This was on my shortlist. The  “this body is yours” line is so perfect. I feared people wouldn’t get it/wouldn’t like that it was the riptide guy so I chickened out. But I commend the person who was braver than I', '2026-07-28T03:40:56Z'),
  (5683, 817, 11, 0, 'Technically not a repeat but this one feels less impressive bc we had another similar song by her in the St Therese round. I feel like I’d have to be really blown away by the submission for it to make my podium given that context', '2026-07-28T03:40:56Z'),
