  (5972, 861, 15, 0, 'The skaters were the gamers of their day, but never developed class consciousness. As such they faced discrimination without a coherent political movement to combat it. In this essay I will examine how the works of Lavigne display this class tensions while failing to address the inherent contradictions in the system that led to such heartless discrimination.', '2026-08-27T18:13:57Z'),
  (5973, 862, 15, 1, 'I strongly dislike Irish nationalism, but this is a baller song.', '2026-08-27T18:13:57Z'),
  (5974, 864, 15, 0, 'Earthy lad, that Afroman ', '2026-08-27T18:13:57Z'),
  (5975, 866, 15, -1, 'Down voting because they took a masterpiece and made it meh
 You don''t do that to my habibi Richard Thompson ', '2026-08-27T18:13:57Z'),
  (5976, 867, 15, 1, 'The song of my people ', '2026-08-27T18:13:57Z'),
  (5977, 870, 15, 0, 'Kill it with fire ', '2026-08-27T18:13:57Z'),
  (5978, 871, 15, 2, 'Thanks Joe', '2026-08-27T18:13:57Z'),
  (5979, 861, 4, 0, 'Absolute classic, and would never have actually thought of it as a story, but mostly since I''ve been hearing it endlessly since I was a child. ', '2026-08-27T20:41:20Z'),
  (5980, 862, 4, 0, 'Didn''t really strike me tbh. I think the style just doesn''t really stand out to me. ', '2026-08-27T20:41:20Z'),
  (5981, 863, 4, 1, 'Not gonna lie this is a gimmicky pick and it totally got me. Used to watch this with my family in the mid 2000s and you caught me at the perfect moment to capitalize on that nostalgia. ', '2026-08-27T20:41:20Z'),
  (5982, 864, 4, 0, 'Absolutely insane move to submit this. Bonkers, raving mad. Can''t downvote simply because of that audacity, even though it deserves it. 

I haven''t heard this all the way through since high school when it was played in a van full of high school guys and I intend to never hear it fully again. The chorus is so insanely good though and I like to listen to that part from time to time.', '2026-08-27T20:41:20Z'),
  (5983, 865, 4, 0, 'I know this is Irish, but side note - Jake Xerxes Fussell is discovering/documenting forgotten American folk music in a way no one has done since the 70s, American gem', '2026-08-27T20:41:20Z'),
  (5984, 866, 4, 0, 'Don''t like these characters. ', '2026-08-27T20:41:20Z'),
  (5985, 867, 4, 0, 'I hate Eagles man', '2026-08-27T20:41:20Z'),
  (5986, 868, 4, 2, 'Thank you Peter Seeley. What a gem. How did this man create so many bangers in his short life? ', '2026-08-27T20:41:20Z'),
  (5987, 869, 4, 1, 'I smile warmly at the idea of Joseph getting to this and then realizing with dawning horror that it''s actually an 80s Bob Dylan song. ', '2026-08-27T20:41:20Z'),
  (5988, 870, 4, 0, 'I liked this a lot but it''s not narrative! ', '2026-08-27T20:41:20Z'),
  (5989, 871, 4, -1, 'I didn''t find this very narratively compelling...not really a story song. And I also thought it was just an alright song. ', '2026-08-27T20:41:20Z'),
  (5990, 861, 11, 0, 'I wanted to go with this one because it has multiple levels of storytelling—the fictional character who’s supposedly singing the song is herself writing a song to tell a story, down to the opening line acknowledging the cliche framing', '2026-08-28T04:08:50Z'),
  (5991, 862, 11, -1, 'I guess this technically tells a story in the sense that it talks about an event that happened but it just doesn’t feel like a *story.* idk quite how to articulate it. Not really a unified narrative with beginning, middle, end', '2026-08-28T04:08:50Z'),
  (5992, 863, 11, 1, 'Okay this is clever and fun', '2026-08-28T04:08:50Z'),
  (5993, 864, 11, 1, 'I wish I were brave enough to submit this absolute masterpiece ', '2026-08-28T04:08:50Z'),
  (5994, 865, 11, 0, 'No shade to St Brendan but I find this one kinda corny', '2026-08-28T04:08:50Z'),
  (5995, 866, 11, 0, 'Well this is sad ', '2026-08-28T04:08:50Z'),
  (5996, 867, 11, 1, 'Classic story song. I didn’t initially want to vote for it bc it’s an obvious pick but in terms of telling a good story it does make the top 4 for me', '2026-08-28T04:08:50Z'),
  (5997, 868, 11, 0, 'I love this song. But I’m gonna be really pedantic here and say that this feels more like a vignette than a story properly speaking ', '2026-08-28T04:08:50Z'),
  (5998, 869, 11, 0, 'It’s fine. Didn’t knock my socks off. Sorry Bob', '2026-08-28T04:08:50Z'),
  (5999, 870, 11, 1, 'One reason this is an interesting pick is that it gets a bit “meta” with the story bit—the song is not only telling a story in the sense of talking about a sequence of events but also self consciously framing itself as a story', '2026-08-28T04:08:50Z'),
  (6000, 871, 11, 0, 'Musically super cool song but to be honest the story is just okay', '2026-08-28T04:08:50Z');
